(comment CalendarsMt "The microtheory that describes all calendar systems known in the world.")
(comment DistrictOfColumbia "The Federal district surrounding the capital city (#$CapitalCityOfRegion) of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, seat of its Federal government, which was formed from land donated to the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica by the states of Maryland and Virginia.  The land donated by Virginia was returned in 1847, so that the District comprises only land northeast of the southwest bank of the #$PotomacRiver at the time of the creation of the District, and the river itself. Currently, the #$CityOfWashingtonDC and the #$DistrictOfColumbia are coextensive.")
(comment KnowledgeSourceManagementMt "This microtheory contains vocabulary necessary to represent external knowledge sources inside Cyc for use with the Knowledge Source Tool.")
(comment Here "#$Here is a special region of space denote the `current' location. The exact interpretation will vary from one context to another.  In dialogue contexts it often refers to the location in which the dialogue is happening.  By contrast, in an #$ImageMicrotheory, #$Here probably refers to the location being depicted in the image.")
(comment GolanHeights "A strategically located territory between Israel and Syria.  The

territory was lost by Syria to Israel during the 1967 Arab-Israeli war

and is currently under Israeli control.")
(comment SouthernIraqiNoFlyZone "An AirspaceRegion above southern Iraq, defined by the 32cnd parallel

and the southern Iraqi border.

Iraqi flights through this region are under extremely tight

restrictions.  See also NorthernIraqiNoFlyZone.")
(comment NorthernIraqiNoFlyZone "An AirspaceRegion above northern Iraq, defined by the 36th parallel

and the northern Iraqi border.

Iraqi flights through this region are under extremely tight

restrictions.  See also SouthernIraqiNoFlyZone.")
(comment MajorLeagueSoccer "A professional #$SportsLeague which was begun

in the U.S. in 1996. As of 1998, there are 12 teams affiliated with MLS.")
(comment ARABSAT "#$ARABSAT (Arab Satellite Communications Organization) is an organization funded and managed by Arab states for the purpose of developing state-of-the-art telecommunications services for its member countries.")
(comment InternationalAtomicEnergyAgency "The agency of the #$UnitedNationsOrganization that is concerned with the cooperative scientific and technical development of atomic power and with verifying that nuclear resources are used for peaceful ends.")
(comment OAPEC "The aim of the Organization of Arab Petroleum Exporting Countries, established in January 1968, is to promote cooperation in the petroleum industry.")
(comment MassMediaMt "This #$Microtheory contains general assertions about mass media, focusing especially on #$MediaOrganizations, their activities, and the #$MediaProducts they distribute.")
