(comment NuclearNonProliferationTreaty "An instance of #$InternationalAgreement. It became effective in 1970 and was
intended to limit the number of nations with nuclear weapons to five: the U.S.
Soviet Union, Britain, France, and China. Signatories agree not to acquire
nuclear weapons and to accept the safeguards of the #$InternationalAtomicEnergyAgency
over their nuclear materials. (Preceding information derived from http://www.tradecompass.com/library/books/terms/NuclearNon-ProliferationTreaty.html.) ")
