(comment JointDefenseAndEconomicCooperationTreaty-ArabLeague "A #$Treaty which provides for the establishment of the #$JointDefenseCouncil-ArabLeague.")
(comment Rasch "Robert Rasch, a source of information and interpretation for the battlespace project.")
(comment PalestinianNationalAuthority "Autonomous government of portions of the PalestinianWestBank-and-Gaza. Governing lands formerly occupied by Israel, it has the goal of becoming an independent Palestinian State whose capital is Jerusalem.")
(comment EarthObservationalAstronomyMt "#$EarthObservationalAstronomyMt represents astronomy from the standpoint of an observer viewing the universe from the planet earth.  In this microtheory, the familiar #$Constellations and #$Asterisms as seen from the #$PlanetEarth have meaning and locations on the celestial sphere.")
(comment BigDipper-Asterism "The Big Dipper, an asterism with seven bright stars in #$UrsaMajor-Constellation.")
(comment OrionsBelt "The belt of Orion, an asterism with three bright stars in a line in #$Orion-Constellation.")
(comment Rigby "Brad Rigby, one of the primary sources of information and interpretation for the battlespace project.")
(comment LittleDipper-Asterism "The Little Dipper, an asterism with seven moderately bright stars in #$UrsaMinor-Constellation.")
(comment Pleiades "The #$Pleiades star cluster in the constellation #$Taurus-Constellation.")
(comment Buddha "Also known as #$SiddharthaGautama. Born: c.563, Died: c.483 B.C. in         Nepal. A soothsayer is said to have predicted at Siddhartha's birth that he         would become a world ruler or a world teacher. His father, King Suddhodana,         of the warrior caste, raised him in great luxury, but at the age of 29         Siddhartha renounced the world to become a wandering ascetic and search         for a solution to the problems of death and human suffering. After six years         of spiritual discipline, he achieved supreme enlightenment at the age of 35         while meditating under a pipal tree at Bodh Gaya. He spent the rest of his life         teaching his doctrines and establishing a community of monks, the #$Sangha,         to continue his work.")
(comment CommonGatewayInterface "An internet standard specifying how to pass arguments from a form on a website, etc., to an external program or script (often written in Perl and residing in a 'cgi-bin' directory) running on the web server. It also defines some environmental variables and allows the browser to be sent a customized webpage or be redirected to a url.")
(comment Melchior "One of the three wise men (or magi) that visited #$JesusOfNazareth at the nativity.")
(comment Kaspar "One of the three wise men (or magi) that visited #$JesusOfNazareth at the nativity.")
(comment Balthazzar "One of the three wise men (or magi) that visited #$JesusOfNazareth at the nativity.")
(comment ChristianTrinityMt "Christian beliefs as they pertain to the  mystery of the holy Trinity (i.e., that #$GodTheFather, #$JesusChrist (as #$GodTheSon) and #$GodTheHolyGhost are simultaneously three beings and one-being.")
(comment ChristianTrinity "The holy trinity in Christian theology. This is a very vexing concept, and any representation is likely to incur the wrath of some group of zealots and be considered heretical.  In this representation I assume  a heretical partonomic structure from the outset, and establish the trinity as a group of  three divine beings, namely: #$GodTheFather, #$GodTheSon, and #$GodTheHolyGhost. Note that much theological thought on the subject claims that the trinity is not a part-whole structure -- each member is simultaneously a member of, and identical to,  the trinity as a whole. I'm not convinced that Cyc (currently) needs a more complex definition than the one offered here for common-sense reasoning in a general (i.e., non-expert) fashion.")
(comment JesusChrist "The divine being one of whose physical incarnations is held to be #$JesusOfNazareth.")
(disjointWith PlantBLO (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Animal (GroupFn Animal))))
(disjointWith VegetableMatter (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Animal (GroupFn Animal))))
(comment ChristianityNaiveMt "Beliefs (typically) held by members of the  Christian faith (i.e., #$ChristianPerson) which conflict with other common-sense beliefs of these members. Loosely speaking, naive Christian views can be seen as metaphorical in the context of everyday reality, but literal in the context of Christian faith.")
(comment ResurrectionOfJesus "The event in which, instances of #$ChristianPerson believe, #$JesusOfNazareth (in his embodiment of #$JesusChrist) raised himself from the dead. This putative event took place three days after the #$CrucifixionOfJesus.")
(comment Interest "A specialization of #$Situation (q.v.).  Instances of #$Interest are temporal situations that an agent may (potentially) have an interest in maintaining or preserving or improving.  Specializations include #$EconomicInterest.")
(comment AffectMt "This microtheory is for information about affect, generally construed.  Thus it includes axioms about pure emotions (such as happy,  sad, angry) and more general affective terms (such as `abandoned').  It also contains axioms about causes, effects and communication of affect.  It assumes the existence of agents that have affective states.")
(comment ThePeanutsCartoonMt "#$ThePeanutsCartoonMt is a context in which to describe certain facts about the characters in Charles Schulz's cartoon series known as ``The Peanuts''.")
(comment Economics "The study of how human beings allocate scarce resources to produce various commodities and how those commodities are distributed for consumption among the people in society")
(comment Algebra "The branch of mathematics that deals with general statements of relations, utilizing letters and other symbols to represent specific sets of numbers, values, vectors, etc., in the description of such relations.")
(comment Firewire-TheProtocol "FireWire is a cross-platform implementation of the high-speed serial data bus -- defined by IEEE Standard 1394-1995 -- that can move large amounts of data between computers and peripheral devices.  It features simplified cabling, hot swapping, and transfer speeds of up to 400 megabits per second. FireWire speeds up the movement of multimedia data and large files and enables the connection of digital consumer products -- including digital camcorders, digital video tapes, DVD players, set-top boxes, and music systems -- directly to a personal computer.")
(comment Heraldry "The #$FieldOfStudy concerned with #$HeraldicDevices.")
(comment RomeoAndJuliet-ThePlay "#$RomeoAndJuliet-ThePlay is the play [#$Play-CW] written by #$WilliamShakespeare and entitled 'Romeo and Juliet'. This is the #$ConceptualWork, not the #$EntertainmentPerformances or the #$PlayScript.")
(comment Hair-TheMusical "The musical play [#$Play-Musical-CW] entitled 'Hair'.")
(comment TeletubbiesMt "The microtheory containing information about the children's show #$Teletubbies-TheTVShow.  Information about this show comes from http://www.pbs.org/teletubbies/.")
(comment GreenBeliefs "A #$BeliefSystem known especially for its emphasis on environmental values.  In Europe the ''Four Pillars'' of the Green Movement are ecology, grassroots democracy, social responsibility, and nonviolence.  In North America, the ''Ten Key Values of the Greens'' are social justice, community-based economics, nonviolence, decentralization, sustainability, feminism, personal and global responsibility, respect for diversity, grassroots democracy, and ecological wisdom.")
(comment Environmentalism "A #$BeliefSystem according to which preservation of the natural environment ought to be a top priority in policy and action.")
(comment Dipsy "One of the four #$Teletubbies.  #$Dipsy is the second biggest.")
(comment Sociology "The scientific study of human social behavior. As the study of humans in their collective aspect, sociology is concerned with all group activities-economic, social, political, and religious. Sociologists study such areas as bureaucracy, community, deviant behavior, family, public opinion, social change, social mobility, social stratification, and such specific problems as crime, divorce, child abuse, and substance addiction. Sociology tries to determine the laws governing human behavior in social contexts.")
(comment MarvelSuperheroesMt "The #$PopCultureMythologyMt subgenre dedicated to the characters of Marvel comics, such as Spiderman and the incredible Hulk. Marvel was founded by Stan 'the man' Lee in 1961, with the first appearance ofSpiderman in Amazing Fantasy 15.")
(comment DCSuperheroesMt "The #$PopCultureMythologyMt subgenre dedicated to the characters of DC comics, such as #$Superman and #$Batman. The name DC derives from 'Detective Comics', the original publication in which Bob Kane's #$Batman first appeared in 1939.")
(comment Hedonism "The doctrine that holds that pleasure is the greatest good.")
(comment PopCultureMythologyMt "The collected assertions that are true only within a popular/non-classical/non-traditional mythological context. Popular culture mythology includes fictitious stories from comic books, movies, urban legends etc. Not all pop-culture creations belong here, only those that have attained a 'mythic status', such as #$Superman and #$Batman. #$Superheroes of this variety belong to a pantheon of superhuman mythic characters that rivals (indeed, often steals from) the range and scale of classical Greek and Norse mythology. Thus, this Microtheory pertains to entities and things that have transcended their original medium (e.g., book or movie) and have become identiable with a certain set of mythic characteristics, traits and beliefs.")
(comment Krypton-ThePlanet "The home planet of #$Superman, which was engulfed by its own sun shortly after #$Superman fled to #$PlanetEarth.")
(comment FriedrichNietzsche "The German rhetorical stylist, philosopher of ethics and essayist who is famous for his development of the notion of #$Nietzschean-Superman, or UberMensch, a person who sets his/her own moral standards and is not dependent on the approval or approbation of his social group.  Despite his remarkable misanthropy and misogyny, Nietzsche never directed his bile against any single ethnic grouping in fact, it was a distaste for racism in general that caused him to end his friendship with the German composer #$RichardWagner. Nonetheless, his moral standpoint was open to misinterpretation, and his philosophies on the superman mentality were later adopted and perverted by the #$GermanNaziParty.")
(comment LiteraryPeopleDataMt "#$LiteraryPeopleDataMt contains data about people known for their literary works.")
(comment EricJones "Alphatech evaluator for the phase I and phase II HPKB Battlespace project and subject matter expert.")
(comment GamezonegamesKSMt "This microtheory contains information slurped from the Gamezone web page, at www.gamezone.com.")
(comment MentalHealth-FieldOfStudy "A very broad field of study which concerns itself with improving the psychological health of humans broadly construed.  Such a broad construal should be interpreted to include social and occupational functioning as it relates to mental health as well.  Thus it includes #$Psychiatry, #$CounselingPsychology, and #$SocialWork as #$subFields.  It is not so broad so as to include #$Psychology-Behavioral.  Although many of the findings of #$Psychology-Behavioral are applicable to areas of concern within #$MentalHealth-FieldOfStudy, the chief aim of #$Psychology-Behavioral is to empirically uncover the 'laws of behavior'.")
(comment PurposeSpecificationAndSuccessCriterionMt "This #$Microtheory contains specialized vocabulary for stating certain kinds of success criteria and purposes for actions.")
(comment FuzzyLogic "A #$FieldOfStudy which is a subfield [#$subFields] of #$Logic in which numbers on a scale from 0 to 1 [#$Real0-1] are used instead of the values \"true\" and \"false\", to represent the truth value statements that do not have a simple yes or no answer. #$FuzzyLogic was developed by Lofti Zadeh of the #$UniversityOfCalifornia-Berkeley.")
(comment DefaultTrue "An instance of #$CycHLTruthValue.  #$DefaultTrue is the attribute of being assumed true unless otherwise known to be false.")
(comment DefaultFalse "An instance of #$CycHLTruthValue.  #$DefaultFalse is the attribute of being assumed false unless otherwise known to be true.")
(comment NasdaqKSMt "This microtheory contains information slurped from the Nasdaq web page, at www.nasdaq.com.")
(comment ComputerSecurityMt "This microtheory is a spec of the ComputerRunningMt.  It contains information  about various kinds of electronic attacks and their effects as well as methods  and programs employed.")
(comment MassMediaDataMt "A microtheory for general (almanac-like) information about specific mass media organizations such as musical groups and TV stations, and specific mass media products such as CDs or TV shows. The relationship between #$MassMediaDataMt and #$MassMediaMt is analogous to the relationship between #$OrganizationDataMt and #$OrganizationMt.")
(comment Ist-HoldsInAssumptionsMt "This microtheory holds a set of assumptions which are intended to enable Cyc to infer temporally qualified assertions involving #$holdsIn from information about what #$ist in a given microtheory, and data about the #$mtTime of the microtheory.  These assumptions are intended to serve as heuristics, and may not be applicable in every context.")
(comment DeepThroat-ThePerson "#$DeepThroat-ThePerson provided information to Bernstein about criminal activities in the #$RichardNixon White House.")
(comment Psychology "The #$FieldOfStudy of psychology.")
(disjointWith Size-Generic-L Size-Generic-Plus)
(comment CityOfNaplesFlorida "The city of Naples located in #$Florida-State")
(comment CityOfPalmSpringsCA "The city of PalmSprings located in #$California-State")
(comment Aerobiology "#$Aerobiology is the subfield of #$Biology and  #$AerosolScience that focuses on suspended particles -- particularly volatile ones -- that are living, contain living organisms, or  were released from living organisms.")
(comment AerosolPhysics "#$AerosolPhysics is a subfield of #$Physics and #$AerosolScience that focuses on the study of the suspension of solid and liquid particles in gas.  It involves the  study of the diffusion of particles, transport phenomena, and relevant aspects of statistical mechanics.")
(comment AerosolScience "#$AerosolScience is the study of the suspension  of solid and liquid particles in gas.")
(comment Scatology "The biologically oriented study of excrement.")
(comment GreekMythologyMt "Within this microtheory, all the mythological creatures of ancient Greece are real animals, and all the facts of Greek mythology are true.")
(comment KateCapshaw "Actress, famous for Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom.")
(comment Veganism "The class of #$BeliefSystems that hold that eating meat and animal products is to be avoided because it is deemed either unhealthy, immoral, unpleasant, etc.")
(comment ComputerNetworkMt "A microtheory containing knowledge pertaining to computer networks, including information about network types and network protocols.  Information about specific computer networks should be in a more specialized microtheory.")
(comment SecurityMt "Contains information relating to security concepts and concerns.  Rules and constants pertaining to establishing or violating security should be found in this microtheory.")
(comment EverythingPSC "A problem solving context in which all assertions in the entire KB are visible.  This context is only appropriate for use in queries which do not care about the consequences of possible contradictions due to conflicting information from mutually inconsistent microtheories.  See also #$InferencePSC.")
(comment Arts "The #$LiberalArtsFieldOfStudy of arts.  #$ArtObject is used to indicate objects d'art.")
(comment Acoustics "#$Acoustics is the scientific study of sound.")
(comment MagicTheGathering-TradingCardGame "#$MagicTheGathering-TradingCardGame is a subset of #$TradingCardGame.  It is produced by #$WizardsOfTheCoast-CommercialOrganization. The cards are collectible and the game is strategic.  The instance of #$ComputerGameProgram, #$MagicTheGathering-ComputerGame, is based on #$MagicTheGathering-TradingCardGame.")
(comment Pokemon-TradingCardGame "#$Pokemon-TradingCardGame is a trading card game produced by #$WizardsOfTheCoast-CommercialOrganization. The cards are collectible and the game is strategic.")
(comment AI-Planning "The subfield of #$ArtificialIntelligence concerned with the representation of plans, the construction of plans based on operators, and the recognition of the plans held by another agent.")
(comment ComputerScienceSystems "The subfield of ComputerScience that deals with the construction of actual computer systems level software, such as operating systems, compilers, langauge design, etc.")
(comment ComputerScienceTheory "The study of the theoretical foundations of computation")
(comment Linguistics-Computational "The field of Computational Linguistics: the study of #$NaturalLanguages using
 computational models. Subfield of both #$ArtificialIntelligence and #$CognitiveScience by some lights")
(comment PhilosophyOfLanguage "The subfield of Philosophy that is concerned with the philosophical character of natural language.")
(comment CentristPoliticalIdeology "Agents with this ideology support traditional government, whatever that means for their situation; they often oppose laws that change current structures or governing philosophies if the current government is not repressive.  They support relaxation of repression, but oppose revolutionary change or action in the streets.")
(comment Racism "The doctrine that holds that people of one\" race\" are less able, intelligent, skillful, caring, moral, etc. than those of the other and/or that they are more suited to different roles in society.")
(comment Sexism "The doctrine that holds that people of one sex are less able, intelligent, skillful, caring, etc. than those of the other and/or that they are more suited to different roles in society.")
(comment Progressivism "A #$BeliefSystem that emphasises peace and justice, while supporting environmental and feminist causes and opposing bias against people for racial, religious, sexual orientation, immigration status, or other such reasons.")
(comment AntiSemitism "The doctrine that holds that #$JewishPersons are less intelligent, caring, moral, etc. than othes, that they are more suited to different roles in society, and/or should be eliminated from the society.")
(comment ProLifeIdeology "An instance of #$PoliticalBeliefSystem.  One who has #$ProLifeIdeology as a #$BeliefSystem holds that intentional abortions (see #$Abortion-Intentional) ought to be an #$IllegalAction.")
(comment DemocraticRepublicanIdeology "Agents with #$DemocraticRepublicanIdeology favor governmental decisions being decided by the populace or their elected representatives.")
(comment Homophobia "The doctrine that holds that HomosexualPersons are immoral and should not be tolerated.")
(comment Xenophobia "The doctrine that holds that foreigners or  immigrants are less able, intelligent, skillful, caring, etc. than those of the other and/or that they are more suited to different roles in society.")
(comment VulnerabilityMt "This microtheory contains information about vulnerability. Only very general definitional information about the nature of vulnerability itself should be asserted in this context.  More specific information, such as what it is that makes frogs vulnerable to the hot sun, should be asserted in more specific microtheories.  See, for example, the specialized vulnerabilty microtheory, #$ComputerVulnerabilityMt.")
(comment Cryobiology "The field of study concerning the effects of low tempratures on living organisms.")
(comment ReasoningWithExpectationMt "This Microtheory contains definitions of two notions in modal reasoning, #$expected-ToBe and #$amenable-ToBe.")
(comment Abolitionism "#$Abolitionism is a political theory which advocates the abolition of slavery [see #$Slave].")
(disjointWith BikiniBottom-PantyLike GString)
(comment Aviation "The study of the design, development, production, operation, and use of aircraft, esp. heavier than air aircraft.")
(comment LogicalTruthMt "This is a microtheory which contains only the assertions required to represent the logical system used in the Cyc knowledge base.  In other words, these are the assertions in CycL which must be present in order to use CycL to represent logical truths.")
(comment LogicalTruthImplementationMt "This is a microtheory which contains only the assertions required for the Cyc theorem prover and its underlying HL representation of the EL to function properly.  In other words, these are the assertions in CycL which are required by Cyc in order to perform any logical inferences using CycL formulas.")
(comment CommunitiesForming-CoABS "#$CommunitiesForming-CoABS is a series of events which take place in forming any instance of #$Community-CoABS. Necessary #$subEvents include at least one  #$Agent-CoABS responding to a #$Broadcast-CoABS.")
(comment VirtualReality-TechField "The field of study whose focus is the simulation of sensory experience.")
(comment EBOnline "The information in the online version of Encyclopedia Britannica which can be found at http://search.eb.com/")
(comment Systematics-Taxonomy "Systematics, aka taxonomy, is the study of the interrelationships between different taxonomic groups of living things.  Systematists use observable characteristics of living things to attempt to reconstruct the events of evolution.  In the last few decades, advances in molecular genetics have made it increasinly possible to determine which plant and animal types are most closely related.")
(comment FictionalWorksMt "This microtheory contains true facts about all fictional Mts, e.g. #$Dracula-TheNovel, #$TheSimpsonsMt.  This Mt includes information about the type of fictional work, the characters (see #$characterInCW), and other information.  #$authorOfLiteraryWork-CW assertions should be made in #$LiteraryPeopleDataMt.  Information presented in a fictional work should be asserted in the PIT associated with that work (see #$ContextOfPCWFn) or in #$FactsInFictionalWorksMt.")
(comment SetTheory "The study of mathematical sets or classes, collections of entities.  Since most of the entities of modern mathematics may be regarded as particular sets or classes of objects, set theory is often regarded as the study of the foundations of mathematics.")
(comment Addressee "an indexical that refers successfully only in discourse contexts")
(comment TheSimpsonsMt "The microtheory containing information about the Fox Network animated TV show 'the Simpsons'.")
(comment ContinentalBasketballAssociation "The official developmental league of the NBA.")
(comment CommunicationsSupportMt "An instance of #$TheoryMicrotheory.  This microtheory concerns the concepts of communications and especially concepts pertaining to providing support for communications, e.g. supplying and maintaining the infrastructure (satellites, telephones) necessary for certain kinds of communications to take place.")
(comment EvolutionaryBiology "#$EvolutionaryBiology is the study of the development of species over time. Its main tenets may be called Darwinian or Neo-Darwinian.")
(disjointWith Monotonic-JustificationStrength Default-JustificationStrength)
(disjointWith Unknown-JustificationStrength Default-JustificationStrength)
(comment Unknown-JustificationTruth "#$Unknown-JustificationTruth is the attribute of being currently neither provably true nor provably false.")
(comment AndromedaGalaxy "The closest major #$Galaxy to the #$MilkyWay-Galaxy.")
(comment Virology "This is the study of viruses. It is closely related to #$Microbiology, #$MolecularBiology, and #$Genetics.")
(comment Pathology "This is the study of disease. It is divided into surgical pathology, clinical pathology, and anatomical pathology. Surgical pathology attempts to determine from a sample of tissue taken from a patient in surgery what disease if any the patient has. This primarily involves microscopic inspection of the sample. Clinical pathology is essentially the application of #$MedicalChemistry. Anatomical pathology deals with the post-mortem determination of cause of death.")
(comment True-JustificationTruth "#$True-JustificationTruth is the attribute of being currently provably true.")
(comment False-JustificationTruth "#$False-JustificationTruth is the attribute of being currently provably false.")
(comment RecursionTheory "This is the subfield of #$MathematicalLogic which studies computable and effectively enumerable sets.")
(comment MathematicalLogic "This is logic in the modern sense. Its #$subFields include #$RecursionTheory, #$ModelTheory, #$SetTheory, #$ProofTheory, and #$MetaLogic.")
(comment ModelTheory "This is the subfield of #$MathematicalLogic which studies the interpretation of formal languages in set-theoretic structures.")
(comment ProofTheory "This is the subfield of #$MathematicalLogic which studies proofs independently of model-theoretic interpretation.")
(comment MetaLogic "This is the subfield of #$MathematicalLogic which treats logical systems as object languages and proves various results, such as the Completeness Theorem, about them. This field is often simply referred to as Logic.")
(comment InformationTheory "This is a mathematical theory of information according to which information is the amount of uncertainty a message  eliminates. This can be measured in terms of entropy.")
(comment NumberTheory "This is the study of the special (arithmetic) properties of the ring of integers and other similar rings.")
(comment OperationsResearch "Operations Research is the use of scientific methodology in the formulation, analysis, and solution  of problems of decision making.")
(comment Topology-FieldOfStudy "This is the study of the notion of continuity in the most abstract sense. Topological spaces are sets imbued with a class of subsets which, intuitively, tells one which elements (points) are near which other elements.")
(comment Optics "Optics is the subfield of physics which studies the properties of light, in particular, its interactions with lens, reflectors, and similar items.")
(comment ParticlePhysics "This is the subfield of #$Physics which studies subatomic particles. ")
(comment SpecialRelativity "#$SpecialRelativity is a physical theory in which there is no absolute notion of time but only time relative to inertial frames of reference.")
(comment GeneralRelativity "#$GeneralRelativity is a physical theory which represents gravity as the (local) geometry of spacetime, this latter being represented as a four-dimensional differentiable manifold. Geometry thus becomes a dynamic element.")
(comment AnimalActivitiesMt "A microtheory to collect all the general knowledge of the activities of #$Animals.")
(comment PathSystemsMt "A microtheory to collect all the relations and constants on #$PathSystems, see 'Introduction to Paths and Traversals' in the Cyc documentation library for details.")
(comment ComputationalAstrophysics "This is a field in which computer modelling and computational capabilities are applied to #$Astrophysics.")
(comment Ethnobotany "#$Ethnobotany is the study of how different cultures use plants for food, medicine, and materials.")
(comment Paleobotany "This is the study of ancient, especially extinct, plants. More directly, the study of the fossils of such.")
(comment Palynology "This is the study of pollen and spores. It is particularly relevant to #$Paleobotany.")
(comment LifeExtension-FieldOfStudy "This is a study which includes various scientific fields of study in their application to the problem of how to increase human life expectancy and quality of life in old age. It also includes fields of study which are probably not appropriately characterized as scientific. Largely due to the latter, this is not simply a subfield of medicine.")
(comment Cryogenics "This is the subfield of engineering which deals with very low temperatures, how to achieve them, and what their effects are.")
(comment AquaticEcotoxicology "This is the study of the toxins which may be found in aquatic environments.")
(comment Radioecology "This is the study of how radioactivity affects ecosystems.")
(comment MicrobialEcology "This is the study of the ecosystems in which micro-organisms live.")
(comment RestorationEcology "This is the application of methods and knowledge embodied in #$Ecology to the problem of how to restore various #$Ecosystems to the state they were in before detrimental intervention by humans.")
(comment Tradition "The vague notion of tradition, of being traditional.  Note that this is not necessarily the same as old-fashioned/anachronistic")
(comment IndustrialEcology "This is the study of how industrial activities can be carried out in an ecologically sound manner.")
(comment QuaternaryPaleoecology "This is the study of ecosystems throughout the recent period of geological time (the Quaternary period).")
(comment SpatialAnalysis "This is the study of how to apply computer data and imaging capabilities to cartography.")
(comment Transgenics "This is the study of mutations and how to produce  mutated strains of species.")
(comment Paleontology "This is the study of extinct types of #$Organism-Wholes, whether animal or plant, via the examination of fossils.")
(comment EvolutionaryPsychology "Evolutionary psychology is the science that seeks to explain through universal mechanisms of behavior why humans act the way they do. Evolutionary psychology seeks to reconstruct problems that our ancestors faced in their primitive environments, and the problem-solving behaviors they created to meet those particular challenges. From these reconstructed problem-solving adaptations, the science then attempts to establish the common roots of our ancestral behavior, and how those common behavioral roots are manifested today in the widely scattered cultures of the planet.")
(comment Memetics "Memetic Science is the name of a new field that deals with the quantitative analysis of cultural transfer. The units of cultural transfer are entities called \"memes\". In a nutshell, memes are to cultural and mental constructs as genes are to biological organisms. Examples of memes are ideas, tunes, fashions, and virtually any cultural and behavioral unit that gets copied with a certain degree of fidelity.")
(comment Histopathology "This is the study of how to diagnose disease from the examination, generally microscopic, of tissues. It is what is practiced by someone engaged in Surgical Pathology.")
(comment MolecularBiochemistry "Molecular Biochemistry emphasizes the correlation of function with the known structure of biological macromolecules and supramolecular structures such as multienzyme complexes, membranes, and viruses.")
(comment Anatomy-FieldOfStudy "This is the study of what parts organisms have. It generally applies only to fairly large multi-cellular animals with a variety of tissues and organs.")
(comment TheoryOfActionMt "A microtheory which holds a theory about actions either by human or artificial agents.  This would typically be a #$genlMt of other Mts in which agents may perform actions, e.g. #$HumanActivitiesMt. It is based on the existing notion that #$Action is a  spec of #$Event, but leaves open the possibility of there being other kinds of actions that isn't captured by #$Action.")
(comment MarineBiology "This is the study of marine life.")
(comment Micropaleontology "Micropaleontology is a division of paleontology devoted to fossils of particularly small size. They are important index fossils because they evolve rapidly and are geographically widespread. They are used in the petroleum industry for subsurface correlation.")
(comment QuaternaryGeology "This is the subfield of geology which studies the earth during the Quaternary period. The Quaternary is a subdivision of geological time  which covers the last two million years up to the present day. (The exact duration is a matter of debate with estimates of the onset of the Quaternary Period placed at between 1.8 million years and 2.6 million years by different authors) The Quaternary can be subdivided into two epochs; the Pleistocene (two million years to ten thousand years ago) and the Holocene (ten thousand years ago to the present day.")
(comment QuaternaryStudies "This is the study of the earth during its most recent geological period, the Quaternary period, which is roughly the last 2 million years.")
(comment Glaciology "This is the study of glaciers.")
(comment Dendrochronology "Dendrochronology is the  dating of past events (climatic changes) through study of tree ring growth. The technique was developed by A.E. Douglass from the University of      Arizona, who noted that the wide rings of      certain species of trees were produced      during wet years and, inversely, narrow      rings during dry seasons.")
(comment Geomorphology "Geomorphology is the study of landforms and the processes that shape them over time.")
(comment StructuralGeology "This is the study of the large-scale geological structures on the earth, particularly the tectonic plates.")
(comment IgneousPetrology "This is the study of igneous rocks.")
(comment MetamorphicPetrology "This is the study of metamorphic rocks.")
(comment OpticalMineralogy "This is the subfield of #$Mineralogy in which the microscopic properties of minerals in thin section are studied.")
(comment SedimentaryPetrology "This is the study of sedimentary rocks.")
(comment Cartography "This is the study of maps and map-making.")
(comment Geodesy "This is the study of the earth's surface as a whole, in  particular the determination of its shape and the relation of its shape to the  direction of gravity.")
(comment UniversityOfMassachusettsSystem "A system of universities, all located in Massachussets.  The #$UniversityOfMassachusettsSystem has dual headquarters in Boston and Hadley.")
(comment CondensedMatterPhysics "This is the study of the special properties of matter in a highly condensed state.")
(comment RelativityTheory "This is the subfield of physics which combines #$SpecialRelativity and #$GeneralRelativity. All modern physical theories pretty much take #$RelativityTheory for granted.")
(comment Econometrics "This is the application of statistical techniques to solving problems and modelling theories in economics.")
(comment Macroeconomics "Macroeconomic theory is the study of an economy's aggregate behavior. Specific topics include the effect of monetary and fiscal policy on output, employment, and price level in both the long and short run; business cycles; the role of different monetary arrangements; determination of the money stock, bank credit, and interest rates; the nature of the interaction between budget and monetary expansion; the relation between inflation, unemployment, and the role of expectations; and the interaction between asset markets and the output market.")
(comment PoliticalEconomics "A branch of the social sciences that takes as its principal subject of study the interrelationships between political and economic institutions and processes. That is, political economists are interested in analyzing and explaining the ways in which various sorts of government affect the allocation of scarce resources in society through their laws and policies as well as the ways in which the nature of the economic system and the behavior of people acting on their economic interests affects the form of government and the kinds of laws and policies that get made.")
(comment Tribology "Tribology is defined as the science and technology of interacting surfaces in relative motion, and embraces the study of friction, wear and lubrication.")
(comment NecessityMt "This #$Microtheory contains definitions of basic notions in modal reasoning in Cyc about necessity and possibility.  See #$necessary and #$possible.")
(comment Year2000MilitaryTechnologyMt "a #$SourceMicrotheory, created for #$ProjectBroadsword, that contains information from www.airforce-technology.com, www.army-technology.com,  and www.naval-technology.com.  These sites, published by Net Resources International Limited, offer unclassified, detailed information about military contractors and their products.")
(comment Astroarchaeology "This is a field which studies the role of astronomical thought in ancient cultures. It is similar to #$Archaeoastronomy but appears to be less scientific and its practioners more methodologically diverse.")
(comment TheoreticalBiology "This is the subfield of #$Biology which attempts to formalize various aspects of biological study by employing models, usually mathematical. ")
(comment Now-Generally "#$Now-Generally is an underspecified piece of time that refers to some sense of \"the current moment\".  #$Now-Generally differs from #$Now (q.v.) in two respects.  First, unlike #$Now, #$Now-Generally is not necessarily a #$TimePoint; its exact duration will vary from context to context.  Second, unlike #$Now, #$Now-Generally does not necessarily subsume the clock time of #$Cyc's cpu.  See #$RealTimeMt and its specializations in which   #$Now-Generally does subsume #$Now.  Depending on the microtheory, #$Now-Generally might refer to an instance, or to piece of time that is several seconds, years or milllennia in duration.  In a microtheory that is not a specialization of #$RealTimeMt, however, #$Now-Generally might refer to a piece of time that is #$temporallyDisjoint from #$Now.  For example, imagine a microtheory representing a particular live broadcast of the 1950's television program \"The Mickey Mouse Club\".  In this microtheory there might be mention of the singing of the lyrics \"Now it's time to say goodbye to all our family....\"  (These lyrics were sung at the end of every episode.)  The word \"now\", as sung in that episode, would be appropriately interpreted as `#$Now-Generally', but (unlike in a specialization of #$RealTimeMt) the piece of time it denotes would be some time interval in the 1950s.  In discourse interpretation contexts, conversational pragmatics and common sense inference should help determine the duration and temporal location of #$Now-Generally.")
(comment Geriatrics-Field "This is the field of study which is mastered by specialists in geriatric medicine. See #$GeriatricDoctor.")
(comment AcademicLifeMt "A microtheory for representing the general aspects of academic life of #$AcademicOrganizations. For example, this microtheory should be used for representing the practices, organization, and employment opportunities at these institutions. Since not all #$EducationalOrganizations are #$AcademicOrganizations, not all assertions about #$EducationalOrganizations should be made in this microtheory.")
(comment PeanutsCartoon-CW "Charles Schulz's cartoon series known as ``Peanuts''.")
(disjointWith MilitaryPerson (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn Person retiredFromField MilitaryPerson))
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOfficer (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn Person retiredFromField LawEnforcementOfficer))
(disjointWith Person (CollectionDifferenceFn Animal Person))
(disjointWith Artifact (CollectionDifferenceFn (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn Basin-Topographical covers-Paintlike Asphalt) Artifact))
(disjointWith Monotreme (CollectionDifferenceFn Mammal Monotreme))
(disjointWith Person (CollectionDifferenceFn Mammal Person))
(disjointWith GeneticallyEngineeredOrganism (CollectionDifferenceFn BiologicalLivingObject GeneticallyEngineeredOrganism))
(disjointWith Path-Customary (CollectionDifferenceFn Path-Spatial Path-Customary))
(disjointWith IsraeliPerson (CollectionDifferenceFn Tourist IsraeliPerson))
(disjointWith (CitizenFn SriLanka) (CollectionDifferenceFn Person (CitizenFn SriLanka)))
(disjointWith MilitaryVehicle (CollectionDifferenceFn Automobile MilitaryVehicle))
(disjointWith Prisoner-Legal (CollectionDifferenceFn Person Prisoner-Legal))
(comment GeneralCycKE "The #$GeneralCycKE knowledge entry mode is used for entering general knowledge into Cyc, e.g. things that are (and should be) in the #$BaseKB.  Select a more specific project unless you are entering truly general knowledge.")
(comment AmbientConditionsDataMt "Microtheory which specifies the ambient weather conditions at specific locales.  It is a specMt of #$AmbientConditionsMt and #$UnitedStatesGeographyDualistMt.")
(disjointWith Investing SpendingMoney)
(disjointWith SpendingMoney Gambling)
(disjointWith BorrowingSomething SpendingMoney)
(comment ProductPhysicalCharacteristicsMt "The microtheory that describes physical characteristics of formal products.  The identity of products comes from #$ProductGMt and the characteristics are defined in  #$ObjectPhysicalCharacteristicsMt.")
(comment HumanFoodGMt "This is the most general microtheory dealing with human food. ")
(comment HistoricalPeopleDataMt "This #$Microtheory is for information about people who are known historically, but were not alive recently.  A reasonable cut-off point would be 1950.  Use #$LiteraryPeopleDataMt instead, if the person is famous for literary works.")
(comment ComputerRunningDataMt "Contains computer knowledge about interactions of specific hardware or software that occur primarily when a computer is operating.")
(comment ReligiousPeopleDataMt "This #$Microtheory is for information about people who are known important in some religion.")
(comment ElectricalSystemsMt "A microtheory containing knowledge pertaining to electrical systems, including information about voltage, resistance, electical components, and circuit types.")
(comment NonfictionalWorksMt "This microtheory contains facts about all instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks, such as information about the type of work, what concepts are mentioned, the characters (if applicable), the publisher, publication date, etc.see #$characterInCW), and other information.  Assertions about the propositional content of the work does not belong in #$NonfictionalWorksMt.  By convention, #$authorOfLiteraryWork-CW assertions are be made in #$LiteraryPeopleDataMt.  The propositional content of a work should be asserted in the microtheory associated with that work (see #$ContextOfPCWFn).")
(comment BrandNameProductGMt "A microtheory which holds assertions about the features and compatibilities of brand name formal products.  Assertions about physical characteristics of brand name products belong in #$BrandNameProductPhysicalCharacteristicsMt  Assertions relating products to instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity belong in #$WorldProductsMt.")
(comment PharmaceuticalGMt "#$PharmaceuticalGMt is the most general microtheory dealing with medicines and drugs.  Unless they are extremely common common specific drugs and brand-name drugs (or assertions about them) belong in #$PharmaceuticalDetailsMt.")
(comment GiftAdvisorMt "This #$Microtheory represents the general rules about finding, selecting, and purchasing products intended to be given as a gift. General rules linking gift givers and gift recipients to suitable gift suggestions and general rules about #$GiftGiving essential to the inferencing by the Generalist component of the CycProductAdvisor should be placed here. GAFs and rules about #$Products and #$ProductTypes relevant to selecting a #$Product for purchase should be made in #$ShoppingGMt, even in cases where the #$Product is typically purchased as a gift item.")
(comment TheBuilder "This cyclist represents the context in which dumps of the world are performed.")
(comment USGovernmentOrganizationDataMt "#$USGovernmentOrganizationDataMt is the microtheory to use to describe US government organizations which have to be available in #$InternationalOrganizationDataMt.  For purely domestic organizations, use the more specific, #$USGovernmentDomesticOrganizationDataMt.")
(comment USGovernmentDomesticOrganizationDataMt "#$USGovernmentDomesticOrganizationDataMt is the microtheory to use to describe domestic US government organizations.  For organizations which have to be available in #$InternationalOrganizationDataMt, use the broader, #$USGovernmentOrganizationDataMt.")
(comment WorldNaturalGeographyMt "This context contains information about individual natural #$GeographicalRegions (mountains, bodies of water, continents, islands, etc.) around the world, except for those in the US, which are #$UnitedStatesNaturalGeographyMt.  Major US features will be made visible in the #$WorldNaturalGeographyMt, so that the #$RockyMountains are visible here but the #$DavisMountains are not.  Assertions regarding instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity or artificial #$TopographicalFeatures  (canals, artificial lakes, excavated harbors, ...) do not belong in #$WorldNaturalGeographyMt, but in #$WorldGeographyMt, #$WorldGeographyDualistMt (for instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity treated as places), or specializations of these microtheories.")
(comment TemplateParsingMt "The microtheory in which definitions necessary for template parsing are stored.  Note that individual templates will not be stored in this Mt.  They should be stored in a language-specific microtheory instead.")
(comment PassoverHoliday "An instance of #$AnnualHolidayType and a specialization of #$JewishHoliday. Each instance of #$PassoverHoliday is an eight-day event beginning at #$Sunset on the fourteenth day of an instance of #$Nissan-JewishMonth.  #$PassoverHoliday commemorates the exodus of #$JewishPersons from #$Egypt during the reign of Pharoah Ramses II.")
(comment UnitedStatesNaturalGeographyMt "This context contains information about individual mountains, lakes, and other natural features in the US.  Major US features will be made visible in the #$WorldNaturalGeographyMt, so that the Rocky Mountains are visible but the Davis Mountains are not.  Assertions concerning instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity belong in #$UnitedStatesGeographyMt (or if they treat them as #$GeographicalRegions) in #$UnitedStatesGeographyDualistMt or specializations thereof.")
(comment ProductAdvisorApplication "An application that uses the Cyc KB to conduct a dialog with a customer to help her decide what product she wants to buy from a large inventory.  Initially, this application will be focuses on helping someone select a gift for someone else, based on knowledge about the recipient, the gift, the situation, etc.")
(comment PharmaceuticalUseMt "An instance of #$TheoryMicrotheory.  The #$PharmaceuticalUseMt contains knowledge about the administration of drugs to animal (including human) subjects, as well as the effects those drugs have on those subjects.")
(comment nextToLikeObjects "A #$RelativeLocationalPredicate that relates tangible objects of the same (specified) type that are located next to or beside each other.  (#$nextToLikeObjects OBJ1 OBJ2 TYPE) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are both instances of TYPE, and OBJ1 is spatially next to OBJ2.  More precisely: (i) OBJ1 and OBJ2 are both instances of TYPE, (ii) OBJ1 and OBJ2 are #$near each other, (iii) no other member of TYPE is #$between OBJ1 and OBJ2, and (iv) no other member of TYPE is both nearer to OBJ1 and in the same general direction from OBJ1 as OBJ2 is, or vice versa.
<p>
One person directly in front of another person in a queue, two houses that are next door to each other, adjacent squares on a chessboard, and sequential steps on a raised ladder are all examples of pairs of objects related by #$nextToLikeObjects.  For a specialization of this predicate that is restricted to non-vertical arrangements (and thus does not hold of the ladder steps), see #$nextToLike-Horizontally.
<p>
Note that two things can be related by #$nextToLikeObjects even though there is an _unlike_ object (i.e. something not an instance of TYPE) between them.  For example, two houses might be #$nextToLikeObjects each other despite the fact that there is a fence, tree, or driveway between them.  Note also that when two objects stand in the relation #$nextToLikeObjects with respect to some collection, it follows that there is some #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects (q.v.) having at least those two objects as members.")
(comment AspectTense-InferenceMt "This microtheory contains assertions that are used to describe the temporal relations between instances of #$AspectTenseMicrotheory. Note that such rules are `higher-order', semantic-level rules, in many cases providing at least a rough translation between the tensed formulas asserted in instances of #$AspectTenseMicrotheory and the tenseless Davidsonian event descriptions used in Cyc. The constant #$mtPrecedes-Immediately is also defined here, as it expresses temporal contiguity between instances of #$AspectTenseMicrotheory. Note that since this is a spec of #$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt we can use notions such as #$reasoningWithTenseMtTime here as well.")
(comment ConceptualUnderspecificationMt "This #$Microtheory contains definitional information about Cyc's underspecified ontology, which will be used to aid the HPSG parsing effort.")
(comment HeathrowAirport-London "#$HeathrowAirport-London is the large international airport on the west side of the #$CityOfLondonEngland that serves London for most overseas airline flights.")
(comment HotelVienna "An imaginary hotel.")
(comment SchengenTreaty "A treaty originally signed in 1985, but not fully implemented until 1995. The seven countries that signed the #$SchengenTreaty - Belgium, the Netherlands, Luxembourg, France, Germany, Portugal and Spain -agreed to allow citizens of the signatory countries greater freedom of movement between those countries.")
(comment PlanningVocabularyMt "This mt has mixed definitions, rules, and test cases, which argues for removing ``Vocabulary'' from the name.")
(comment OrientExpressEuropeanTour "An imaginary tour of Europe.")
(comment EqualityReasoningMt "This microtheory is being used as a repository of vocabulary and rules to facilitate equality reasoning.")
(comment WorldCulturalGeographyDataMt "The #$Microtheory which relates human activities and societal elements to instances of #$GeographicalRegion (treating #$GeopoliticalEntity as a spec thereof).  Each assertion in #$WorldCulturalGeographyDataMt should reference both an instance of #$GeographicalRegion or #$GeopoliticalEntity and some societal element which is neither of these.  Definitional assertions for instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity and #$GeographicalRegion or interrelationships between such do not belong in this #$Microtheory.")
(comment UnitedStatesCulturalGeographyMt "The #$Microtheory which relates human activities and societal elements to instances of GeographicalRegion (treating GeopoliticalEntity as a spec thereof) in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica. Each assertion in #$UnitedStatesCulturalGeographyMt should reference both an instance of #$GeographicalRegion or #$GeopoliticalEntity and some societal element which is neither of these. Definitional assertions for instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity and #$GeographicalRegion or interrelationships between such do not belong in this Microtheory.")
(comment relationAllSpecsExists "(#$relationAllSpecsExists PRED COL1 COL2) means that for every SUBCOL1 which is a subcollection of COL1, there exists some INS2 which is an instance of COL2, such that (PRED SUBCOL1 INS2) holds.")
(comment relationExistsAllSpecs "(#$relationExistsAllSpecs PRED COL1 COL2) means that for every SUBCOL2 which is a subcollection of COL2, there is some INS1 which is an instance of COL1, such that (PRED INS1 SUBCOL2) holds.")
(comment ComputerVulnerabilityMt "#$ComputerVulnerabilityMt is the most general microtheory encompassing knowledge about the electronic vulnerabilities computers have as attributes.  The microtheory contains two broad areas of knowledge: (1) Definitions for the upper level -- i.e.  non-leaf -- nodes in the computer vulnerability hierarchy, (2) definitions of the upper level -- i.e. non-leaf -- nodes in the software fault hierarchy, and (3) definitional knowledge for predicates that utilize this vocabulary to represent vulnerability and fault knowledge.  Two classes of knowledge are explicitly excluded from this microtheory and should be placed in a more specific microtheory (or microtheories): instance level, or leaf-node vulnerability and fault attributes, and knowledge about the faults in specific computer programs.")
(comment NaturalGeographyMt "This #$Microtheory is for definitions, rules, and assertions about #$Collections of natural #$TopographicalFeatures and geographical predicates.  It includes general information about geography without making any assertions about the #$PlanetEarth or any #$Individual on it.  For the placement of other geographical assertions see #$Dualist-Physical-AndGenericGeographyMtNote.")
(comment PoliticalGeographyMt "This #$Microtheory is for is for definitions, rules, and assertions about #$Collections of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  It includes general information about political geography without making any assertions about the PlanetEarth or any Individual on it.  For the placement of other geographical assertions see #$Dualist-Physical-AndGenericGeographyMtNote.")
(disjointWith BarAreaInPrivateResidence (CollectionDifferenceFn Bar-Place BarAreaInPrivateResidence))
(comment WorldCompleteDualistGeographyMt "The collector #$Microtheory of the #$WorldGeographyDualistMicrotheorySpindle.")
(comment WorldGeographyDualistMicrotheorySpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle for geographic microtheories about nations in the world, each microtheory of which treats instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity as being instances of #$GeographicalRegion.  For microtheories which contain assertions relating instances of #$GeographicalRegion and either #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$Artifact use #$WorldGeographyMicrotheorySpindle.  For microtheories dealing solely with the natural world use the #$WorldNaturalGeographyMicrotheorySpindle.")
(comment WorldGeographyMicrotheorySpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle for geographic microtheories about nations in the world, each microtheory of which contains assertions relating instances of #$GeographicalRegion and either #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$Artifact.  For microtheories dealing solely with the natural world use the #$WorldNaturalGeographySpindle.  For microtheories treating instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity as being instances of #$GeographicalRegion use the #$WorldGeographyDualistMicrotheorySpindle.")
(comment WorldNaturalGeographyMicrotheorySpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle for geographic microtheories about nations in the world, each microtheory of which contains assertions dealing solely with the natural world within the specified region. For microtheories which contains assertions relating instances of #$GeographicalRegion and either #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$Artifact use #$WorldGeographyMicrotheorySpindle.  For microtheories treating instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity as being instances of #$GeographicalRegion use the #$WorldGeographyDualistMicrotheorySpindle.")
(comment GenBank-DBContent "A genetic sequence database. This is the collection of all publicly available DNA sequences maintained by the National Institues of Health (NIH). Three organizations contribute to maintaining GenBank: the DNA DataBank of Japan (DDBJ), the European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL), and GenBank at the National Center for Biotechnology Information.")
(comment ChemistryMt "This microtheory contains information about chemistry.")
(comment EBert "#$EBert is an application that lets Cyc access the IMDB database and draw its own inferences from the info there.")
(comment IntermediateVocabularyMt "The microtheory that contains definitions of  concepts used to form the sort of intermediate CycL vocabulary needed to make a generalizable NL parsing system possible.")
(comment BiochemistryMt "This microtheory contains information about biochemistry, i.e. related to chemical processes which occur in living organisms.")
(comment AilmentVocabularyMt "The #$VocabularyMicrotheory for #$AilmentMt.")
(comment PeloponnesianWarMt "This microtheory contains information about the #$PeloponnesianWar.")
(comment UnitedStatesModernMilitaryVehiclesDataMt "This microtheory is the context in which information is asserted about specific modern military vehicles owned by the armed forces of the United States.  More general information about types of vehicles should be asserted in the #$ModernMilitaryVehiclesMt.")
(comment SimpleAstronomyVocabularyMt "The #$VocabularyMicrotheory for #$SimpleAstronomyMt")
(comment UniverseVocabularyMt "The #$VocabularyMicrotheory for #$UniverseGeneralMt.")
(comment SimpleAstronomyDataVocabularyMt "The #$VocabularyMicrotheory which is the #$genlMt-Vocabulary of #$SimpleAstronomyDataMt.")
(comment MainstreamAmericanCultureMt "#$MainstreamAmericanCultureMt is the microtheory that contains assertions expressing the beliefs and describing the rituals of 'mainstream' America in the year 2000. This is a microtheory for anything that is definitional information about beliefs or customs of the 'mainstream' American culture.  For assertions about the organizations, institutions and professions of modern American life, please see the #$UnitedStatesSocialLifeMt.")
(comment DeonticReasoning-InferenceMt "This microtheory contains assertions about relations between
instances of #$DeonticReasoningMicrotheory.  The basic notions
involved in such assertions are #$mtDeonAccessible and #$mtDeonIdeal
etc.  Note that rules in this microtheory amount to semantic
interpretations of formulas in microtheories that are instances of
#$DeonticReasoningMicrotheory, and thus should not be present in those
microtheories.  Note also that although this microtheory is made a
spec mt of #$DeonticReasoning-LogicMt, it is done only because we need to
mention deontic to-be operators in certain rules in this microtheory.
In each spec mt of this microtheory, modal operators/predicates should
only occur inside of certain `meta language' predicates like #$ist,
#$mtConverts-PlainOp and #$mtConverts-OpPlain etc., and no instance of
#$ModalReasoningMicrotheory should be a specMt of this microtheory.")
(comment ReformulatorMode-Preferify "A #$ReformulatorMode in which #$CycLExpressions are
reformulated into their preferred form.  Which form is preferred
is determined by #$reformulationDirectionInMode meta-assertions
on reformulator rules.")
(comment ReformulatorMode-Tersify "A #$ReformulatorMode in which #$CycLExpressions are
reformulated into their most terse, concise form.  Which form is
considered to be more terse is determined by
#$reformulationDirectionInMode meta-assertions on reformulator
rules.")
(comment ReformulatorMode-Verbosify "A #$ReformulatorMode in which #$CycLExpressions are
reformulated into a more verbose, expanded form.  Which form is
considered to be more verbose is determined by
#$reformulationDirectionInMode meta-assertions on reformulator
rules.")
(comment ReformulatorMode-Simplify "A #$ReformulatorMode in which #$CycLExpressions are
reformulated into a simpler form.  Which form is considered to be simpler
is determined by #$reformulationDirectionInMode meta-assertions
on reformulator rules, in conjunction with the #$CycLSimplifier.
There is no inverse of this mode.")
(comment ReformulationBackwardDirection "A meta-property of a #$CycLReformulatorDirective, meaning
that there exist two arguments in the directive such that the
higher-numbered arg (e.g. arg2 for a binary predicate) is the 'from'
arg, the input to the reformulator, and that the lower-numbered arg
(e.g. arg1 for a binary predicate) is the 'to' arg, the output of the
reformulator.  Its semantics are more fully determined by context.
See #$reformulationDirectionInMode for how this
direction can be used.")
(comment ReformulationNeitherDirection "A meta-property of a #$CycLReformulatorDirective,
meaning that no arg is to be interpreted as either the 'from' or 'to' arg.
See #$reformulationDirectionInMode for how this
direction can be used.")
