(comment GuestCyclist "This constant is for use by guests (users who may not have full rights of access) who want to interact with Cyc.")
(comment SKSIMt "The microtheory containing non-definitional assertions concerning the SKSI vocabulary.")
(disjointWith IntelligenceAgent (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn Person retiredFromField IntelligenceAgent))
(comment MuffetTestMt "The microtheory describing the #$Dog, #$Muffet.  Tests using #$Muffet belong in #$MuffetTestMt or a specMt (such as #$CyclistsMt).")
(comment CSyntaxProgrammingLanguageMt "This micotheory contains vocabulary on the structure and syntax of programming languages like C, C++, and Java.")
(comment CoreCycLMt "This is a microtheory which contains only the assertions required to represent useful logical truths in CycL.  It extends the #$LogicalTruthMt with additional assertions which are so useful as to be considered `core' to the CycL language.")
(comment CoreCycLImplementationMt "This is a microtheory which contains only the `core' assertions required for the Cyc theorem prover and its underlying HL representation of the EL to conclude useful inferences.  It extends the #$LogicalTruthImplementationMt with assertions necessary for Cyc's implementation to make use of the terms defined in the #$CoreCycLMt.")
(comment UniversalVocabularyImplementationMt "This is the microtheory which contains the assertions about CycL terms which are necessary for Cyc's inference engine to reason about those terms.")
(comment intervalEntryFormatInArgs "An instance of #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate (q.v.) that is used only with argument-places that are constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of either #$ScalarInterval or #$TimeInterval or some specialization of either.  (#$intervalEntryFormatInArgs PRED N) means that, for any particular way of fixing the other arguments to PRED besides the Nth, for any two intervals such that if either one is taken as the Nth argument PRED holds of those arguments, those intervals must \"overlap\" (see #$quantityIntersects and #$temporallyIntersects).  That is, if the sequences <... ARGN ...> and <... ARGN-PRIME ...> differ at most in their Nth items and both (PRED ... ARGN ...) and (PRED ... ARGN-PRIME ...) hold, then (i) if (#$argIsa PRED N #$ScalarInterval) then (#$quantityIntersects ARGN ARGN-PRIME) holds and (ii) if (#$argIsa PRED N #$TimeInterval) then (#$temporallyIntersects ARGN ARGN-PRIME) holds.   
For example, #$intervalEntryFormatInArgs holds of #$bodyTemperature with respect to its second argument-place because, while a given creature (at a given moment in time) has a single exact (see #$ScalarPointValue) body temperature, we want the predicate #$bodyTemperature to be flexible enough to allow us to specify this temperature with varying degrees of precision (e.g. as \"98.6 degrees Fahrenheit\" or as \"between 98 and 99 degrees Fahrenheit\" or as \"less than 100 degrees Fahrenheit\").
For another example, #$intervalEntryFormatInArgs holds of #$foundingDate with respect to its second argument-place because, while a given city has a single exact (see #$startingPoint) time when it was founded, we want the predicate #$foundingDate to be flexible enough to allow us to specify this date with varying degrees of precision (e.g. as \"June 14, 1964,\" \"June 1964,\" or simply \"1964\").
Note that many interval-entry format argument-places that are constrained to time-intervals have #$Date as their asserted #$argIsa constraint.")
(comment USCensusRaceAndOriginType "The collection of all categories of US resident [(#$ResidentFn (#$TerritoryFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica))] distinguished by \"race\" or origin as listed on the US census form.  US residents who fill out the census for self-select which category they are an instance of.  This collection is context-dependent because in different decades, different lists of categories appear.  Prior to 1790 there were no instances of this collection (in a non-fictional context).")
(comment ObjectTypeByLightingCondition "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ObjectTypeByLightingCondition is a collection of objects in the same lighting condition.")
(comment PhysicalQualityOfTangibleOnly "A collection of collections each of which represents a quality or property that can sensibly be ascribed and restricted to paradigmatic cases of #$PartiallyTangible things, such  as physical bodies.")
(comment HumanChildTypeByShoeSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanChildTypeByShoeSize is a collection of people whose shoe size is the same.  For instance. ChildrensShoeSize3 is the collection of all people who wear shoe size 3.")
(comment Quantity-ScriptCriticality "instances are quantities of risks associated with performing instances of #$HumanActivity each exhibiting a particular risk to human life or value of property.")
(comment SituationTypeByUserRights "A collection of collections.  Every Instance of #$SituationTypeByUserRights is a collection of instances of #$Situation that are situations that consist in the holding of some particular user right.  For example, if I have #$FullUseRights to my car, then there is some situation or state of affairs that corresponds to my having that right.  So, we represent the notion of \"full use rights\" via the collection of all similar situations #$FullUseRights.  Note:  the situation of my having full use rights to my car is only an instance of #$FullUseRights during the temporal extent of the situation.  That situation starts when I gain those rights and ends when I lose them.  It is during this interval that the situation is an instance of #$FullUseRights.  If (#$rightsGranted MyBuyingMyCar #$FullUseRights) holds, then my situation became a member of #$FullUseRights by virtue of the event MyBuyingMyCar.  Nothing further is entailed regarding whether I still enjoy any rights to the object of the purchase MyBuyingMyCar.  #$rightsGranted simply states a causal sort of connection between an event and a type of situation.  Elements of #$SituationTypeByUserRights include: #$FullUseRights (the agent can do whatever s/he wants with it), #$ExclusiveUserRights (the agent is the only authorized user), #$PrimaryUserRights (this agent's uses take priority over everyone else's), #$GroupUserRightsOf-Organization (the agent's right to use something depends on membership in a group), and more.")
(comment AddressTypeByMailingStatus "A collection of collections.  Instances are the possible mailing statuses of instances of #$Address-LocationDesignator.  If an #$Address-LocationDesignator has #$BadMailingStatus, letters and packages being posted to this address are being returned to sender.  If an address has #$GoodMailingStatus, letters and packages posted to this address are not being returned.  Note that this does not necessarily mean they are received by their intended recipients.")
(comment ObjectTypeBySequentialStructuralFeature "A collection of collections.  Each instance is a collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that share some specific sequential structural property.  These collections characterize physical properties specific to objects that can be conceived of as `sequential' in a broad sense. Examples: #$Uninterrupted-SequentialStructure, #$Interrupted-SequentialStructure etc..")
(comment AnimalTypeByMentalState "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$AnimalTypeByMentalState is a subcollection of #$SentientAnimal whose instances share a mental state.")
(comment GraphicalStructureByFormat "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$GraphicalStructureByFormat is the collection of document structures or text strings characterized by some format or appearance.  An instance of #$GraphicalStructureByFormat may describe the arrangement or appearance of components within an instance of #$GraphicalStructure or it may describe the format of an instance of #$GraphicalStructure or #$AbstractInformationStructure within an encompassing instance of #$AbstractInformationStructure or #$GraphicalStructure.")
(comment TemporalThingTypeByExistentialStatus "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$TemporalThingTypeByExistentialStatus is a collection whose members in some way share an existential status, i.e., the extent to which they exist, fail to exist, or their existential history.")
(comment PageNumberingSchema "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PageNumberingSchema is a collection of texts that follow the same format for numbering pages.  Three of the most notable instances are #$SimpleSequentialSchema, #$RepetitionBySubsectionSchema, and the #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema.")
(comment Formality "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$Formality is a collection of instances of #$SomethingToWear such that each has the same degree of formality.  For  instance, #$Casual is the collection of instances of #$SomethingToWear that are considered casual such as jeans, sweaters, etc..")
(comment Virgo-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the sixth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Virgo, or The Virgin.  Ruled by the #$PlanetMercury. #$Persons born between August 23 and September 22 have this sign.See #$hasZodiacSign")
(comment Taurus-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the second sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Taurus, or The Bull. Ruled by #$PlanetVenus. #$Persons born between April 20 and May 20 have this sign.")
(comment MentallyConcentrating "The collection of #$SentientAnimals mentally focussed on a particular task.")
(comment Indoors-IsolatedFromOutside "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized which are in an indoor environment.  I.e. it is in a room of some sort with comfortable conditions to humans, e.g.  it is room temperature, normal humidity, has breathable air at roughly sea level pressure, is protected from weather, can have lightness/darkness independent of night and day, and so forth.")
(comment Aquarius-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the eleventh sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Aquarius, or The Water-Bearer. Ruled by the #$PlanetUranus. #$Persons born between January 20 and February 19 have this sign.")
(comment AbleMinded "The collection of #$SentientAnimals able to function using all their mental capacities.")
(comment Afloat-OnWater "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that are floating on some body of water.")
(comment RepetitionBySubsectionSchema "A subcollection of #$TextualMaterial.  Each instance of #$RepetitionBySubsectionSchema is divided into several formally delineated subsections, such as chapters or subsections, with each subsection exhibiting its own internal sequential numbering scheme.")
(comment Sagittarius-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the ninth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Sagittarius, or The Archer. Ruled by the #$PlanetJupiter. #$Persons born between November 23 and December 21 have this sign.")
(comment Silhouetted "The collection of objects that are sillhouetted.  An object is #$Silhouetted if light is shining on the side of the object away from the viewer, and there is comparatively little light shining on the side of the thing facing the viewer, so hardly any detail is discernible on the object.")
(comment ResumedAgency "Instances of this collection are  multi-individual agents that were previously instances of #$Disbanded but have resumed functioning the same agentive role that the multi-individual agent performed prior to its disbandment (see #$dateOfDisbandment).  Usually multi-individual agents with this status will be comprised of some or all of the individual agents that comprised the multi-individual agent previously.  If an agent has this attribute it implies that the multi-individual agent that resumes after a disbanding is the same agent as the multi-individual agent that disbanded (assuming common-sense identity theories).  The ability to take on this attribute, i.e., the ability of an agent to survive a break in its own agency, may underscore an important difference between persons as #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and instances of #$MultiIndividualAgent.")
(comment GoodMailingStatus "The collection of addresses whose instances enjoy the property that letters and packages posted to them are not returned.  Note that this does not necessarily mean that the letters are received by their intended recipients.")
(comment Scorpio-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the eighth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Scorpio, or The Scorpion. Ruled by the #$PlanetPluto. #$Persons born between October 23 and November 22 have this sign.")
(comment Gemini-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the third sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Gemini, or The Twins. Ruled by #$PlanetMercury. #$Persons born between May 21 and June 20 have this sign.")
(comment InOuterSpace "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that are not within the earth's atmosphere, or that of any other celestial body.")
(comment Pisces-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the twelfth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Pisces, or The Fish. Ruled by the #$PlanetNeptune. #$Persons born between February 20 and March 20 have this sign.")
(comment Aries-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the first sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Aries, or The Ram. Ruled by #$PlanetMars. #$Persons born between March 21 and April 19 have this sign.")
(comment Outdoors-ExposedToWeather "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that are outside under the sky, exposed to weather, not immersed in water, not in space, and not underground.")
(comment SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema "A subcollection of the collection #$TextualMaterial.  Each instance of #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema exhibits sequential numbering by increments of one throughout most of its main body: however, there are one or more 'priviledged' subsections exhibiting separate and internal sequential numbering schemas.  This arrangement is often to be observed in texts with introductions and appendices, which exhibit their own internal numbering separate from the rest of the text.")
(comment Capricorn-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the tenth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Capricorn, or The Goat. Ruled by the #$PlanetSaturn. #$Persons born between December 22 and January 19 have this sign.")
(comment InPublic "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that most english speakers relevant to the current microtheory would agree are \"in public\".  In most imaginable microtheories, there are a multitude of sufficient conditions for being in public (for example being outdoors in a city).  And a multitude of conditions implying that you are not \"in public\" e.g. you are in your home.  Please see the rules on the constant.")
(comment FrontLighting "The collection of front-lit objects.  An object is front-lit if light is shining on the side of the objects facing the viewer.")
(comment SimpleSequentialSchema "A subcollection of the collection of  instances of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType that are also specializations of #$TextualMaterial.  Instances of #$SimpleSequentialSchema number the first page 1 and continue with page numbering increasing by increments of 1 through to the last page.")
(comment Backlit "The collection of objects that are being lit from behind.")
(comment BadMailingStatus "The collection of addresses such that letters and packages posted to its instances are returned to sender.")
(comment Cancer-TheSign "The collection of people associated with the fourth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Cancer, or The Crab. Ruled by the #$MoonOfEarth. #$Persons born between June 21 and July 22 have this sign.")
(comment hasStyle "(#$hasStyle THING STYLE) means that the artifact THING is of the style or genre STYLE.  This is a specialization of #$isa and one of the broadest predicates you can use to ascribe a style to an object.  When possible try to use one of #$hasStyle's specializations like #$artisticStyle, #$clothingStyle, or #$architecturalStyle.")
(comment PlanComplexity "A specialization of #$EvaluativeAttribute.  Instances are levels of complexity for plans (e.g., instances of #$CourseOfAction).  These levels are represented as collections of plans that have that evaluatory complexity. The primary use of these instances is to determine whether a plan is likely to succeed or fail.")
(disjointWith TooComplex SufficientlySimple)
(disjointWith SufficientlySimple TooSimple)
(comment Epistemology "The subfield of #$Philosophy concerned with the nature of knowledge.")
(comment |rdfs:Resource| "#$rdfs:Resource is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$Thing")
(comment |rdfs:Class| "#$rdfs:Class is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$Collection")
(comment |rdfs:Property| "#$rdfs:Property is an imported DAML/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$BinaryPredicate")
(comment |rdf:Property| "#$rdf:Property is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$BinaryPredicate")
(comment |rdfs:Literal| "rdfs:Literal is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$SubLAtomicTerm")
(comment |xsd:float| "xsd:float is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$SubLRealNumber")
(comment |rdfs:type| "rdfs:type is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$isa")
(comment rdf-type "rdf:type is an imported RDF/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$isa")
(comment |rdfs:subPropertyOf| "rdfs:subPropertyOf is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$genlPreds")
(comment |rdfs:comment| "rdfs:comment is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$comment")
(comment |rdfs:seeAlso| "#$rdfs:seeAlso is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$seeAlso")
(comment |rdfs:isDefinedBy| "rdfs:isDefinedBy is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$containsInformationAbout")
(comment |rdfs:domain| "rdfs:domain is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$arg1Isa")
(comment |rdfs:range| "rdfs:range is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$arg2Isa")
(comment EnglishConceptualUnderspecificationMt "This microtheory contains generalization assertions between inferentially useful predicates and the underspecified (parsing) predicates that correspond to highly ambiguous relation-words of English.")
(comment AntiAmericanIdeology "#$AntiAmericanIdeology is a #$PoliticalBeliefSystem associated with agents -- groups, regimes, or individuals -- who have a negative vested interest (see #$negativeVestedInterest) in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment SymbolicSystems "The #$FieldOfStudy of Symbolic Systems. Those who study Symbolic Systems typically study a combination of #$ComputerScience, #$Psychology, #$Philosophy and #$Linguistics. They may concentrate in areas such as #$ArtificialIntelligence or Human-Computer Interaction.")
(comment MLBShowdown-TradingCardGame "#$MLBShowdown-TradingCardGame is produced by #$WizardsOfTheCoast-CommercialOrganization. It's licensed by #$MajorLeagueBaseball, and allows people to play #$BaseballGames and even #$BaseballSeasons with (#$ProfessionalFn #$BaseballPlayers). The cards are collectible and the game is strategic.")
(comment NFLShowdown-TradingCardGame "#$NFLShowdown-TradingCardGame is produced by #$WizardsOfTheCoast-CommercialOrganization. It's licensed by the #$NationalFootballLeague, and allows people to play #$FootballGame-Americans and even #$FootballSeasons with (#$ProfessionalFn #$FootballPlayers). The cards are collectible and the game is strategic.")
(comment CycAPIMt "A microtheory for assertions about the aspects of the #$CycProgram which are exposed in its API.")
(disjointWith PlayingAComputerGame (CollectionDifferenceFn PlayingABoardGame PlayingAComputerGame))
(comment Speaker "an indexical that refers successfully only in discourse contexts")
(comment BusinessGMt "The #$Microtheory that defines the concept of #$Business and the major business-related organizations and activities. Notable specializations include #$WesternBusinessPracticesMt and #$BusinessMoneyMt.")
(comment GKEFormulaTemplatesMt "A microtheory for formula templates used in Guided Knowledge Entry.")
(comment AcidsAndBases-ChemistryDomainMt "This is the microtheory in which general backward rules about Arrhenius, Broensted-Lowry, and Lewis acids and bases should be asserted.")
(comment ChemicalSolutions-ChemistryDomainMt "This is the microtheory in which general backward rules about solutions should be asserted.")
(comment FridayPostgresNimaKSConnSpec "The NIMA database running on Postgresql on friday.cyc.com.")
(comment JDBCDatabaseProtocol "The #$MachineProtocol for communicating with database servers.")
(comment abductiveExpansion "An instance of #$UnderstandingEnrichmentRelation.  (#$abductiveExpansion EXPLANANDUM HYP-EXPLANANS) means that if EXPLANANDUM is true, a good way to make sense of EXPLANANDUM is to postulate that HYP-EXPLANANS is true, and that HYP-EXPLANANS broadens the level of detail in terms of which EXPLANANDUM is understood.  For example, if it is true that someone applies toothpaste to a toothbrush (and that is our explanandum), and it is known that applications of toothpaste to toothbrushes are typical components of events in which one brushes one's own teeth, then a good way to make sense of the application of toothpaste to the toothbrush is to suppose (as a hypthothetical explanans) that there is an event of which the application is a component which is itself an event in which the applier is brushing her own teeth. (#$abductiveExpansion EXPLANANDUM HYP-EXPLANANS) also means that the truth of EXPLANANDUM is evidence (though generally not sufficient evidence) for the truth of HYP-EXPLANANS.  Thus, if a person applies toothpaste to a toothbrush, that is evidence that she is about to brush her teeth. It is possible that various legitimate values for HYP-EXPLANANS are mutually inconsistent for a single value of EXPLANANDUM -- perhaps the reason someone applies toothpaste to a toothbrush is to brush a dog's teeth.")
(comment InxightThingFinderCategoryDatabase "The database of categories used by the #$InxightThingFinder software to classify entities that are extracted from unstructured texts. Such categories include 'name', 'person', and 'place'. The set of categories may be extended by developers using Thing Finder for particular applications.")
(comment DispositionalQuantity "The collection of all the different quantities of dispositional properties; e.g. a particular degree of thermal conductivity.  The various specializations of this collection are the collections of all the degrees of a particular dispositional property.  For example, #$ThermalConductivity is a specialization of this collection and its instances are usually denoted with the generic value functions as in (#$HighAmountFn #$ThermalConductivity).  All degrees of thermal conductivity are instances of this collection even those not explicitly reified")
(comment UnitedStatesHistoryMt "The microtheory for representing #$AmericanHistory.")
(comment influencesThing "(#$influencesThing INFLUENCER INFLUENCED) holds just in case INFLUENCER in some  way has a non-trivial influence on INFLUENCED.  Exactly what counts as non-trivial  is context dependant.  A positive example would be  (#$influencesThing BlackTuesday (#$EconomyFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)). ")
(comment PhysiologicalQuantity "The collection of particular quantities of physiological properties; e.g. (#$HighAmountFn #$LevelOfPain).  Each reified specialization of this collection is a collection of quantities in a certain dimension; pain, strength, endurance etc.")
(comment HumanTypeByClothingSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeByClothingSize is a collection of people representing a particular body measurement.  Each reified  specialization is a collection of these collections that represent a particular type of body measurement (e.g. #$HumanTypeByInseamLength).")
(comment HumanTypeBySleeveLength "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeBySleeveLength is a collection of people that have the same sleeve length (arm length from shoulder to wrist).   Instances of this collection will usually be functionally denoted with #$SleeveLengthFn.   For instance, (#$SleeveLengthFn (#$Inch NUM)) denotes the collection of people whose arms measure NUM inches from shoulder to wrist.")
(comment HumanTypeByGloveSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeByGloveSize is a collection of people who wear the same size gloves.")
(comment HumanTypeByWomensGloveSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeByWomensGloveSize is a collection of people who wear the same size gloves.")
(comment HumanTypeByMensGloveSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeByMensGloveSize is a collection of people who wear the same size men's gloves.")
(comment HumanTypeByCupSize "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$HumanTypeByCupSize is a collection of people who have the same female breast cup size.  For instance, #$CupSize-C is the collection of people who have breast cup size C.")
(comment clothingSize "(#$clothingSize ITEM SIZE-TYPE SIZE) holds just in case ITEM is designed to fit people of size SIZE with respect to SIZE-TYPE.  For instance,  (#$clothingSize PairOfPants01 #$HumanTypeByInseamLength (#$InseamLengthFn (#$Inch 30))) holds  just in case  PairOfPants01 is designed to fit people whose inseam measures 30 inches.")
(comment Ragged "Miss Manners says:  yuck!")
(disjointWith Ragged Casual)
(disjointWith Casual Informal)
(disjointWith Informal SemiFormal)
(disjointWith SemiFormal VeryFormalClothing)
(comment CBRNE-QuestionSource-4-30-2003 "The source of questions in the CBRNE delivered to Cycorp on 4/30/2003.")
(comment VehicleDeviceState "The collection of states that a vehicle may be in as a device. This includes states such as #$OverdriveState and #$VehicleTransmissionState-Parked.")
(disjointWith HomoSapiens (CollectionDifferenceFn Mammal HomoSapiens))
(disjointWith HomoSapiens (CollectionDifferenceFn Animal HomoSapiens))
(comment AndrogynousPerson "People who exhibit characteristics or preferences stereotypical to or  befitting both men and women. Like its genls collection, this is a  culturally-relative distinction, since things that are considered masculine or feminine vary somewhat from culture to culture.  For this reason,  be sure to make assertions involving genders of persons in a  culture-specific microtheory.  ")
(comment cosatisfiableInArgs "A #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that the type-constraints on two specified argument-places of a given #$Relation are mutually compatible.  <code>(#$cosatisfiableInArgs RELN M N)</code> means that there could be a particular thing that is admissible as an argument (see #$admittedArgument) to <code>RELN</code> both in its <code>M</code>th and its <code>N</code>th argument-places.  More precisely: the (single-argument) argument-type constraints (see #$argIsa and #$argGenls) on <code>RELN</code>'s <code>M</code>th and <code>N</code>th argument-places do <i>not</i> preclude the possibility of there being some <code>THING</code> such that both <code>(#$admittedArgument THING M RELN)</code> and <code>(#$admittedArgument THING N RELN)</code> hold.  (Note that this by itself does not entail that such a <code>THING</code> actually exists -- though typically that will be the case -- but only that the existence of such a thing is logically compatible with the argument-constraints on <code>RELN</code>.)
<p>
Also note that <code>(#$cosatisfiableInArgs RELN M N)</code> is <i>not</i> incompatible with <code>(#$interArgDifferent RELN M N)</code>.  The latter sentence is not about argument-constraints but about truth-conditions, and means that <code>RELN</code> does not hold of any sequence whose <code>M</code>th and <code>N</code>th items are identical.  For example, <code>(#$cosatisfiableInArgs #$biologicalMother 1 2)</code> and <code>(#$interArgDifferent #$biologicalMother 1 2)</code> both hold: a given animal might both have a mother and be a mother, but cannot be its own mother.
<p>
See also the shared #$NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement.")
(comment attributeCleanupNote "this constant was created as a repository for  comments regarding the attribute cleanup.")
(comment antidote "An instance of #$IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate.  (#$antidote POISON-TYPE ANTIDOTE-TYPE) says that ANTIDOTE-TYPE is an antidote for POISON-TYPE.  That is, ailments due to exposure to POISON-TYPE can be minimized or counteracted by the introduction of instances of ANTIDOTE-TYPE into the maleficiary's system.")
(comment objectActsOnObjectInEvent "(#$objectActsOnObjectInEvent EVENT SOMETHING SOMETHING-ELSE) holds iff SOMETHING-ELSE is a #$patient-Generic in the #$Event as a proximal effect of a role played by SOMETHING. The latter's (relevant) role must be a specialization of #$actors, and might or might not be an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate. For example, if it #$holdsSometimeDuring an event that a #$Gun #$launchesProjectile a certain #$ProjectileShellAssembly, then there ought to be a rule which determines that (#$objectActsOnObjectInEvent <EVENT> <THE GUN> <THE PSA>) holds as well, and Cyc should further be able to determine that <THE GUN> acts on the parts of <THE PSA>, namely the #$ProjectileCasing and #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet which are (originally) #$physicalParts of it. This predicate is not transitive, in that if the SOMETHING-ELSE acts on some other object, this doesn't mean that SOMETHING acts on it as well, So, in this example, the fact that (#$objectActsOnObjectInEvent <EVENT> <THE BULLET> <THE OBJECT>) holds for whatever the bullet hits, this is not an argument for (#$objectActsOnObjectInEvent <EVENT> <THE GUN> <THE OBJECT>) holding as well (of course, its holding coincidentally isn't ruled out, either).")
(comment hasIntelligenceLevel "(#$hasIntelligenceLevel INT-ANIMAL INT-LEVEL) holds just in case INT-ANIMAL has the quantity of intelligence designated by INT-LEVEL.  For instance, (#$hasIntelligenceLevel #$AlbertEinstein #$HighIntelligence).")
(comment situationTemporalParts "A #$TemporalPartPredicate and a specialization of both #$timeSlices and #$subSituations (qq.v.).  #$situationTemporalParts is the #$timeSlices relation restricted (via #$typedGenlPreds) to holding between instances of #$Situation.  <code>(#$situationTemporalParts SIT SITPART)</code> means that <code>SITPART</code> is a temporal part, or time-slice, of <code>SIT</code>, and is a temporal situation in its own right.  Thus, <code>SITPART</code> is the situation that includes \"everything there is to\" <code>SIT</code> during (and only during) the particular #$TimeInterval that <code>SITPART</code> occupies.  For a similar predicate that only relates events, see the specialization #$subProcesses.")
(comment Afloat-Generic "The collection of instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that are floating on some liquid.  See the specialization #$Afloat-OnWater for spatial things that are floating specifically on #$Water.")
(comment BasicVegetarianDiet "An instance of #$DietProgram representing the most basic of vegetarian diets.  #$BasicVegetarianDiet is characterized simply by a proscription (see #$dietProscribes) against eating #$Meat.  It is noncommittal regarding what sorts of thing one should eat (see #$dietPrescribes).")
(comment MyTestScript "test script for #$SchedulingASocialDinnerAtRestaurant - assert (instantiatesScript MyTestScript #$SchedulingASocialDinnerAtRestaurant) to gen. subscenes.")
(comment IntermittentlyFlawedFn "A #$UnaryIntersectionFunction that maps a given type of thing to the collection of all intermittently flawed things of that type.  (#$IntermittentlyFlawedFn THING) denotes the collection of instances of THING that possess at least one intermittent flaw.")
(comment FlawedFn "A #$UnaryIntersectionFunction that maps a given type of thing onto the collection of all flawed things of that type.  (#$FlawedFn THING) denotes the collection of instances of THING that are flawed in some way.")
(comment residentsOfRegion "(#$residentsOfRegion GEO-THING RES-COL) means that RES-COL is the collection of people who are residents of the (#$territoryOf the) #$GeographicalThing GEO-THING.")
(comment EconomicInterestsOfFn "A unary function that maps a given #$SocialBeing to the collection of its #$EconomicInterests (q.v.).  (#$EconomicInterestsOfFn AGENT) is the collection ECON-INT-COL, consisting of all of (and only) AGENT's economic interests.  See also #$economicInterestIn.")
(comment LexicalAttribute "All lexical terms that were formerly attributes will now reside here.")
(comment hasDispositionalQuantity "(#$hasDispositionalQuantity TEMP-THING DISP-QUANT) holds just in case the temporal thing TEMP-THING has the dispositional quality in the quantity specified.  This is a very general predicate and should only be used when a more specific predicate is not available.")
(comment truthOfTheory "(#$truthOfTheory THEORY TV) holds just in case THEORY has the truth value TV.  For instance, if #$ZermeloFrankel-SetTheory describes a correct theory of set behavior (under a realist assumption that sets exist), then (#$truthOfTheory #$ZermeloFrankel-SetTheory  #$MonotonicallyTrue) holds.")
(comment hasPollutionIntensity "(#$hasPollutionIntensity TEMP-THING POLL-QUANT) holds just in case the temporal thing TEMP-THING has the pollution intensity in the quantity specified.  ")
(comment quantityOfChange "(#$quantityOfChange TEMP-THING QUANT) holds just in case the temporal thing TEMP-THING has changed some quality in the quantity specified.  this is a very general predicate since the type of change is not specified.  When possible try to use a more informative predicate (c.f. #$changesQuantityInDirection). ")
(comment CenterForDiseaseControlandPreventionWebsite "The CDC website, available at http://www.cdc.gov/.")
(comment situationConstituentWithTypeAndDesc "(#$situationConstituentWithTypeAndDesc SIT IND TYPE DESC) means that the #$Individual IND is both a participant in the #$Situation SIT (#$situationConstituents) and is an instance of TYPE which can be refrred with the description (or name) DESC.")
(comment situationConstituentWithType "(#$situationConstituentWithType SIT IND TYP) means that the #$Individual IND is both a participant in the #$Situation SIT (#$situationConstituents) and is an instance of TYPE.")
(comment situationConstituentWithDesc "(#$situationConstituentWithDesc SIT IND STRING) means that the #$Individual IND is both a participant in the #$Situation SIT (#$situationConstituents) and may be referred to with the #$TextString STRING.")
(comment reifiedAsForEfficiency "This predicate states that its arg2 (a #$CycLConstant) is acting as a placeholder for arg1 (which can be anything). This is similar to specs of #$equals but avoids any inference pitfalls that such specs might run into. The proximal motivation for this constant is to work around the problems created by the #$SchemaObjectFns for the BBN/CDE strengthening project, particularly the occasionally-horrendous access times to the database, and the fact that the #$SchemaObjectFns tend to neutralize or bog down inferences using predicates like #$isa and #$genls.")
(comment VectorIntervalType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a specialization of #$VectorInterval.")
(comment LakeBed "A dried up or drained area of a former lake.")
(comment ReformulatorMode-Loosen "A #$ReformulatorMode in which #$CycLExpressions are reformulated into a form that, though not preferred, uses a syntax that allows for wff-substitutions in the #$GuidedKnowledgeEntryTool.")
(comment UseInLoosenMode "An instance of #$ReformulatorRuleProperty.  Instances are #$CycLReformulatorRules that are used by the reformulator when it is called in #$ReformulatorMode-Loosen.")
(comment industryOfRegion "(#$industryOfRegion LOCAL-INDUSTRY INDUSTRY-TYPE REGION)
means that LOCAL-INDUSTRY is of type INDUSTRY-TYPE and 'belongs to'
REGION -- that is, its income contributes to the Gross National
Product of the nation containing REGION. If a private industry, it
pays taxes to the national government of REGION. Not all of the
industry's facilities are necessarily located in REGION. For instance,
it may have factories in countries where labor is cheaper. See also
#$IndustryOfRegionFn.")
(comment PersonalQuantity "The collection of all quantities of features that
are had by individuals by virtue of their actions or decisions.  This is a rather vague but intuitive notion.  For instance, The #$IntelligenceLevel of some individual is not something that is generally thought to be under their conscious control though their #$LevelOfFitness often is.  These are the sort of personal properties that often vary with the circumstances.  ")
(comment USStateDepartmentWebsite-PatternsOfGlobalTerrorism2000 "A section of the US State Department Website dedicated to tracking terrorism, entitled 'Patterns Of Global Terrorism'.  A report like this one is published annually, while this one is for the year 2000. This website is available at http://www.state.gov/s/ct/rls/pgtrpt/2000/.")
(comment PhenotypeFeatureType "A collection of collections each of which represents a particular phenotype.  A phenotype is a purely observable physical feature of an organism.  Hair color, blood type, cell structure, etc. all count as types of phenotypes.  Definitive of phenotypes is that they are features of organisms that are the physical manifestations of the gene patterns and environment of the organism.")
(comment degreesOfActivityAbility "The corresponding predicate to #$AbilityToFn.  
(#$degreesOfActivityAbility ACTIVITY COLL) holds just in case COLL is the collection of all
the different degrees of abilities to do activity.")
(comment hasDiplomaticRelationsWith "(hasDiplomaticRelationsWith COUNTRY1 COUNTRY2) means that COUNTRY1 has some
sort of positive diplomatic standing with COUNTRY2).")
(comment hasStatusWithAgent-Generic "A predicate that expresses the status an agent has with another agent.
(#$hasStatusWithAgent-Generic AGENT1 (STATUSFN AGENT2)) means that AGENT2 considers
AGENT1 to have the status.  For example, (#$hasStatusWithAgent-Generic Bob (#$EmployeeFn Kinko's)) means that Bob is an instance of the collection of Kinko employees or that, at the very least, Kinko's believes Bob has that status.  Please use a more specific predicate whenever possible.")
(comment hasDiplomaticStatusWithAgent "#$hasDiplomaticStatusWithAgent is a specialization of #$isa.  (#$hasDiplomaticStatusWithAgent AGENT STATUS) means that AGENT has the particular status represented by STATUS.  Most often, STATUS will be expressed by a NART denoting the collection of individuals that have that status.
<p>
For example, (#$NotDiplomaticallyRecognizedByFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) is the collection of countries that are not diplomatically recognized by the USA.
<p>
<p>")
(comment notDiplomaticallyRecognizedBy "(notDiplomaticallyRecognizedBy COUNTRY1 COUNTRY2) means that COUNTRY2 does
not extend diplomatic recognition to COUNTRY1. ")
(comment NotDiplomaticallyRecognizedByFn "(NotDiplomaticallyRecognizedByFn COUNTRY) is the collection of all 
countries that are not diplomatically recognized by COUNTRY.")
(comment hasStatusWithOrganization "(#$hasStatusWithOrganization AGENT STATUS) means that AGENT has some membership STATUS, where STATUS is a NART created compositionsally with an Organization. For instance (#$hasStatusWithOrganization #$Angola (#$MemberFn #$UnitedNationsOrganization)) in <MT INTERVAL PARAMETER> means it is true in MT at least during the time interval INTERVAL to granularity PARAMETER that Angola has membership status with respect to the United Nations .")
(comment mayObserveOrgProceedings "The status of an agent that is permitted to have observers at the proceedings of an organization, such as the #$UnitedNationsOrganization.")
(comment PositiveAmountFn "A #$GenericValueFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType to a #$GenericQuantity of that type.  In a given context, <code>(#$PositiveAmountFn QUANTTYPE)</code> is the properly interval-like quantity (and instance) of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> that is considered a <i>positive amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.
<p>
For example, (#$PositiveAmountFn #$Happiness) is the range of happiness from very low to very high happiness.  It is more (see #$followingValue) than (#$NoAmountFn #$Happiness).
<p>
See also the corresponding predicate #$positiveAmountOf.")
(comment SuspendedMemberFn "All members of the collection (SuspendedMemberFn ?ORG) were former members of ORG, but their membership has been suspended.")
(comment suspendedFromOrganization "(suspendedFromOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT used to be a member of  ORG, but has been suspended from that organization.")
(comment emeritusMemberOf "(#$emeritusMemberOf AGT ORG) means that AGT used to be a member of  ORG, but has since retired or left without prejudice.")
(comment expelledFromOrganization "(#$expelledFromOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT used to be a member of  ORG, but was expelled and is not a member at least during the time interval specified by the assertion.  No claim is made as to whether AGT is a member of ORG outside of the time interval in which this assertion is made.  So, #$expelledFromOrganization doesn't express the brute fact that AGT at some time in the past was expelled from ORG.  Rather, it gives a status that can hold for some time interval and fail to hold at some later interval if they are allowed to rejoin.  Typically, though, this will hold of AGT and ORG from the time of the expulsion till the end of the temporal extent of AGT or ORG.")
(comment EmeritusMemberFn "All members of the collection (EmeritusMemberFn ?ORG) were former members of ORG, but they have retired or otherwise separated from that ORG without  prejudice.  Emeritus members may or may not be granted observer  or even voting status.")
(comment ExpelledMemberFn "All members of the collection (ExpelledMemberFn ?ORG) were former members of ORG, but they have been permanently expelled.")
(comment foundingMemberOfOrganization "(#$foundingMemberOfOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT founded or assisted in founding ORG, and is still a member of ORG.")
(comment FoundingMemberFn "(#$FoundingMemberFn ORG) is the collection of all the founding members of ORG.  Each instance may or may not still be a member of ORG.")
(comment permanentMemberOfOrganization "(permanentMemberOfOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT is a permanent member of ORG, and AGT's membership status cannot be suspended or revoked.")
(comment appointedToAndConfirmedInOrganization "(appointedToAndConfirmedInOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT is a member of an organization ORG, and furthermore gained AGT's member status by being  both appointed by the appropriate official and then confirmed by some body.")
(comment appointedToOrganization "(appointedToOrganization AGT ORG) means that AGT is a member of the organization ORG, and furthermore gained AGT's member status as a result of an appointment.")
(comment ElectedMemberFn "All members of the collection (ElectedMemberFn ?ORG) are current members of  ORG, and have acheived this membership status by some election.")
(comment PermanentMemberFn "All members of the collection (PermanentMemberFn ?ORG) are current members of  ORG, and their memberships can neither be suspended or revoked.")
(comment AppointedMemberFn "All members of the collection (AppointedMemberFn ?ORG) are current members of  ORG, and have acheived this membership status by some appointment.")
(comment ZipCodeStemFn "A unary #$TermMacroFunction that maps #$ZipCode strings to their five-digit intial stems: it removes the four-digit suffix (and preceding hyphen) from #$ZipCode-NineDigits and leaves #$ZipCode-FiveDigits as-is.  (#$ZipCodeStemFn ZIP) is the string ZIP5 composed of the first five digits in ZIP.  If ZIP is already a #$ZipCode-FiveDigit, then ZIP5 = ZIP.  For example, #$ZipCodeStemFn maps both of the strings \"01122-3344\" and \"01122\" to the string \"01122\" itself.  This function can be used in conjunction with #$StringToIntegerFn to compare zip codes numerically.")
(comment worksOffsiteFor "(worksOffsiteFor EMPLOYEE EMPLOYER) means that EMPLOYEE is actively working for EMPLOYER, but at a location other than the main office(s).")
(comment employmentStatus "(#$employmentStatus PERSON STATUS) means that PERSON has a particular employment status with respect to a particular person, company or organization. For instance, (#$employmentStatus JOHN-DOE (#$EmployeeFn FOO-INC)) means that JOHN-DOE is a current employee of FOO-INC.")
(comment terminatedEmployeeOf "(terminatedEmployeeOf EMPLOYEE EMPLOYER) means that EMPLOYEE resigned, been fired or otherwise terminated from his/her job working for EMPLOYER.")
(comment EmployeeFn "<code>(#$EmployeeFn ORG)</code> is collection of individuals that are currently employees of ORG.  <code>(#$employmentStatus AGENT (#$EmployeeFn ORG))</code> means that <code>AGENT</code> is a current employee of <code>ORG</code>.")
(comment OffsiteEmployeeFn "(#$OffsiteEmployeeFn ORG) is the collection of employees of ORG that work offsite.  (#$employmentStatus AGENT (#$OffsiteEmployeeFn ORG)) means that AGENT is a current employee of ORG, but does not work at the main headquarters of ORG. ")
(comment onProbationInOrganization "(onProbationInOrganization AGENT ORG) means that AGENT is on probation with the ORG. Usually some rule infraction precedes this state.")
(comment dismissedFromOrganization "(dismissedFromOrganization AGENT ORG) means that AGENT has been dismissed from the organization ORG. Usually implies some disagreement, although employees who are layed off probably fall into this category.")
(comment businessProhibitionBetween "(#$businessProhibitionBetween COUNTRY1 COUNTRY2) is a relationship between the governments of COUNTRY1 and COUNTRY2 meaning that trade is not permitted to occur between them.")
(disjointWith Eyewear-NonPrescription Eyewear-Corrective)
(comment ParaconsistentLogic "The subfield of #$Logic which is concerned with drawing inferences from inconsistent bodies of information in a sensible way.  #$ParaconsistentLogic was first developed by Stanislaw Jaskowski of #$Poland and Newton da Costa of #$Brazil.")
(comment RelevanceLogic "The subfield of #$ParaconsistentLogic which is concerned with capturing the idea that if a #$Sentence S1 entails a #$Sentence S2, S1 ought to be _relevant_ (in some sense) to S2.  (In practice, this usually amounts to the notion that S1 and S2 ought to share at least one non-logical constant.)  #$RelevanceLogic was initially developed by Alan Ross Anderson and Nuel Belnap of the #$UniversityOfPittsburgh.  In #$Australasia-Region, #$RelevanceLogic is usually known as \"relevant logic\".")
(comment topicOfDatabase "(#$topicOfDatabase DB TOPIC) means that TOPIC is a primary topic of DB, a #$Database-AbstractContent.  TOPIC may characterize the type of data contained in DB, or some individual centrally involved in that data.  E.g., a database of terrorist attacks in the Middle East may have as topics both the activity-type #$TerroristAttack and the place #$MiddleEast-Region.")
(comment TheCycProcessOwner "#$TheCycProcessOwner denotes the cyclist (if any) who started up (and is thererfore the process `owner') the process for the current, individual Cyc image. Note that for any given thread of execution, this may be (and often is) the same as #$TheUser.")
(comment intraArgRelnIntraResultReln "A quaternary #$MetaFunction (q.v.) predicate used for stating that when a given function is applied to successive argument(-sequence)s that are related in a specified way, then the successive resulting values will themselves be related in another specified way.  (#$intraArgRelnIntraResultReln FUNC N PRED-ARGS PRED-RESULTS) means that when FUNC is applied to successive argument-sequences ARGS1 and ARGS2 such that (i) ARGS1 and ARGS2 differ (at most) only in their respective Nth items ARGN1 and ARGN2 and (ii) (PRED-ARGS ARGN1 ARGN2) holds, then (PRED-RESULTS (FUNC . ARGS1) (FUNC . ARGS2)) holds.  For example, (#$intraArgRelnIntraResultReln #$GroupOfCardinalityFn 2 #$different #$disjointWith) means that for any TYPE, N, and M, if N =/ M, then these two collections are disjoint:
<p>
<pre>
  (#$GroupOfCardinalityFn TYPE N)
  (#$GroupOfCardinalityFn TYPE M) .
</pre>")
(comment potentialTargetForScriptedAttackType "(#$potentialTargetForScriptedAttackType TARGET SCRIPTED-ATTACK-TYPE) holds just in case TARGET is a likely target for attacks of type SCRIPTED-ATTACK-TYPE.  Depending on the attack type different conditions must hold for this to be true of some target.  For instance, (#$potentialTargetForScriptedAttackType CHEMICAL-PLANT-01 #$AttackingAnInstallationByIntentionalPlaneCrash) holds, if the destruction of CHEMICAL-PLANT-01 is likely to cause panic or harm to the surrounding community and it is possible for the attack to occur.  In order for this predicate to hold of some TARGET and attack type, it must be possible for there to exist an instance of the attack type, ATTACK in which (#$intendedAttackTargets ATTACK TARGET) holds.  Furthermore, TARGET must be vulnerable to (in some sense) the type of attack indicated by SCRIPTED-ATTACK-TYPE -- Fort Knox will never be a potential target, in this sense, of AttackByBB-Gun even if some particular BB-gun attack targets it.")
(comment OWLFort "The KB subset collection of OWL terms.")
(comment OWLTerm "The KB subset collection of OWL constants.")
(comment OWLNart "The KB subset collection of OWL NARTs.")
(comment OWLAnonymousClass "The collection of OWL anonymous classes not having a #$UniformResourceIdentifier (URI).")
(comment temporalIndexForSentenceInMt "(#$temporalIndexForSentenceInMt TIME-INTERVAL PAR SENT MT) holds just in case SENT is true in MT at TIME-INTERVAL to the granularity determined by PAR.  That is, iff SENT holds in MT at every time interval t that is subsumed by TIME-INTERVAL that subsumes some instance of PAR.
<p>
More formally:
<p>
(#$temporalIndexForSentenceInMt TIME-INTERVAL PAR SENT MT)
<p>
iff
<p>
(#$ist (#$MtSpace MT
(#$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn TIME-INTERVAL PAR)) SENT).")
(comment |owl:Thing| "#$owl:Thing is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$Thing")
(comment |rdf:XMLLiteral| "rdf:XMLLiteral is an imported RDF/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$XMLFile")
(comment |owl:differentFrom| "owl:differentFrom is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$different")
(comment |owl:equivalentProperty| "owl:equivalentProperty is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$synonymousExternalConcept")
(comment |owl:DeprecatedClass| "The collection of OWL classes that are deprecated.")
(comment |owl:DeprecatedProperty| "The collection of OWL properties that are deprecated.")
(comment |owl:Nothing| "owl:Nothing is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$Nothing")
(comment OntologyRelatingPredicate "Instances of ontologyRelatingPredicate are binary predicates used to relate two ontology instances. ")
(comment |owl:backwardCompatibleWith| "owl:backwardCompatibleWith is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$backwardsCompatibleOntology")
(comment |owl:disjointWith| "owl:disjointWith is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$disjointWith")
(comment |owl:sameAs| "owl:sameAs is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$equals")
(comment |owl:equivalentClass| "owl:equivalentClass is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$coExtensional")
(comment |owl:incompatibleWith| "owl:incompatibleWith is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$incompatibleOntology.")
(comment |owl:inverseOf| "owl:InverseOf is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$inverseBinaryPredicateOf")
(comment |owl:priorVersion| "owl:priorVersion is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$ontologyPriorVersion")
(comment |owl:versionInfo| "owl:versionInfo is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$ontologyVersionInfo.")
(comment BehaviorLanguageFORT "The KB subset collection of Behavior Language constants.")
(comment CBLTaskMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage task method.")
(comment CBLSensationMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage sensation method.")
(comment CBLMessageMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage message method.")
(comment CBLMethod "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage methods.")
(comment CBLUtilityMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage utility method.")
(comment CBLCriticMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage critic method.")
(comment CBLSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage sensors that is partitioned into software and hardware sensors.")
(comment computationForLanguage "(computationForLanguage COMPUTATION-EVENT COMPUTER-LANGUAGE) means that COMPUTATION-EVENT is an element of program scripts written in COMPUTER-LANGUAGE. ")
(comment CBLActuator "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuators that is partitioned into hardware and software actuators.")
(comment CBLActuatorSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuator-sensors that is partitioned into hardware and software sensor-actuators.")
(comment CBLCommand "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage command events.")
(comment CBLTask "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage task command events.")
(comment CBLGroup "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage group command events.")
(comment CBLForEach "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage for-each command events.")
(comment CBLWhile "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage while command events.")
(comment CBLWithProbability "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage with-probability command events.")
(comment CBLCall "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage call command events.")
(comment CBLSucceed "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage succeed command events.")
(comment CBLFail "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage fail command events.")
(comment CBLThrow "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage throw command events.")
(comment ComputationEvent "This is the collection of program actions that happen in a particular computer (have a location) and change the state of that computer.")
(comment CBLPhysicalSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage sensors which are implemented as hardware devices.")
(comment CBLSoftwareSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage sensors that are implemented in software as computer processes.")
(comment CBLSoftwareActuator "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuators that are implemented in software as computer processes.")
(comment CBLSoftwareActuatorSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuator-sensors that are implemented in software as computer processes.")
(comment CBLPhysicalActuator "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuators which are implemented as hardware devices.")
(comment CBLPhysicalActuatorSensor "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage actuator-sensors which are implemented as hardware devices.")
(comment CBLSuspend "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage suspend command events.")
(comment CBLResume "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage resume command events.")
(comment CBLAssign "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage assign command events.")
(comment CBLWithLearning "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage with-learning command events.")
(comment CBLSend "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage send command events.")
(comment CBLBuiltInTaskMethod "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events.")
(comment CBLDefinedTaskMethod "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage defined (not built-in) task command events.")
(comment CBLGetAvailableCycImagesAndHosts "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that get available Cyc images and hosts.")
(comment CBLCycImageControl "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that control Cyc images.")
(comment CBLFindConstant "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that find Cyc constants.")
(comment CBLCreateConstant "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that create Cyc constants.")
(comment CBLRenameConstant "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that rename Cyc constants.")
(comment CBLKillConstant "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that kill Cyc constants.")
(comment CBLMust "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage command events that check conditions that must be true.  They are most typically used to verify method preconditions and postconditions.")
(comment CBLGetRelevantObjects "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that get relevant objects for a given object of attention, given relevancy relationship and relevant context.")
(comment CBLTrainRelevantObjects "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that train which objects are relevant for the given object of attention, given relevancy relationship and given context.")
(comment CBLObjectHavingDocumentation "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage terms that can have documentation.")
(comment CBLObjectHavingJustification "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage terms that can have justification.")
(comment CycBehaviorLanguageSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle which collects microtheories containing #$CycBehaviorLanguage node and method definitions.")
(comment cblJustification "(cblJustification CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-OBJECT CYCL-SENTENCE) means that CYCL-SENTENCE provides justification existence and behavior of the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-OBJECT.")
(comment CBLObjectHavingName "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage terms that can have a name.")
(comment cblName "(cblName CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-OBJECT PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER provides the name for the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-OBJECT.")
(comment CBLStateVariable "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage state variables.")
(comment CBLParameter "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage method parameters.")
(comment cblNodeHasTaskMethod "(cblNodeHasTaskMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-METHOD as a means of handling the associated task.")
(comment cblNodeHasSensationMethod "(cblNodeHasSensationMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSATION-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSATION-METHOD as a means of handling the associated sensation.")
(comment cblNodeHasMessageMethod "(cblNodeHasMessageMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-MESSAGE-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-MESSAGE-METHOD as a means of handling the associated message.")
(comment cblMethodForTask "(cblMethodForTask CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-METHOD PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-METHOD is a method for #$CycBehaviorLanguage tasks identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.  For the method to be applicable, the input and output parameters must also match by number and type subsumption.")
(comment cblMethodForSensation "(cblMethodForSensation CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSATION-METHOD PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSATION-METHOD is a method for #$CycBehaviorLanguage sensations identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.  For the method to be applicable, the input and output parameters must also match by number and type subsumption.")
(comment cblMethodForMessage "(cblMethodForMessage CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-MESSAGE-METHOD PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-MESSAGE-METHOD is a method for #$CycBehaviorLanguage messages identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.  For the method to be applicable, the input and output parameters must also match by number and type subsumption.")
(comment cblInputParameters "(cblInputParameters CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD LIST) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has LIST of #$CBLParameters as its input parameters.")
(comment cblOutputParameters "(cblOutputParameters CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD LIST) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has LIST as its output parameters.")
(comment cblEffect "(cblEffect CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD CYCL-SENTENCE) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has as it effect (suitable for planning) CYCL-SENTENCE.  It is not used by the #$CycBehaviorEngine when interpreting #$CycBehaviorLanguage.")
(comment cblSpecificPrecondition "(cblSpecificPrecondition CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD CYCL-SENTENCE) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has as its specific precondition CYCL-SENTENCE.  The #$CycBehaviorEngine uses this precondition to quickly filter applicable methods to handle a task, sensation, message or exception.")
(comment cblMethodHasUtilityMethod "(cblMethodHasUtilityMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-UTILITY-METHOD) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-UTILITY-METHOD.  The #$CycBehaviorEngine uses this method to rank applicable methods to handle a task, sensation, message or exception.")
(comment cblMethodHasCriticMethod "(cblMethodHasCriticMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-CRITIC-METHOD) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-CRITIC-METHOD.  The #$CycBehaviorEngine executes the critic method after the given task, sensation, message or exception method to create a critique of the primary method's performance.")
(comment cblMethodSucceedWhen "(cblMethodSucceedWhen METHOD EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage METHOD has EXPRESSION as its success condition.")
(comment cblMethodFailWhen "(cblMethodFailWhen METHOD EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage METHOD has EXPRESSION as its failure condition.")
(comment cblAdditionalParameter "(cblAdditionalParameter CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-UTILITY-METHOD CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-PARAMETER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-UTILITY-METHOD has CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-PARAMETER as one of its additional input parameters.")
(comment cblSenses "(cblSenses CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSOR PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-SENSOR senses the sensation type identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.")
(comment cblSendsMessage "(cblSendsMessage ACTUATOR-OR-SENSOR PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that ACTUATOR-OR-SENSOR may send the message type identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.")
(comment CBLNode-Self "This individual denotes the self node in the #$CycBehaviorLanguage.")
(comment cblTaskToNode "(cblPerformTaskAtNode TASK-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage TASK-COMMAND is sent to the node identified by evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblRelationshipHasKeyword "(cblRelationshipHasKeyword BINARY-PREDICATE STRING) means that the CycL BINARY-PREDICATE corresponds to a defining relationship in #$CycBehaviorLanguage and has STRING as its keyword.")
(comment cblInputParameterValues "(cblInputParameterValues CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND LIST) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND has the given LIST of input values that are evaluated and are positionally bound to the corresponding input parameters before the method begins interpretation by the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment cblBindOutputTo "(cblBindOutputTo CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND LIST) means that the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND output parameters are positionally bound to the #$CBLStateVariables contained in LIST.")
(comment cblGroupLock "(cblGroupLock GROUP-COMMAND STATE-OBJECT) means that GROUP-COMMAND will obtain a lock on the resource STATE-OBJECT, waiting if necessary if another execution thread has the lock.  The #$CycBehaviorEngine ensures that the locked command group will execute without conflict from another execution thread.")
(comment cblPerformAtAbsouteTime "(cblPerformAtAbsouteTime CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND is performed at the absolute time resulting from evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblPerformInRelativeTime "(cblPerformInRelativeTime CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-TASK-COMMAND is performed at the relative time (from the method start) that results from evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingParallelSubtasks "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands for which the #$CycBehaviorEngine will execute subtasks in parallel.")
(comment cblArrangeOrderGivenStateVariables "(cblInputParameters CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD LIST) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has LIST of #$CBLParameters as its input parameters.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingGroup "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands having an explicit group (see #$CBLGroup).")
(comment cblObjectTypeHasKeyword "(cblObjectTypeHasKeyword OBJECT-TYPE STRING) means that the CycL OBJECT-TYPE corresponds to a defining characteristic in #$CycBehaviorLanguage and has STRING as its keyword.")
(comment CBLUnassert "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in task command events that unassert sentences.")
(comment CBLAsk "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage command events that ask queries.")
(comment cblTaskName "(cblTaskName TASK-COMMAND PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that within #$CycBehaviorLanguage, PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER provides the task name for the TASK-COMMAND to accomplish.")
(comment cblForEachStateVariable "(cblForEachStateVariable FOR-EACH-COMMAND STATE-VARIABLE) means that within #$CycBehaviorLanguage, STATE-VARIABLE provides the state variable for binding in the FOR-EACH-COMMAND.")
(comment cblForEachIn "(cblForEachIn FOR-EACH-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage FOR-EACH-COMMAND will bind the associated state variable to each element of the list resulting from evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment CBLForEachHavingParallelBindings "This is the collection of #$CBLForEach commands for which the #$CycBehaviorEngine will bind all list values in parallel.")
(comment cblWhileCondition "(cblWhileCondition WHILE-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage WHILE-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as its Boolean condition.")
(comment cblWithProbabilityExpression "(cblWithProbabilityExpression WITH-PROBABILITY-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage WITH-PROBABILITY-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as its probability.")
(comment cblWIthProbabiltyGiven "(cblWIthProbabiltyGiven WITH-PROBABILITY-COMMAND LIST) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage WITH-PROBABILITY-COMMAND has LIST of #$CBLStateVariables as its relevant state variables.")
(comment cblCallObjectType "(cblCallObjectType CALL-COMMAND OBJECT-TYPE) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage CALL-COMMAND has OBJECT-TYPE as the the type of the object on which call the given method.")
(comment cblCallObject "(cblCallObjectMethod CALL-COMMAND PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage CALL-COMMAND calls the Java object identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.")
(comment cblCallMethod "(cblCallMethod CALL-COMMAND PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage CALL-COMMAND calls the Java method identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.")
(comment cblBindResultTo "(cblBindResultTo COMMAND STATE-VARIABLE) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMAND binds the result of the comand to STATE-VARIABLE.")
(comment cblSucceedExpression "(cblSucceedExpression SUCCEED-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage SUCCEED-COMMAND sends a success message containing the evaluated EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblFailExpression "(cblFailExpression FAIL-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage FAIL-COMMAND sends a failure message containing the evaluated EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblParameterValues "(cblParameterValues COMMAND LIST) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMAND has LIST of arguments to be evaluated as its inputs.")
(comment cblSuspendExpression "(cblSuspendExpression SUSPEND-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage SUSPEND-COMMAND suspends the containing execution thread and notifies the #$CycBehaviorEngine that the object resulting from evaluating EXPRESSION is to be used to resume the thread.  See #$CBLResume")
(comment cblResumeExpression "(cblResumeExpression RESUME-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage RESUME-COMMAND resumes the suspended execution thread identified by evaluating EXPRESSION.  See #$CBLSuspend.")
(comment CBLAssignFromAmong "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage assign-from-among command events.")
(comment cblAssignExpression "(cblAssignExpression ASSIGN-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASSIGN-COMMAND has EXPRESSION to be evaluated and assigned to the given state variable.")
(comment cblAssignFromAmongExpressions "(cblAssignFromAmongExpressions ASSIGN-FROM-AMONG-COMMAND LIST) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASSIGN-FROM-AMONG-COMMAND has LIST of expressions to be evaluated and from among them one value to be assigned to the given state variable.")
(comment cblAssignTo "(cblAssignTo ASSIGN-COMMAND STATE-OBJECT) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASSIGN-COMMAND assigns a value to STATE-OBJECT.")
(comment cblInitializeStateVariableWithExpression "(cblInitializeStateVariableWithExpression STATE-VARIABLE EXPRESSION) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage STATE-VARIABLE is initialized with the evaluated EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblAssignFromAmongExpressionsGivenStateVariables "(cblAssignFromAmongExpressionsGivenStateVariables ASSIGN-FROM-AMONG-COMMAND LIST) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASSIGN-FROM-AMONG-COMMAND assigns a value from a given list of expressions, to the given state variable, within the relevancy context provide by the LIST of state variables.")
(comment CBLRewardSpecification "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage reward specifications.")
(comment cblRewardWhenConditon "(cblRewardWhenConditon REWARD-SPECIFICATION EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage REWARD-SPECIFICATION has EXPRESSION as its Boolean reward condition.")
(comment cblRewardAmount "(cblRewardWhenConditon REWARD-SPECIFICATION EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage REWARD-SPECIFICATION has EXPRESSION as its real-number reward amount.")
(comment cblRewards "(cblRewards WITH-LEARNING-COMMAND LIST) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage WITH-LEARNING-COMMAND allocates rewards as specified in LIST.")
(comment cblSendMessageNamed "(cblSendMessageNamed SEND-COMMAND PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage SEND-COMMAND sends the message identified by PROGRAM-IDENTIFIER.")
(comment cblSendTo "(cblSendTo SEND-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage SEND-COMMAND sends its message to the self, parent or child node identified by evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment NewsArticleNamedFn "'(#$NewsArticleNamedFn NEWS-AGENCY DATE STRING)' denotes the news document that was published or written by NEWS-AGENCY on DATE with STRING as the title or headline.  For example, (#$NewsArticleNamedFn #$ReutersPressAgency (#$DayFn 24 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 2004))) \"Colombia Kidnap Victims Pleas for Freedom, Dialogue\") is the article released by Reuters on January 24th 2004 with the headline \"Colombia Kidnap Victims Pleas for Freedom, Dialogue\".")
(comment nthWordInNLParagraph "(#$nthWordInNLParagraph PARAGRAPH NUM STRING) holds just in case STRING is the NUMth word in PARAGRAPH.  Hyphenated words or words connected by a slash are considered one word for purposes of counting.")
(comment NthWordInNLParagraphFn "'(#$NthWordInNLParagraphFn PARAGRAPH NUM)' denotes the NUMth word of PARAGRAPH.  This is the function corresponding to #$nthWordInNLParagraph.")
(comment nLDocumentLocatedAt "(#$nLDocumentLocatedAt DOCUMENT IDSTRING) holds just in case the abstract document can be located at IDSTRING.  Most often IDSTRING will be a URL or a location within a particular file directory.")
(comment inferenceReliesOnInfoStructure "(#$inferenceReliesOnInfoStructure TEST-QUERY INFO) holds just in case the query TEST-QUERY requires the information provided by INFO.  INFO will usually be denoted by #$DocumentSentenceFn which specifies a particular sentence in a particular #$NLDocument.  This can also relate a query to a particular word or paragraph in a document or, in the most general case, to the document itself. ")
(comment infoUnderstoodByReferenceToInfo "(#$infoUnderstoodByReferenceToInfo INFO-1 STRING-A INFO-2 STRING-B) holds just in case the phrase denoted by STRING-A in INFO-1 can be or is likely to be understood by reference to the phrase denoted by STRING-B in INFO-2 within the context of some #$NLDocument.  INFO-1 will most often be denoted by an #$NLSentence denoting function which specifies the document in which the sentence occurs and STRING-A occurs as a part of the sentence.  Likewise for INFO-2 and STRING-B.")
(comment BiologicalQuantity "The collection of particular degrees of biological quantities.  Instances of this collection represent particular degrees of properties that are either had by or relate to biological organisms.  For example, Quantity-Mutagenicity is the degree to which something is prone to cause cellular mutation.")
(comment inferenceReliesOnStringInInfoStructure "(#$inferenceReliesOnInfoStructure TEST-QUERY INFO STRING) holds just in case the
query TEST-QUERY requires the information provided by the text string STRING which is a part of INFO.  INFO will usually be denoted by #$DocumentSentenceFn which specifies a particular sentence in a particular #$NLDocument. ")
(comment Replying "A specialization of #$Acknowledging-CommunicationAct.  Each instance of #$Replying is a communication act done in response to another such act.  Typically, the earlier communication act will have been directed to the replier (though this need not be the case), and the reply is directed to the performer of that earlier act.  The content of a #$Replying must be such that it (i) acknowledges (at least tacitly) receipt of the earlier communication and (ii) addresses (in some way or other) the content of the earlier communication.
<p>
#$Replyings occur in a wide variety of situations.  For one thing, a reply
can be given in response to most any type of speech act.   Obviously, one can reply to a question (see the specialization #$ReplyingToAQuestion).  One can also reply to a command (say by agreeing or refusing to follow it), an assertion (say by expressing agreement with it, questioning it, or just saying \"Hmmm\"), or an exclamation (say by expressing sympathy for the exclaimer).   Furthermore, a #$Replying and the act it replies to need not be confined to a single conversation or discourse in the usual sense.  One can reply by telephone to an invitation sent in the mail or to a classified ad placed in a newspaper.  One can reply to a letter by sending another letter.  A touchy film director might reply to a negative review in the Times via a Letter to the Editor.
<p>
See also #$inReplyTo, which relates a #$Replying to the communication act(s) to which it replies.")
(comment inReplyTo "A specialization of #$acknowledgedAct (q.v.) that relates an act of #$Replying to the communication act(s) that it is replying to.  (#$inReplyTo REPLY COMM) means that REPLY is performed in response to COMM, and that the latter is acknowledged and its content (in some way) addressed in REPLY.  The respective senders (see #$senderOfInfo) of REPLY and COMM are assumed to be distinct: one cannot reply to one's own message.  See the comment on #$Replying for more details.")
(comment GeneralCycKBIntegrityTest "This is the collection of KB integrity test specifications that are general tests of the Cyc KB; that is, these test specifications are not exclusive to one particular project or application.")
(comment ConversionToTemporalQualification-TestSpecification "The collection of all query specifications to test the davidsonian-to-nondavidsonian conversion framework.")
(comment AnimalLiberationBeliefs "The class of #$BeliefSystems which hold that it is morally wrong for humans to use #$NonHumanAnimals for food, transportation, entertainment, etc.  Some people having #$AnimalLiberationBeliefs are willing to engage in direct, even violent, action to liberate nonhuman animals from (what is perceived as) human oppression.")
(comment irExpansionSet-RequiredRelations-Coarse "An instance of #$IRExpansionPredicate. (#$irExpansionSet-RequiredRelations-Coarse COL LISTS) identifies LISTS as the set of binary lists of the form (#$TheList BIN-RELN TYPE) or (#$TheList TYPE BIN-RELN), where BIN-RELN is a relation that _any_ instance of COL is known to be in with respect to some instance of TYPE. More precisely, a binary list (#$TheList BIN-RELN TYPE) belongs to  LISTS iff Cyc knows that (#$relationAllExists BIN-RELN COL TYPE); symmetrically, a binary list of the form (#$TheList TYPE BIN-RELN) belongs to LISTS iff Cyc knows that  (#$relationExistsAll BIN-RELN TYPE COL)).")
(comment orderingType "(#$orderingType ORDERING SET-OR-COLLECTION) says that ORDERING is an ordering of the elements of SET-OR-COLLECTION.")
(comment defaultDefiningMtForSentence "This is currently a stub predicate intended to be used for determining where a particular CycL sentence should be asserted.")
(comment CBLCurrentFriendshipCampaign "This is the collection of CycBehaviorEngine current friendship campaigns.  Each campaign is a 100 day effort to behave in a friendly fashion.")
(comment TheCurrentKBNumber "#$TheCurrentKBNumber is an #$IndexicalConcept which refers to the current Cyc KB number.")
(comment TheCurrentSystemNumber "#$TheCurrentSystemNumber is an indexical concept which refers to the current Cyc executable system number.")
(comment TheCurrentHostName "#$TheCurrentHostName is an #$IndexicalConcept which refers to the hostname of the computer on which the current Cyc process is running.")
(comment CBLCurrentCycServerHost "This is the collection of #$ComputerServers that host #$Cyc under the control of the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment irExpansionSentencesFromRequiredRelations-Instance "An instance of #$IRExpansionPredicate. (#$irExpansionSentencesFromRequiredRelations-Instance INST COL SENT) identifies SENT as a possible expansion to suggest for the #$Individual INST insofar as INST is an instance of COL. *ongoing*.")
(comment wordIndexesCycTerm "(#$wordIndexesCycTerm WORD TERM) means that TERM is one the #$CycLReifiedDenotationalTerms (or \"forts\") that have been indexed under the string WORD in an externally maintained information retrieval engine.
<p>
For example, (#$wordIndexesCycTerm \"pooch\" #$Dog) is true if in response to query \"pooch\" the targeted information retrieval engine returns among others the term #$Dog.  Because Cyc could be targeting different IR engines, the truth value of a #$wordIndexesCycTerm GAF is dependent on a particular microtheory (different microtheories being used to establish which IR engine is targeted).")
(comment meetsSomeGenlsConstraintOfTopicType "(#$meetsSomeGenlsConstraintOfTopicType TERM TOPIC-TYPE) means that TERM meets at least one of the #$genls constraints imposed by TOPIC-TYPE.")
(comment ProChoiceIdeology "An instance of #$PoliticalBeliefSystem.  One who has #$ProLifeIdeology as a #$BeliefSystem holds that at least some intentional abortions (see #$Abortion-Intentional) ought to be a #$LegalAction.")
(comment CBLAbstractNode "This is the collection of #$CBLNodes that cannot be instantiated.")
(comment CBLStateObject "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage terms that can hold state (be assigned a value) of a certain type.")
(comment cblAssignableType "(cblAssignableType PARAMETER-OR-VARIABLE TYPE) means that instances of PARAMETER-OR-VARIABLE can be assigned objects that are instances of TYPE.")
(comment cblAssignableElementType "(cblElementAssignableType PARAMETER-OR-VARIABLE TYPE) means that instances of PARAMETER-OR-VARIABLE are lists whose elements can be assigned objects that are instances of TYPE.")
(comment CBLMutableStateObject "This is the collection of #$CBLStateObject that can be assigned a new value after they have been initialized.  See also #$CBLImmutableStateObject.")
(comment CBLImmutableStateObject "This is the collection of #$CBLStateObject that cannot be assigned a new value after they have been initialized.  See also #$CBLMutableStateObject.")
(comment CBLValueObjectIsMutableStateObject "This is the collection of #$CBLObjectHavingType that is of type list, and whose elements can be assigned a new value after they have been initialized.  See also #$CBLImmutableStateObject.")
(comment CBLSharedStateObject "This is the collection of #$CBLStateObject that can be safely shared among #$CycBehaviorEngine process threads.  See also #$CBLUnsharedStateObject.")
(comment CBLUnsharedStateObject "This is the collection of #$CBLObjectHavingType that cannot be safely shared among #$CycBehaviorEngine process threads.  See also #$CBLSharedStateObject.")
(comment cblMaximumMethodDuration "(cblMaximumMethodDuration CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS EXPRESSION) means that all methods defined in CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS will throw a timeout exception after the duration that results from evaluating EXPRESSION, unless it succeeds or fails beforehand.")
(comment CBLApplicabilityMethod "Instances of this collection define a #$CycBehaviorLanguage applicability method.")
(comment cblMethodHasApplicabilityMethod "(cblMethodHasApplicabilityMethod CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-APPLICABILITY-METHOD) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-APPLICABILITY-METHOD.  The #$CycBehaviorEngine executes the applicability method before the given task, sensation, message or exception method to determine whether the primary method is applicable to the given node and input parameter state.")
(comment cblMethodHasUtility "(cblMethodHasUtility CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD NON-NEGATIVE-NUMBER) means that CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-METHOD has the utility NON-NEGATIVE-NUMBER in the interval [0.0 ... 1.0].")
(comment cblMaximumDuration "(cblMaximumDuration METHOD-OR-TASK EXPRESSION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage METHOD-OR-TASK will throw a timeout exception after the duration that results from evaluating EXPRESSION, unless it succeeds or fails beforehand.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingSucceedAny "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands having that succeed if any of the group commands succeed.")
(comment cblGroupSucceed "(cblGroupSucceed GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as its success threshold.")
(comment cblGroupOrderingConstraint "(cblGroupOrderingConstraint GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as a constraint upon the named commands within the GROUP-COMMAND.")
(comment cblGroupCausalLink "(cblGroupCausalLink GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as a causal link among the named commands within the GROUP-COMMAND.")
(comment cblGroupOptimallyAllocate "(cblGroupOptimallyAllocate GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as a time duration resource to be optimally allocated among the commands within the GROUP-COMMAND, given the set of #$CBLStateVariables specifed in the corresponding #$cblGroupGivenStateVariable assertions ")
(comment cblGroupGivenStateObject "(cblGroupOptimallyAllocate GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as a time duration resource to be optimally allocated among the commands within the GROUP-COMMAND, given the set of #$CBLStateVariables specifed in the corresponding #$cblGroupGivenStateVariable assertions ")
(comment cblPrecondition "(cblMethodPrecondition METHOD-OR-CALL MUST-COMMAND) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage METHOD-OR-CALL has MUST-COMMAND as a precondition for execution by the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment cblPostcondition "(cblMethodPostcondition METHOD-OR-CALL MUST-COMMAND) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage METHOD-OR-CALL has MUST-COMMAND as a postcondition that holds after execution of the method or call by the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment cblNodeInvariantCondition "(cblNodeInvariant NODE-CLASS EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage NODE-CLASS has EXPRESSION as an invariant condition that holds before and after the execution of any node method by the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment CBLNodeAddress "Instances of this collection define unique #$CycBehaviorLanguage node addresses that identify the position of nodes with respect to their parent node hierarchy.")
(comment CBLBuiltInStateVariable "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables.")
(comment CBLLog "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage log command events.")
(comment CBLLogHavingSevereLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands for which the logging level is severe.")
(comment CBLLogHavingWarningLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the warning logging level.")
(comment CBLLogHavingInfoLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the info logging level.")
(comment CBLLogHavingFineLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the fine logging level.")
(comment CBLLogHavingFinerLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the finer logging level.")
(comment CBLLogHavingFinestLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the finest logging level.")
(comment CBLLogHavingConfigLevel "This is the collection of #$CBLLog commands having the config logging level.")
(comment cblLogExpression "(cblLogExpression LOG-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage LOG-COMMAND has EXPRESSION to be evaluated and logged.")
(comment CBLStartChildNode "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage start-child-node command events.")
(comment cblStartChildNodeExpression "(cblStartChildNodeClassExpression START-CHILD-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage START-COMMAND starts a new child node that is an instantiation of the #$CBLNode obtained by evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment cblStartChildNodeNamed "(cblStartChildNodeNamed START-CHILD-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage START-CHILD-COMMAND starts a new child node with the given EXPRESSION name.")
(comment CBLStartChildNodeHavingBuiltIn "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage start-child-node command events, in which the started child node is built-in as opposed to defined.")
(comment CBLObjectHavingMaximumDuration "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage terms that can have a maximum duration.")
(comment CBLStopChildNode "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage stop-child-node command events.")
(comment cblStopChildNodeNamed "(cblStopChildNodeNamed STOP-CHILD-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage STOP-CHILD-COMMAND stops the child node with the given EXPRESSION name.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingTypecast "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands having the typcast effect during assignment of the value expression to the #$CBLStateObject.")
(comment CBLComment "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage comment command events.")
(comment CBLBuiltIn_DefaultCycAccess "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables that hold an instance of the java CycAccess object.")
(comment CBLBuiltIn_DefaultBehaviorAPIWidgets "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables that hold an instance of the java BehaviorAPIWidgets object.")
(comment cblMustExpression "(cblMustExpression MUST-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage MUST-COMMAND has EXPRESSION that must evaluate to #$True.")
(comment cblMustReason "(cblMustReason MUST-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that if #$CycBehaviorLanguage MUST-COMMAND throws an assertin error, then EXPRESSION is evaluated as the reason.")
(comment CBLSleep "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage sleep command events.")
(comment cblSleepDuration "(cblSleepDuration SLEEP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage SLEEP-COMMAND have its execution suspended by the #$CycBehaviorEngine for the time duration resulting from evaluating EXPRESSION.")
(comment taxonomicSiblingCollections "An instance of both #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections and #$KBDependentRelation. (#$taxonomicSiblingCollections COL1 COL2) means that COL1 and COL2 are siblings with respect to the subsumption relation (#$genls in Cyc), i.e., that they both are direct specializations of a common subsuming collection. More accurately: there exists a collection SUPER such that both (#$nearestGenls COL1 SUPER) and (#$nearestGenls COL2 SUPER).
<p>
This predicate expresses a property of collections as they are defined in a hierarchical classification or taxonomy: it is a KB-dependent property in that its extension is determined by the state of the KB (more precisely, of its subsumption hierarchy) at any given moment. For this reason too, it is a #$notAssertible predicate. Note that because \"the nearest generalization\" is not unique for a given term in the Cyc taxonomy, #$taxonomicSiblingCollections is not a transitive relation.")
(comment defaultDefiningMtForBinaryPredicateOnType "(#$defaultDefiningMtForBinaryPredicateOnType BIN-PRED COL MT) means that, by default, assertions asserting (BIN-PRED INS VALUE) where (isa INS COL) should go in MT.")
(comment CBLBuiltIn_Username "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables that hold an instance of the username object.")
(comment CBLInitial "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage initial command events.")
(comment CBLFinal "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage final command events.")
(comment cblSharedStateVariable "(cblSharedStateVariable NODE-CLASS CLASS-STATE-VARIABLE) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage NODE-CLASS has CLASS-STATE-VARIABLE as one of its shared state variables.")
(comment cblDefiningContextForNode "(cblDefiningContextForNode MT CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE) means that MT contains the #$CycBehaviorLanguage sentences that define the CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE.")
(comment cblNodeHasUtilityMethod "(cblNodeHasUtilityMethod NODE-CLASS UTILITY-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the UTILITY-METHOD as a method to determine the utility of task, sensation and message methods in the node.")
(comment cblNodeHasCriticMethod "(cblNodeHasMessageMethod NODE-CLASS UTILITY-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the UTILITY-METHOD as a method to determine the utility of task, sensation and message methods in the node.")
(comment CBLBuiltIn_DefaultCycHostname "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables that hold an instance of the default Cyc hostname object.")
(comment CBLBuiltIn_DefaultCycBasePort "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage built-in state variables that hold an instance of the default Cyc base TCP port object.")
(comment trueSentence-CaseInsensitive "(#$trueSentence-CaseInsensitive SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is true, modulo case.")
(comment IntelligenceAnalysisTaskTemplates-Basic "This is a specialization of IntelligenceAnalysisTask-TemplateTopic.  #$FormulaTemplates of this tyoe collect data about specific intelligence analysis tasks.")
(comment IntelligenceAnalyst-TemplateTopic "This is a template topic type for describing indivudal #$IntelligenceAnalysts and their task assignments.")
(comment IntelligenceAnalystTemplates-TaskAssignments "This is a specialization of IntelligenceAnalyst-TemplateTopic.  #$FormulaTemplates of this tyoe collect data about an indivudal #$IntelligenceAnalyst's task assignments.")
(comment IntelligenceAnalystTemplates-Basic "This is a specialization of IntelligenceAnalyst-TemplateTopic.  #$FormulaTemplates of this tyoe collec basic background data about indivudal #$IntelligenceAnalysts.")
(comment Agronomy "#$Agronomy is the application of science to agricultural concerns such as crop production and soil management.")
(comment cblNodeHasApplicabilityMethod "(cblNodeHasApplicabilityMethod NODE-CLASS APPLICABILITY-METHOD) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage nodes defined from CYC-BEHAVIOR-LANGUAGE-NODE-CLASS have the APPLICABILITY-METHOD as a method to determine the applicability of task, sensation and message methods in the node.")
(comment CBLGroupHavingIfCondition "This is the collection of #$CBLGroup comands having an associated if-condition.")
(comment CBLGroupHavingElse "This is the collection of #$CBLGroup comands having an associated instance of #$CBLGroupHavingIfCondition.")
(comment IntelligenceAnalysisAssess-TemplateTopic "This is a template topic type for evaluating sources of information.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingOrderedSubtasks "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands for which the #$CycBehaviorEngine will execute subtasks in their sequential order.")
(comment cblIfCondition "(cblIfCondition GROUP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage GROUP-COMMAND has EXPRESSION as its Boolean condition.")
(comment CBLCommandHavingStateVariableDefinition "This is the collection of #$CBLCommands that define the #$CBLStateVariable that receives the command value.")
(comment cblCommentString "(cblCommentString COMMENT-COMMAND STRING) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMENT-COMMAND has STRING as the comment.")
(comment ExpertSource-TemplateTopic "This is a template topic type for evaluating individual experts.")
(comment ExpertSourceTemplates-Basic "This is a specialization of #$ExpertSource-TemplateTopic.  #$FormulaTemplates of this type of collection consists of basic background data about individual experts.")
(comment cblCommandDefinesVariable "(cblCommandDefinesVariable COMMAND METHOD-STATE-VARIABLE) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMAND defines the output METHOD-STATE-VARIABLE.")
(comment NonIKBConstant "Membership of a constant in this collection overrides its being a #$IKBConstant, so that it isn't included in IKB builds.")
(comment cblMethodOrderingConstraint "(cblMethodOrderingConstraint NODE-CLASS EXPRESSION) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage NODE-CLASS has EXPRESSION as an method ordering constraint during the execution of any node method by the #$CycBehaviorEngine.")
(comment unsatisfactoryActType "(#$unsatisfactoryActType ACT-TYPE ATTEMPT-TYPE) holds just in case ATTEMPT-TYPE is the collection of attempts to do acts of type ACT-TYPE, but each instance is unsatisfactory to its performer in the sense that at least one of the main goals the performer had in performing the act was not achieved.  This is the corresponding predicate to the function #$UnsatisfactoryAttemptToFn.  For a fuller explanation of this notion please see the comment on #$UnsatisfactoryAttemptToFn.")
(comment CBLNodeStateVariable "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage node class state variables.")
(comment CBLMethodStateVariable "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage method state variables.")
(comment PredicateNamedFn "(#$PredicateNamedFn STRING PREDICATE-TYPE) denotes the instance of PREDICATE-TYPE that is named by STRING.")
(comment TranscriptSource-TemplateTopic "This is a template topic type for describing and evaluating transcripts of speeches, interviews, or any other speech event.")
(disjointWith Vegetarian Cannibal)
(disjointWith ZeroDimensionalUnitOfMeasure (CollectionDifferenceFn UnitOfMeasure ZeroDimensionalUnitOfMeasure))
(comment roleWithEventTypeEntailsSomeTimeInTimeIndex "<code>(#$roleWithEventTypeEntailsSomeTimeInTimeIndex ROLE-PRED SIT-TYPE)</code> holds just in case some present tense progressive version of ROLE-PRED holds sometime in the time period picked out by the #$startingDate and #$endingDate of any instance of SIT-TYPE.  For example
<p>
(#$roleWithEventTypeEntailsSomeTimeInTimeIndex #$meetingParticipants #$Meeting-SocialGathering)
<p>
holds because we could create a present tense progressive version of #$meetingParticipants (call it 'currentlyAttendingMeeting') and that predicate would hold of the same args as #$meetingParticipants sometime in the time interval picked out by the starting and ending dates of the event in question.  More formally:
<p>
If
<p>
(#$and
(#$meetingParticipants SIT Joe)
(#$isa SIT #$Meeting-SocialGathering)
(#$startingDate SIT T1)
(#$endingDate SIT T2))
<p>
then
<p>
(currentlyAttendingMeeting SIT Joe)
<MT (#$SomeTimeInIntervalFn (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn T1 T2) GUID) #$TimePoint>
<p>
<p>
<p>")
(comment roleWithEventTypeEntailsTimeIndex "<code>(#$roleWithEventTypeEntailsTimeIndex ROLE-PRED SIT-TYPE)</code> holds just in case some present tense progressive version of ROLE-PRED holds in the time period picked out by the #$startingDate and #$endingDate of any instance of SIT-TYPE.  For example
<p>
(#$roleWithEventTypeEntailsSomeTimeInTimeIndex #$containerUsed #$StorageOfSomethingInAContainer)
<p>
holds because we could create a present tense progressive version of #$containerUsed (call it 'currentlyContains') and that predicate would hold of the the container and contained object in the time interval picked out by the starting and ending dates of the event in question.  More formally:
<p>
If
<p>
(#$and
(#$containerUsed SIT CONTAINER)
(#$isa SIT #$StorageOfSomethingInAContainer)
(#$startingDate* SIT T1)
(#$endingDate* SIT T2)
(#$containedObject SIT OBJ)
<p>
then
<p>
(currentlyContains CONTAINER OBJ)
<MT (#$TimeIntervalInclusiveFn T1 T2) #$TimePoint>
<p>
*This particular interpretation requires versions of #$startingDate and #$endingDate that correspond to the starting point and ending point of the situation in question and not just the \"sometime in date\" interpretation they currently employ
<p>
<p>")
(comment roleWithEventTypeAgnosticWRTTimeIndex "<code>(#$roleWithEventTypeAgnosticWRTTimeIndex ROLE-PRED SIT-TYPE)</code> holds just in case the time at which the role player plays the role described by ROLE-PRED in instances of SIT-TYPE is not determined by the starting and ending dates of instances of SIT-TYPE.")
(comment noPossibleAntecedent "This is a #$UnaryPredicate used to flag #$LinguisticExpressionPegs which have no possible antecedents (see #$contextuallyPossibleAntecedent) in the local disourse context.  This can bu used as a rough guide for identifying referents in need of \"bridging\" assertions.")
(comment assignmentResourceRequests "The predicate #$assignmentResourceRequests is used to relate an instance of #$Assignment-Specification to an instance of #$ResourceRequest.  An assertion of the form (#$assignmentResourceRequests ASSIGN REQUEST) is used to express the fact that REQUEST is a preliminary reservation of certain resources for the sake of completing the #$Assignment-Specification ASSIGN, this should be contrasted with the actual #$Allotment (q.v.).")
(comment cblSleepUntil "(cblSleepUntil SLEEP-COMMAND EXPRESSION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage SLEEP-COMMAND have its execution suspended by the #$CycBehaviorEngine until the time interval or event resulting from evaluating the EXPRESSION.")
(comment CityOfEastbourneEngland "An instance of #$City.  The #$CityOfEastbourneEngland is
located in #$EastSussex-CountyEngland.")
(comment cblAskQuerySpecification "(cblAskQuerySpecification ASK-COMMAND QUERY-SPECIFICATION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASK-COMMAND has QUERY-SPECIFICATION as the query.")
(comment cblAskQueryVariable "(cblAskQueryVariable BINDING-SPECICATION EL-VARIABLE) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage BINDING-SPECICATION has EL-VARIABLE as its query variable for which a single query result is bound or for which a list of all query results is bound.")
(comment CBLBindingSpecification "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage binding specifications that relate an #$CBLAsk command with query results bound to a given #$CBLStateObject.")
(comment cblAskBindingSpecification "(cblAskBindingSpecification ASK-COMMAND BINDING-SPECIFICATION) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage ASK-COMMAND has BINDING-SPECIFICATION as one of its binding specifications that relates a query variable with #$CBLStateObject that receives a single query result or a list of query results.")
(comment cblAskBindResultsListTo "(cblAskBindResultsListTo BINDING-SPECICATION STATE-VARIABLE) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage BINDING-SPECICATION has STATE-VARIABLE as its variable to which all the query result bindings are bound as a list.")
(comment cblAskBindResultTo "(cblAskBindResultTo BINDING-SPECICATION STATE-VARIABLE) means that the #$CycBehaviorLanguage BINDING-SPECICATION has STATE-VARIABLE as its variable to which the sinqle query result binding is bound.")
(comment CBLCallSubL "This is the collection of #$CycBehaviorLanguage call-subl command events.")
(comment cblCallSubLFunction "(cblCallSubLFunction CALL-SUBL-COMMAND SUBL-FUNCTION) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage CALL-SUBL-COMMAND calls the SUBL-FUNCTION.")
(comment cblCallSubLPackage "(cblCallSubLPackage CALL-SUBL-COMMAND LISP-PACKAGE) means #$CycBehaviorLanguage CALL-SUBL-COMMAND calls the specified SubL function contained in the LISP-PACKAGE.")
(comment AntiIsraelIdeology "#$AntiIsraelIdeology is a #$PoliticalBeliefSystems associated with agents -- groups, regimes, or individuals -- who have a negative vested interest (see #$negativeVestedInterest) in the state of #$Israel.")
(comment cblHost "(cblHost COMMAND HOST-NAME) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMAND has an associated Cyc image running at the computer named HOST-NAME.")
(comment cblPort "(cblPort COMMAND NETWORK-PORT-NUMBER) means that #$CycBehaviorLanguage COMMAND has an associated Cyc image listening at the NETWORK-PORT-NUMBER.")
(comment TerroristCell "The collection of terrorist cells.  Each instance of this collection is a group of terrorists that is a suborganization of some terrorist group.")
(comment TerroristSupportOrganization "The collection of organizations that provide some sort of support to terrorist organizations.")
(comment schoolTypeAttended "(#$schoolTypeAttended PERSON SCHOOL-TYPE)<MT TIME PAR> holds just in case there is some time earlier than TIME such that in MT to PAR PERSON has attended some instance of SCHOOL-TYPE at that time.")
(comment PersonTypeByChildStatus "A collecion of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of instances of #$Person that have a particular status describing whether they have children.")
(comment Childless-Status "The collection of persons who have no children -- either adopted or by birth.")
(comment HasChildren-Status "The collection of persons who have children -- either adopted or by birth.")
(comment PersonWithCriminalRecord "The collection of persons who have a criminal record.")
(comment PersonWithPoliticalActivismRecord "The collection of persons whose legal record records the fact that they have
been involved in political activism.")
(comment PersonWithCriminalPoliticalActivismRecord "A specialization of #$PersonWithPoliticalActivismRecord and #$PersonWithCriminalRecord.  This is the collection of persons whose records indicate they have been involved in both criminal activity and policial activism.")
(comment PersonWithNoCriminalRecord "The collection of persons who have no criminal record.")
(comment dateJoinedJihad "(#$dateJoinedJihad AGENT DATE) holds just in case DATE was the date that AGENT joined the \"jihad\".  This is a special case predicate designed to facilitate the mapping of the Matrix spreadsheet into the EDB.")
(comment ageOfAgentWhenJoinedJihad "(#$ageOfAgentWhenJoinedJihad AGENT TIME-QUANTITY) hold just in case (#$age AGENT TIME-QUANTITY) held at the time AGENT joined the jihad.")
(comment placeJoinedJihad "(#$placeJoinedJihad AGENT PLACE) holds just in case PLACE was the place where AGENT joined the \"jihad\".  This is a special case predicate designed to facilitate the mapping of the Matrix spreadsheet into the EDB.")
(comment dateLeftJihad "(#$dateLeftJihad AGENT DATE) holds just in case DATE was the date that AGENT left the \"jihad\".  This is a special case predicate designed to facilitate the mapping of the Matrix spreadsheet into the EDB.")
(comment MatrixTerroristAct "The collection of terrorist acts referenced in the MATRIX.xls.  The instances of this collection are acts referenced in the MATRIX.xls for which it is unclear exactly what act is being referred to.  For example, row 103 column E in the key for the spreadsheet simply says \"Training\".  Our best guess is that that refers to the temporally discontinuous event of Al Qaida training its operatives.  So, a event called \"#$TrainingOfAlQaidaOperatives\" was created and made an instance of this collection. ")
(comment termNeedsBetterLexification "(#$termNeedsBetterLexification TERM) states that TERM is poorly lexified and that its lexification should be improved.")
(comment TeaRoomSpace "The collection of buildings that house instances of #$TeaRoom-Organization.")
(comment TeaRoom-Organization "This is the collection of restaurants which primarily serve tea and other beverages, sometimes supplemented with pastries and other desserts.")
(comment WhabbistMuslimPerson "An instance of #$PersonTypeByReligion.  Each instance of this collection is a member of the Whabbist sect of Islam.")
(comment isLeaderOf "(#$isLeaderOf PERSON1 PERSON2) holds just in case PERSON1 and PERSON2 are members of the same organization, ORG, and (#$hasLeaders ORG PERSON1) and (usually) (#$not (#$hasLeaders ORG PERSON2)) holds.")
(comment hasReligiousLeaders "(#$hasReligiousLeaders AGT PERSON) holds just in case PERSON is a spiritual/religious leader of AGT.")
(comment religiousLeaderOf "(#$religiousLeaderOf PERSON AGT) holds just in case PERSON is the spiritual/religious leader of AGT.")
(comment PersonTypeByReligiousBackground "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of individuals with a particular religious background.")
(comment CycBehaviorLanguageDefinitionSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle which collects microtheories containing #$CycBehaviorLanguage node and method definitions.")
(comment CycBehaviorLanguageActionHistorySpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle which collects microtheories containing #$CycBehaviorEngine action histories.")
(comment cblNodeRunningDefinition "(cblNodeRunningDefinition NODE-RUNNING NODE) means that the #$CycBehaviorEngine program running is defined by #$CBLNode NODE.")
(comment cblNodeRunningParent "(cblNodeRunningParent NODE-RUNNING PARENT-NODE-RUNNING) means that the #$CycBehaviorEngineNodeRunning NODE-RUNNING has PARENT-NODE-RUNNING as its parent.")
(comment cblNodeRunningName "(cblNodeRunningName NODE-RUNNING NAME) means that the #$CycBehaviorEngineNodeRunning NODE-RUNNING has NAME as its identifying name.")
(comment cblNodeRunningAddress "(cblNodeRunningName NODE-RUNNING ADDRESS) means that the #$CycBehaviorEngineNodeRunning NODE-RUNNING has ADDRESS as its fully qualified identifying address.")
(comment cblNodeRunningActionHistory "(cblNodeRunningActionHistory NODE-RUNNING ACTION-HISTORY) means that the #$CycBehaviorEngineNodeRunning NODE-RUNNING has ACTION-HISTORY as its microtheory in which the record of actions taken are stored.")
