(comment Disestablishmentarianism "A #$PoliticalBeliefSystem according to which the unification of church and state should be disestablished.  This #$BeliefSystem presupposes, of course, a unification of church and state.")
(comment ChacoRegion-SouthAmerica "A large geographical region in South America.  It is part of the La Plata basin.  It includes parts of Bolivia, Argentina, and Paraguay.  It also includes the largest forested area in Latin America after the Amazon basin.    ")
(comment Secularism-Political "A belief system that seeks to minimize the influence of religion and religious institutions on the public institutions and activities of a society.")
(comment ArabSocialism "A hybrid political system that combines #$PanArabism with #$Socialism. Historically, this is the offical ideology of the  #$BaathArabSocialistParty and its articulation is largely attributed to #$MichelAflag.")
(comment PatriarchOfAntioch "This collection designates one of the principal leaders of the #$MaroniteChurch.")
(comment LinkParser "A parser for English developed at #$CarnegieMellonUniversity by Davy Temperley, Daniel Sleator and John Lafferty.<br> #$LinkParser is a syntactic parser of English, based on link grammar, an original theory of English syntax. Given a sentence, the system assigns to it a syntactic structure, which consists of a set of labeled links connecting pairs of words. The parser also produces a <i>constituent</i> representation of a sentence (showing noun phrases, verb phrases, etc.).")
(comment PanArabism "A belief system aimed at the unification of #$EthnicGroupOfArabs, possibly in the form of a single country.  It is largely characterized by a desire to end Western influence in the Middle East and by a hostility toward the state of #$Israel.  It should be differentiated with #$IslamicNationalistIdeology, since #$PanArabism is characterized by its relation to #$Secularism-Political and #$Socialism, but it is very similar to #$ArabNationalism, except that Arab Nationalists are not characterized by their desire for a single state.")
