(comment GeodeticCoordinateSystem "A polar coordinate system centered on the center of the earth, and in terms of which locations of things can be expressed using the two predicates #$latitude and #$longitude (respectively, the #$altitudeAnglePredicate and the #$azimuthAnglePredicate of the #$GeodeticCoordinateSystem).  The latitude of the #$EarthsEquator is 0 degrees; the latitude of the #$AxialNorthPoleOfEarth is 90 degrees; and the longitude of the #$PrimeMeridian-Greenwich is 0 degrees.  (These assertions 'pin down' the orientation of the earth with respect to the #$GeodeticCoordinateSystem.)  See also #$PolarCoordinateSystem, #$latitude and #$longitude.")
