(comment capabilityToRoleSitType "A ternary predicate.  (#$capabilityToRoleSitType ROLE SIT-TYPE CAP) holds just in case CAP is the instance of #$Capability that is the capability to play ROLE in instances of SIT-TYPE.  The is the corresponding predicate to #$CapabilityFn.")
(comment CapabilityFn "A binary function.  This function takes a specialization of #$Situation and an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate and returns the instance of #$Capability, CAP, such that anyone, AGT, for which the following is true (#$behaviorCapable AGT SIT-TYPE ROLE) has that capability (#$hasCapability-Atomic AGT CAP).")
(comment NonNumericScalarQuantity "A specialization of #$ScalarQuantity and #$ScalarProperInterval (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$NonNumericScalarQuantity is a properly interval-like quantity that is not given in terms of a numerically-specified measurement (cf. #$MeasurableQuantity).  Typically, a non-numeric quantity is specified in a way that compares it to certain other non-numeric quantities of the same general type.  For example,  #$BreadboxSized is a non-numeric #$Volume that is less than (see #$followingValue) the volume #$HumanSized.
<p>
Note that no #$MathematicalFunctionOnScalars (e.g. #$PlusFn, #$ScalarExponentFn) is defined (see #$undefined) on any non-numeric scalar quantity.
<p>
An important specialization of #$NonNumericScalarQuantity is #$GenericQuantity.
<p>
For predicates that relate things to non-numeric quantities that characterize them, see #$NonNumericQuantitySlot.")
