(comment ConceptFilterSpecificationFn "(#$ConceptFilterSpecificationFn CONCEPT-FILTER MODE TRIGGER) denotes the instance of #$ConceptFilterSpecification in which CONCEPT-FILTER is used in the following way: MODE tells the application what sort of terms from the filter to display -- e.g that it should display only terms in the filter or that it should display terms from the filter and any instances it finds (See #$ConceptOnlyFilterParameter and #$ConceptAndInstancesFilterParameter).  TRIGGER states the condition under which a term or its instance would be displayed (or mapped).  There are four conditions.  1. The concept itself must be present in the corpus being parsed (see #$TriggerFromConcept), 2. The concept or one of its specs must be present in the corpus being parsed (see #$TriggerFromConceptOrSpec), 3. the concept or one of its instances must be present in the corpus being parsed (#$TriggerFromConceptOrInstance), 4. the concept, its instances or specs must be present --the union of conditions 2 and 3 (see #$TriggerFromConceptSpecOrInstance).")
(comment CompanyWithStockTickerSymbolFn "(CompanyWithStockTickerSymbonFn XXX) returns the publicly-held corporation whose ticker symbol (on some exchange) is XXX.")
