(comment OfficeCodeOfConduct "General principles of appropriate behavior in a modern Western-style business office.  Applies only during working hours at the place of business.")
(comment adjustedEPSForPeriod "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation. (#$adjustedEPS ORG MONEY TIME) means MONEY is the amount that would be earned (i.e. profit) by ORG per share of stock during the time interval that is subsumed by TIME, if all amortization and exceptional costs to ORG were added back to ORG's profits. This value is called \"adjusted EPS\" or \"headline EPS\" (because it is often the EPS reported by companies). The exact nature of the adjustments made varies from company to company.  See also #$adjustedEarningsPerShare-ForStockType.")
(comment adjustedEPS "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation. (#$adjustedEPS ORG MONEY)<T> means MONEY is the amount that would be earned (i.e. profit) by ORG per share of stock during the time interval T but not necessarily any sub-interval of T, if all amortization and exceptional costs to ORG were added back to ORG's profits. This value is called \"adjusted EPS\" or \"headline EPS\" (because it is often the EPS reported by companies). The exact nature of the adjustments made varies from company to company.  See also #$adjustedEarningsPerShare-ForStockType.")
(comment dilutedEPSForPeriod "(#$dilutedEPSForPeriod ORG MONEY TIME) means MONEY is the amount earned (i.e. profit) by ORG during TIME per share of stock.  This is calculated using the diluted number of shares in ORG, which may be higher than the actual number of shares outstanding.  The diluted number of shares includes the number of shares that are 'spoken for', through means such as options or warrants to buy stock.")
(comment revenueForPeriod "(#$revenueForPeriod ORG MONEY TIME) relates the amount of MONEY booked as revenue by ORG during the time period DATE.  DATE will typically be a fiscal quarter or year, but could be some other sort of conventionally defined #$Date.")
(comment dilutedEPSForPeriodByAccountingCOC "(#$dilutedEPSForPeriodByAccountingCOC ORG MONEY TIME COC) means MONEY is the amount earned (i.e. profit) by ORG during TIME per share of stock according to the calculation techniques allowed by the #$AccountingCOC COC.  This is calculated using the diluted number of shares in ORG, which may be higher than the actual number of shares outstanding.  The diluted number of shares includes the number of shares that are 'spoken for', through means such as options or warrants to buy stock.")
(comment adjustedEPSForPeriodByAccountingCOC "(#$adjustedEPSForPeriodByAccountingCOC ORG MONEY TIME COC) means MONEY is the amount that would be earned (i.e. profit) by ORG per share of stock during the time interval that is subsumed by TIME according to the calculation techniques allowed by the #$AccountingCOC COC, if all amortization and exceptional costs to ORG were added back to ORG's profits. This value is called \"adjusted EPS\" or \"headline EPS\" (because it is often the EPS reported by companies). The exact nature of the adjustments made varies from company to company.  See also #$adjustedEarningsPerShare-ForStockType.")
