(comment ObjectTypeBySensibleFeature "A collection of collections.  Each specialization of this collection is a collection of collections of objects characterized by some sensible feature.  For example, #$ObjectTypeByTaste is the collection of collections of objects characterized by their taste.  It includes the collection of salty things, sweet things, etc.  ")
(disjointWith Hot-SpicyFood NoTaste)
(comment Dialetheism "An instance of #$PhilosophyBeliefs.  #$Dialetheism is the view that there are, or at least could be, true contradictions.  According to #$Dialetheism, there is, or could be, some #$Proposition PROP such that both PROP and (#$not PROP) are true.")
(comment TheFuture-Generic "An indexical term that can be used to denote some indeterminate chunk of time that starts after the time of the context.  For example, to represent the statement \"in the future dogs will talk\" we could assert:

<pre>
   (#$ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn CURRENT-TIME))
    (#$holdsIn #$TheFuture-Generic((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Dog #$Talking #$performedBy)))</pre>

The above could be given a minimal interpretation in any microtheory like the following

<pre>
(ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn CURRENT-TIME))
       (#$thereExists ?FUTURE-INTERVAL
        (#$and
          (#$startsAfterEndingOf ?FUTURE-INTERVAL CURRENT-TIME)
          (#$isa ?FUTURE-INTERVAL #$TimeInterval)
          (#$ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn ?FUTURE-TIME))
            ((#$TypeCapableFn #$behaviorCapable) #$Dog #$Talking #$performedBy))))
            


 
")
(comment ThePast-Generic "An indexical term that can be used to denote some indeterminate chunk of time that ends before the time of the context.  For example, to represent the statement \"in the future dogs can't talk\" we could assert:

<pre>
   (#$ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn CURRENT-TIME))
    (#$holdsIn #$ThePast-Generic(#$typeBehaviorIncapable #$Dog #$Talking #$performedBy)))</pre>

The above could be given a minimal interpretation in any microtheory like the following

<pre>
(ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn CURRENT-TIME))
       (#$thereExists ?INTERVAL
        (#$and
          (#$startsAfterEndingOf CURRENT-TIME ?INTERVAL)
          (#$isa ?INTERVAL #$TimeInterval)
          (#$ist (#$MtSpace CURRENT-MONAD (#$MtTimeDimFn ?INTERVAL))
            (#$typeBehaviorIncapable #$Dog #$Talking #$performedBy))))
            


 
")
(comment AnimalTypeByPhysiologicalFeature "A collection of collections.  The broadest collection of features of #$Animals that describe the physiological aspects of an animal, including its physiological (1) capacities, (2) conditions, and (3) states.  Examples include: (1) Capacities: #$FertileAnimal, #$HearingImpairedAnimal, #$Paraplegic; (2) Conditions: #$Anemic, #$AthleticPhysicalBuild; (3) States: #$Intoxicated, #$Injured, #$Inflamed.  Instances of #$PlantTypeByPhysiology, such as #$InBloom, are excluded.")
(comment highAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$HighAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$highAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$highAmountOf #$Happiness (#$HighAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$highAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a high degree.")
(comment veryLowToLowAmountOf "<code>(#$veryLowToLowAmountOf QUANT-TYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the quantity that corresponds to a <i>low to very low</i> quantity of <code>QUANT-TYPE</code>.")
(comment veryLowAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$VeryLowAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$veryLowAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>very low amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$veryLowAmountOf #$Happiness (#$VeryLowAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$veryLowAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a very low degree.")
(comment lowAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$LowAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$lowAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>low amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$lowAmountOf #$Happiness (#$LowAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds. And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$lowAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a low degree.")
(comment mediumToVeryHighAmountOf "The instance of #$GenericValuePredicate (q.v.) that corresponds to (see #$correspondingGenericValuePredicate) the generic-value function #$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn (q.v.).  <code>(#$mediumToVeryHighAmountOf QUANTTYPE QUANTITY)</code> holds just in case <code>QUANTITY</code> is the #$GenericQuantity that corresponds to a <i>medium-to-very-high amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code>.
<p>
For example, <code>(#$mediumToVeryHighAmountOf #$Happiness (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Happiness))</code> holds.  And <code>(#$levelOfCompatibility OLDTHING NEWTHING #$mediumToVeryHighAmountOf)</code> holds just in case <code>OLDTHING</code> and <code>NEWTHING</code> are compatible to a medium-to-very-high degree.")
(disjointWith TerroristCoordinatedMultipleBombAttackOnCivilians (UnsuccessfulAttemptToFn TerroristCoordinatedMultipleBombAttackOnCivilians))
(disjointWith SomethingExisting NLQuantAttribute)
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntity (CollectionDifferenceFn Organization GeopoliticalEntity))
(disjointWith Organization-NonGeopoliticalEntity GeopoliticalEntity)
(disjointWith Organization-NonGeopoliticalEntity GeopoliticalEntityOrRegion)
(disjointWith Organization (CollectionDifferenceFn SomethingExisting Organization))
(comment conceptTaggingIrrelevantTerm "(#$conceptTaggingIrrelevantTerm X) is true for those concepts X that should, by default, not be returned for any string when tagging a string with Cyc concepts.  For example, it makes little sense to return a term like (#$InstanceNamedFn \"Fred\" #$Thing) when performing concept-tagging for the purpose of document indexing.")
(comment easilyUnderstoodByHumans "(#$easilyUnderstoodByHumans X) is true for those concepts X that one would expect an average person to recognize and understand.   For example, the concepts #$arg1Isa is not easily understandable by humans.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntityOrRegion (CollectionDifferenceFn PartiallyTangible GeopoliticalEntityOrRegion))
(comment SortSetViaBinPredFn "#$SortSetViaBinPredFn is a binary list denoting function that takes a set in arg1, any binary relation and returns the list that is the result of pairwise comparing each element in arg1 and sorting the list according to the results of the comparison.  For example, (#$SortSetViaBinPredFn (#$TheSet 3 1 6) #$greaterThan) returns (TheList 6 3 1).")
(comment CAEAnalysisTopic "The collection of #$Topics that have special support for fact entry in the #$CycAnalyticEnvironment-TheProgram.")
(disjointWith TerroristAttack (UnsuccessfulAttemptToFn TerroristAttack))
(disjointWith UnitedStatesCodeTitle (FormerFn UnitedStatesCodeTitle))
(disjointWith UnitedStatesCodeSection (FormerFn UnitedStatesCodeSection))
(comment LexicalMicrotheory-NonLexWiz "An instance #$LexicalMicrotheory-NonLexWiz is a #$LexicalMicrotheory that is not intended to be used for straightforward mappings of lexical items to Cyc terms, and therefore should not be used by either the #$CycBrowserLexificationAssistantModule or the #$CycLexificationWizard.")
(disjointWith NoTaste (TasteFn Cinnamon-Spice))
(disjointWith NoTaste (TasteFn Licorice))
(disjointWith NationalForest (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest NationalForest))
(disjointWith (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn Forest geographicalSubRegions (TerritoryFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica)) (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn Forest geographicalSubRegions (TerritoryFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica))))
(disjointWith (NationalForestsInFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica) (CollectionDifferenceFn Forest (NationalForestsInFn UnitedStatesOfAmerica)))
(disjointWith CoronaryArteryBypassGraft-SurgicalProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn CoronaryArteryProcedureNonCongenital-Surgical CoronaryArteryBypassGraft-SurgicalProcedure))
(comment AntiWesternIdeology "#$AntiWesternIdeology is a #$PoliticalBeliefSystem associated with agents -- groups, regimes, or individuals -- who have a negative vested interest (see #$negativeVestedInterest) in western countries (see #$WesternCountry).")
(comment WesternIdeology "#$WesternIdeology is a #$PoliticalBeliefSystem associated with agents -- groups, regimes, or individuals -- who have a positive vested interest (see #$positiveVestedInterest) in western countries (see #$WesternCountry).")
(comment SocietyOfThoracicSurgeons "The major US organization of thoracic surgeons.")
(comment |rdfs:label| "#$rdfs:label is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$prettyString")
(comment TheLogicalFieldIndexical "The indexical quoted instance of #$LogicalFieldIndexical.  Used in assertions where a non-specific logical field indexical is needed.")
(disjointWith HeartValveRepairOrReplacement (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepairOrReplacement))
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet CoronaryArteryStenosis-Finding MedicalDiagnosis)))
(comment YearNumberInDateFn "(#$YearNumberInDateFn DATE) returns the integer representing the year that subsumes DATE, if there is one.")
(comment DayNumberInDateFn "(#$DayNumberInDateFn DATE) returns the integer representing the day of the month that subsumes DATE, if there is one.")
(comment MonthTypeNamedInDateFn "(#$MonthTypeNamedInDateFn DATE) returns the #$MonthOfYearType representing the month that subsumes DATE, if there is one.")
(disjointWith SurgicalProcedure (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet AtrialDisorder MedicalDiagnosis)))
(comment followupMtForInterest "(#$followupMtForInterest MT TOPIC) indicates that MT contains information that can be used by the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader to form questions related to TOPIC.")
(comment Aesthetics "The subfield of #$Philosophy concerned with the nature of aesthetic judgment.")
(disjointWith Slave (CollectionDifferenceFn Person Slave))
(comment electedToOrganization "<code>(#$electedToOrganization AGT ORG)</code> means that <code>AGT</code> is a member of the organization
<code>ORG</code>, and furthermore gained <code>AGT</code>'s member status as a result of an election.")
(comment drugInteractsWith "(#$drugInteractsWith DRUG1 DRUG2) indicates that there is a significant interaction between DRUG1 and DRUG2.  Typically this means that extra caution should be used when a patient is taking or being prescribed both DRUG1 and DRUG2")
(comment |xsd:int| "xsd:int is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$SubLInteger")
(comment assertionDependsOn "(#$assertionDependsOn ASSERT TERM) means that the assertion ASSERT depends on the existence of TERM, and if TERM is removed, ASSERT should also be removed.  It does not have any code support at this time that enforces this constraint.")
(comment TransformationOfOneValueToAnotherInSKSI "This is the collection of situation types in which one value is transformed into another in the context of SKSI encoding or decoding statements.  Instances of these collection are associated with descriptions that indicate to Cyc how to do the required transformation.  Note that this includes the \"null\" transformation in which the value is simply passed along without change.")
(comment MosbysDictionaryOfComplementaryAndAlternativeMedicine--2005Edition "Mosby's medical dictionary of Complementary and Alternative Medicine")
(comment AmericanHeritageMedicalDictionary--2007Edition "American Heritage Medical Dictionary")
(comment DorlandsMedicalDictionaryForHealthConsumers--2007Edition " Dorland's Medical Dictionary for Health Consumers")
(comment GaleEncyclopediaOfMedicine--2008Edition "The GALE encyclopedia of medicine")
(comment FeelingAbnormalAmountOfFn "(#$FeelingAbnormalAmountOfFn SENSE) relates a #$SensoryReactionType SENSE to the #$PhysiologicalCondition of having an abnormal amount of SENSE.  For example, (#$FeelingAbnormalAmountOfFn #$LevelOfDizziness) means the condition of feeling dizzy (since any amount of dizziness is abnormal).")
(comment SAICLDSCDemonstrationSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle within the larger #$TKBDemonstrationSpindle for storing SAIC-derived source representations. ")
(comment AnimalPhysiologyMt "Naive theory of animal physiology.  Animals are considered to be alive.  A corpse is an instance of (#$DeadPhysicalRemainsFn #$Animal) not of #$Animal.  #$anatomicalParts of animals can be assumed to be physically attached to the animal.")
(comment corpDilutedEarningsPerShare "An instance of #$TemporallyQualifiableRelation. (#$corpDilutedEarningsPerShare ORG MONEY)<T> relates the amount of MONEY earned (i.e. profit) by ORG per share of stock during the time interval T, but not necessarily any time interval subsumed by T.  This is calculated using the diluted number of shares in ORG, which may be higher than the actual number of shares outstanding.  The diluted number of shares includes the number of shares that are 'spoken for', through means such as options or warrants to buy stock.  See also #$dilutedEarningsPerShare-ForStockType and #$dilutedEPSForPeriod.")
(comment TestVocabularyMt "All vocabulary concerning the internal testing methods will be asserted in this microtheory. However, because some of the actual tests are microtheories, we must assert (#$isa TEST-MT #$TestQuestionMicrotheory) in the #$BaseKB.  Other elements of #$CycSystemTestRun should have their isas assertions in #$TestVocabularyMt, not #$BaseKB. This microtheory must make the minimal number of assumptions possible. This is because all #$TestQuestionMicrotheory's have #$TestVocabularyMt as a #$genlMt and any given test should be able to make arbitrary assumptions.  Assertions which are specific instructions about how the #$CycTestingDaemon should run particular tests (e.g. #$TestSummaryRequests or #$TestInitializers) should be asserted not in the #$TestVocabularyMt but in the #$TestOperationMt.")
(comment arrangementNearestPredicates "A specialization of #$arrangementPredicates (q.v.) that relates an #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects (q.v.) to the maximally specific spatial relationships that hold of or among its members.  More precisely, (#$arrangementNearestPredicates GROUP PRED) means that (i) (#$arrangementPredicates GROUP PRED) holds and (ii) there is no reified proper specialization SPECPRED of PRED such that (#$arrangementPredicates GROUP SPECPRED) holds.  For example, a contiguous arrangement of like objects might have both #$touches and #$touches-Directly as arrangement-predicates, but only the latter as a _nearest_ arrangement-predicate.")
(comment RCCMt "This is the #$TheoryMicrotheory that contains the basic axiomatizations for

the implementation in #$Cyc of the 'Region Connection

Calculus' developed by #$DavidRandell, #$ZhanCui and #$AnthonyCohn, as well as many new relations and collections which extend the language and simplify the implementation in #$CycL.  The most general features of the spatial logic are axiomatized here, while more specific, possibily contradictory, theories of space are handled in spec mts. For instance, the #$RCCMt is agnostic regarding the existence of

atomic regions, i.e., regions with no proper parts. Instead, there are two mutually exclusive specializations:

#$RCCWithAtomicRegionsMt in which the collection #$AtomicSpaceRegion is defined, and #$RCCContinuousSpaceMt

which postulates that every region has a nontangential proper part.  That is to say, any region has infinitely many

nontangential proper parts (see #$nontangentialProperPartOfSpaceRegion). Other direct specializations include the #$RCCWithPointsMt, in which a theory of incidence with nondimensional points is developed, and the #$RCCTopologicalTransitionMt, in which we develop a theory of the discrete topological state transitions that occur between regions that move into contact with one another . Note that this

Mt, as well as the #$RCCWithPointsMt, is also agnostic regarding the ontological status of atoms. See also the #$SharedNoteOnRCCMicrotheories.")
(comment TheAgent "A #$TheTerm that refers to an element of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible.  Originally created to refer to the specific #$Agent-PartiallyTangible to which an #$Obligation applies.  See #$ist-Prohibition.")
(comment hasCapacity "(#$hasCapacity AGENT CAPACITY) holds just in case AGENT has the instance of #$AgentCapacityQuantity CAPACITY.  See #$AgentCapacityQuantity for an explantion of \"agent capacities\".")
(comment PlasmaPhysics "This is the study of the special properties of

matter in the #$Plasma-StateOfMatter.")
(comment DemocraticPartyIdeology "The ideology typically held by those persons who are members of the #$DemocraticParty-US in the U. S. A.")
(comment AbilityToFn "(#$AbilityToFn ACTIVITY) denotes the collection of the various degrees of abilities to do the instance of #$SkilledActivity ACTIVITY.  For Instance, 
(#$AbilityToFn #$FigureSkating) denotes the collection of all degrees of figure skating 
ability.  Since this function returns a specialization of #$ScalarInterval, it is permissible to use them with the generic value functions (e.g. 
(#$LowAmountFn (#$AbilityToFn #$FigureSkating)) denotes the instance of 
#$AgentCapacityQuantity that represents a low amount of ability to figure skate.)")
(comment HeavyMetal-TheMovie "An animated Movie based on the contents of the popular science-fiction and fantasy #$ComicBookSeries #$HeavyMetal-TheMagazine. This Collection is the set of all copies and prints of that film.")
(comment hasEnvironmentalQuantity "(#$hasEnvironmentalQuantity IND QUANT) holds just in case the individual IND has the quantity of the feature specified by QUANT.   For instance,  (#$hasEnvironmentalQuantity WorkSpace123 (#$LowAmountFn #$AcousticNoiseLevel)) holds just in case WorkSpace123 has a low level of noise.  This is a very general predicate.  In most cases you will want to employ a more specialized version specific to the #$EnvironmentalQuantity  being attributed.")
(comment WestSideStory-ThePlay "The musical play [#$Play-Musical-CW] entitled 'West Side Story'.  Performances [#$performanceOfWork] of #$WestSideStory-ThePlay are #$EntertainmentEvents.  The #$PlayScript of ``West Side Story'' is a #$subWorks.")
(comment SimpleAstronomyDataMt "What any educated person should know about the #$Sun, moon, #$Planets, etc. See also #$UniverseDataMt and #$EarthObservationalAstronomyMt.")
(comment agentsExistentialState "(#$agentsExistentialState AGENT STATUS) means that AGENT, an instance

of #$Agent-Generic, is in the existential state, STATUS, an instance of

#$TemporalThingTypeByExistentialStatus.")
(comment GeometryGMt "The most general microtheory for laying out the axiomatization of

geometric concepts. Assertions made in #$GeometryGMt ought to be \"visible\" to

any of its specializations. For instance, Euclid's parallel postulate is

true in #$EuclideanGeometryMt but would not hold in a microtheory axiomatizing

any non-euclidean geometry. Meanwhile, the notion of a line -- being common

to all geometrical theories -- is to be defined in #$GeometryGMt where

universal features of lines are to be axiomatized.")
(comment OWLIndeterminateIndividual "The collection of OWL individuals having the default non unique names assumption.  Unlike Cyc which has the Unique Names Assumption (different named terms are default #$different) OWL provides #$owlSameAs and #$owlDifferentFrom to explicitly assert identity relationships between individuals.")
(comment AgentGMt "The #$Microtheory that defines the concept of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible and properties of agents.")
(comment EmergencyProcedureForFn "(#$EmergencyProcedureForFn ACTION) returns the collection representing the prescribed steps in a plan to deal with an emergency situations involving ACTION. For example, (#$EmergencyProcedureForFn #$StingingByBee) would denote the emergency procedure for treating a bee sting.")
(comment FunctionalRoleAnalysisMt "A Cyc #$Microtheory containing assumptions and definitions
which allow for analysis of #$FunctionalSystems in terms of the
functional roles played by their components, and assessment of
#$Agent-PartiallyTangibles in terms of the roles that they play within such systems. One
of the distinguishing features of the FunctionalRoleAnalysisMt is that
it assumes that instances of #$Agent-PartiallyTangible will play one or more roles in
one or more #$FunctionalSystems, as a matter of definition.")
(comment GeographyMt "This #$Microtheory is for rules and assertions about that refer to both collections of #$GeopoliticalEntity and collections of physical objects or which refer to constructed #$GeographicalRegions (such as #$Canals).  General assertions about natural types of #$GeographicalRegion belong in #$NaturalGeographyMt.  General assertions about types of #$GeopoliticalEntity which do not refer to natural #$GeographicalRegions belong in #$PoliticalGeographyMt. Assertions in these microtheories are about specs of #$GeographicalRegion without making any assertions about the #$PlanetEarth or any #$Individual on it.  Assertions about natural features of the Earth belong in #$WorldNaturalGeographyMt.  Those about instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity, treated as #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles, belong in #$WorldGeographyMt.  Those assertions which treat instances of #$GeopoliticalEntity as #$GeographicalRegions (e.g. stating that one #$City borders on a certain #$River) belong in #$WorldGeographyDualistMt.  If the assertions refer to objects in the territory of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, they belong in the corresponding US-related microtheory (#$UnitedStatesNaturalGeographyMt, #$UnitedStatesGeographyMt, or #$UnitedStatesGeographyDualistMt).  (See #$Dualist-Physical-AndGenericGeographyMtNote)")
(comment ReformulationForwardDirection "A meta-property of a #$CycLReformulatorDirective, meaning
that there exist two arguments in the directive such that the
lower-numbered arg (e.g. arg1 for a binary predicate) is the 'from'
arg, the input to the reformulator, and that the higher-numbered arg
(e.g. arg2 for a binary predicate) is the 'to' arg, the output of the
reformulator.  Its semantics are more fully determined by context.
This is the default #$preferificationDirection for
#$reformulatorRules.  See #$reformulationDirectionInMode for how this
direction can be used.")
(comment KEInteractionResourceTestMt "An Mt for storing and testing assertions about #$KEInteractionResources.")
(comment GraphicalStructure "A specialization of #$AbstractVisualStructure (q.v.).  #$GraphicalStructure is the collection of all abstract structures that are graphical in nature, and thus could be part (or all) of the structure of a document.  This includes (at least) typographical structures (such as abstract characters and strings; see the specialization #$TypographicalStructure), formatting structures (see e.g. #$List-Information, #$Table-AIS, and #$NLParagraph), and pictographic structures (see e.g. #$Graph-AIS).  It does <i>not</i> include abstract sound structures (cf. #$SoundStructure).")
(comment PortalTypeByState "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PortalTypeByState is a collection of #$Portals that share the same openness property - either #$OpenPortal or #$ClosedPortal.")
(comment arrangementPredicates "This predicate relates an #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects to a spatial relationship that holds of or among its members.  (#$arrangementPredicates GROUP PRED) means that either (i) PRED is a unary instance of #$SpatialPredicate that holds of all #$groupMembers of GROUP or (ii) PRED is an N-ary (for N > 1) spatial predicate that \"connects\" all of the members of GROUP; that is, for each MEMBER of GROUP, PRED holds among MEMBER (in any one of PRED's argument-positions) and some N-1 members of GROUP.  For example, contiguous arrangements are connected by #$touches-Directly, and proximally-grouped arrangments (such as a grove of trees) are likely to be connected by #$near or #$nextToLikeObjects.  See also #$arrangementNearestPredicates.")
(comment DramaticPerformanceTypeByName "A collection of collections. Every element of #$DramaticPerformanceTypeByName is a collection of performances of some named dramatic work. Given a named dramatic work, such as 'Hamlet', the collection of all performances of that work will be an instance of this class.  The work may be a play, an opera, or a ballet. For example, the collection of all performances of the ballet, 'Swan Lake,' is an element of #$DramaticPerformanceTypeByName, as is the class of all performances of e.g., 'Hamlet', 'West Side Story', and 'The Magic Flute'. (See #$DramaticPerformance for an explanation of the criteria for being a DramaticPerformance. Although all plays and operas are instances of #$DramaticPerformance, not all ballets are.)")
(comment SanctionsOnAngola-August1997 "The event of the #$UNSecurityCouncil imposing sanctions on Angolan rebels in resolution #1135/97, which imposed travel restrictions on members of #$UNITA and ordered the closing of the organization's offices.")
(comment IADemonstrationSpindle "The #$MicrotheorySpindle 
which contains source microtheories especially relevant to the
March 2002 demo.")
(comment ElectedOfficialInRegionFn "(ElectedOfficialInRegionFn REGION) denotes the collection of elected officials in REGION.  These may be officials of REGION, or of a subdivision of REGION.")
(comment ContextOfPCWInterpretationByFn "A binary function that returns an instance of #$Microtheory when given a #$PropositionalConceptualWork and an #$IntelligentAgent as arguments. (#$ContextOfPCWInterpretationFn PCW AGENT) denotes the microtheory containing the propositions (and their upward closure) that AGENT goes on the record as claiming that PCW contains. Essentially, it is the the interpretation by AGENT of PCW, or at least the portion of the interpretation that AGENT is willing claim.")
(comment SentenceOfCWFn "A binary function that returns an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork when given a #$PropositionalConceptualWork and a #$CharacterString. (#$SentenceOfCWFn PCW STRING) denotes the #$PropositionalConceptualWork that is a subwork of PCW that is derived from the sentence STRING.")
(disjointWith FootballQuarterback (FormerFn FootballQuarterback))
(disjointWith Karateka (FormerFn Karateka))
(disjointWith TaeKwonDoPractitioner (FormerFn TaeKwonDoPractitioner))
(disjointWith UnitedStatesPresident (FormerFn UnitedStatesPresident))
(disjointWith Singer (FormerFn Singer))
(disjointWith President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState (FormerFn President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState))
(comment DhakaStockExchange "The main stock exchange of Bangladesh")
(comment urlStringOfCW "(#$urlStringOfCW CW STRING) means that STRING is the #$UniformResourceLocator string for CW, and can be used to find CW on the internet.")
(disjointWith PubliclyHeldCorporation (CollectionDifferenceFn Organization PubliclyHeldCorporation))
(comment |xsd:short| "#$xsd:short is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$Integer")
(comment |xsd:decimal| "#$xsd:decimal is the collection of #$RealNumbers equivalent to some integer times some non-positive power of 10.")
(comment |xsd:long| "#$xsd:long denotes the collection of #$Integers from -263 through 263-1, inclusive.")
(comment |rdfs:subClassOf| "<code>(#$rdfs:subClassOf SUB-CLASS SUPER-CLASS)</code> means that <code>SUB-CLASS</code> and <code>SUPER-CLASS</code> are collections that have been ontologized in at least one OWL ontology, where in that ontology it has been declared that <code>SUB-CLASS</code> is a sub-class of <code>SUPER-CLASS</code>.  #$rdfs:subClassOf is nearly equivalent to #$genls; the main distinction is that #$rdfs:subClassOf is restricted to hold of instances of #$OWLClass (q.v.).")
(comment Pathobiology "A sub-field of #$Pathology.  #$Pathobiology is the study of the biological aspect of disease.")
(comment CellularPathology "A sub-field of #$Pathology.  #$CellularPathology is the study of the effects of disease on cellular structures.")
(disjointWith NoTaste (TasteFn (FruitFn PeachTree)))
(comment (URIFn "tag:govshare.info,2005:rdf/census/details/samp/") "Namespace for Census data gathered from only about one-sixth of the population.")
(comment (URIFn "tag:govshare.info,2005:rdf/census/details/100pct/") "Namespace for Census data gathered from all surveyed households.")
(comment DecisionTreeConceptFilter "A specialization of #$ConceptFilter defined by a decision tree, not by #$isa or #$genls assertions, a #$Set-Mathematical, or a #$Taxonomy.")
(comment followupMtForTask "(#$followupMtForTask MT TASK) indicates that MT contains information that can be used by the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader to form questions when working on TASK.")
(disjointWith Relation (CollectionDifferenceFn Thing Relation))
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject (CollectionDifferenceFn TemporalThing BiologicalLivingObject))
(comment synonymousSNOMEDCT09Concept "(#$synonymousSNOMEDCT09Concept CONCEPT NUMBER DESCRIPT-STRING) means that CONCEPT is denoted in SNOMED-CT 09 with the ID NUMBER, and the description DESCRIPT-STRING.")
(comment ImageCreation "A specialization of #$HumanActivity.  Each instance of #$ImageCreation is an action in which an #$Image is created by (see #$actors) a #$HomoSapiens.  Many instances of #$ImageCreation will also be instances of #$VisualImageRecording, but not all, as some #$ImageCreations do not involve keeping a record of the created #$Image.")
(comment musicalFanOf "(#$musicalFanOf IND PERFORMER) means that the individual IND is a fan of PERFORMER by dint of PERFORMER's musical abilities or accomplishments.")
(comment sportsFanOf "(#$sportsFanOf IND SPORTING-AGENT) means that the individual IND is a fan of SPORTING-AGENT by dint of SPORTING-AGENT's sports abilities or accomplishments.")
(comment fanOfTVSeries "(#$fanOfTVSeries IND SERIES) means that IND is a fan of the #$TVSeriesProduct SERIES.")
(comment YahooWebsearchCountFn "A function that returns the number of Yahoo (see #$Yahoo-SearchEngine) hits for its argument string.")
(comment nounCompoundDecisionTreeDetects "(#$nounCompoundDecisionTreeDetects TREE TERM) means that TREE is a #$NounCompoundHeadDisambiguationDecisionTree that is used to determine whether or not the correct denotation of the head of a noun-compound is a specialization of TERM.")
(comment Abraham-Patriarch "A patriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, father to #$Isaac-Patriarch and grand-father to #$Jacob-Patriarch.")
(comment Sarah-Matriarch "A matriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, wife of #$Abraham-Patriarch, mother of #$Isaac-Patriarch.")
(comment Isaac-Patriarch "A patriarch of the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, son of #$Abraham-Patriarch and father of the patriarch #$Jacob-Patriarch.")
(comment biologicalSiblings "A #$FamilyRelationSlot, (#$biologicalSiblings PERSON1 PERSON2) means that PERSON1 and PERSON2 either have at least the same #$biologicalFather or the same #$biologicalMother (that is, they are #$halfSiblings), or that they have the same #$biologicalFather and #$biologicalMother (that is, they are #$fullSiblings).")
(comment Nahor-HebrewBibleFigure "The brother of #$Abraham-Patriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament.")
(comment Milcah-HebrewBibleFigure "The sister in law of #$Abraham-Patriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament.")
(comment biologicalCousins "A #$FamilyRelationSlot, (#$biologicalCousins PERSON1 PERSON2) means that PERSON2 is a biological cousin of PERSON1, i.e. PERSON2's #$biologicalFather or #$biologicalMother is related via #$halfSiblings or #$fullSiblings to PERSON1's #$biologicalFather or #$biologicalMother.")
(comment parallelCousins "A #$FamilyRelationSlot, (#$parallelCousins PERSON1 PERSON2) means that PERSON2 is a parallel cousin of PERSON1, i.e. that PERSON1 and PERSON2 are biological cousins because their mothers are biological siblings or their fathers are biological siblings.")
(comment Bethuel-HebrewBibleFigure "The newphew of #$Abraham-Patriarch and the parallel cousin of #$Isaac-Patriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament.")
(comment Rebecca-Matriarch "A matriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, wife of #$Isaac-Patriarch, mother of #$Jacob-Patriarch and #$Esau-HebrewBibleFigure.")
(comment Laban-HebrewBibleFigure "A figure in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, father-in-law of #$Jacob-Patriarch and brother of #$Rebecca-Matriarch.")
(comment Rachel-Matriarch "A matriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, wife of #$Jacob-Patriarch and mother of #$Joseph-Patriarch.")
(comment Lea-Matriarch "A matriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, wife of #$Jacob-Patriarch and sister of #$Rachel-Matriarch.")
(comment Jacob-Patriarch "A patriarch in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, #$Jacob-Patriarch is the father of #$Joseph-Patriarch.")
(comment Esau-HebrewBibleFigure "A figure in the #$Genesis-BookOfBible in the #$OldTestament, #$Esau-HebrewBibleFigure. is the brother of #$Jacob-Patriarch.")
(comment crossCousins "A #$FamilyRelationSlot, (#$crossCousins PERSON1 PERSON2) means that PERSON2 is a cross cousin of PERSON1, i.e. that PERSON1 and PERSON2 are biological cousins because one person's mother is related via #$biologicalSiblings to the other person's father.")
(comment Handmaiden "A #$PersonTypeByOccupation, a hand-maiden is typically an attendant upon a woman of socially high status. Depending on the local culture, she may also be a concubine of the husband of her mistress.")
(comment TransformationOfOneValueToAnotherInSKSI-AdHoc "This is a collection of situation types in which one value is transformed into another in the context of SKSI encoding or decoding statements.  Instances of these collection are associated with descriptions that indicate to Cyc how to do the required transformation.  Note that this includes the \"null\" transformation in which the value is simply passed along without change.  This collection is specifically those transformations useful in ad hoc reporting.")
(comment HerbalDrugSubstance "The collection of herbal medications, which consists of plants and plant extracts that are used for medical effect.")
(comment DrugTypeNotSuitableForSuggestions "The collection of #$DrugSubstances that are not suitable for use when providing lists of medications to users.")
(comment TheYear-Indexical "#$TheYear-Indexical is a special #$CalendarYear which denotes the current date from the perspective of wherever it was encountered.  For example, if one is reading an article on June 15, 2010, the sentence 'The new widget is expected to be unveiled on June 20', the indexicalReferent for #$TheYear-Indexical inside the date (represented at (#$DayFn 20 (#$MonthFn #$June #$TheYear-Indexical))) would be (#$YearFn 2010). This particular year does NOT have any special support to allow the Cyc system to automatically figured what year #$TheYear-Indexical refers to.  Instead, it's intended to function as a placeholder until a fully-grounded #$CalendarYear can be found.")
(disjointWith HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure (CollectionDifferenceFn SurgicalProcedure HeartValveRepair-SurgicalProcedure))
(comment UserGeneratedGeneralKEMt "A #$Microtheory which contains assertions gleaned directly from users via the #$CycAssistedDocumentReader or similar tools.  Assertions in this Mt have not been vetted by experienced #$HumanCyclists, and should therefore be approached with caution.")
(disjointWith ScoringOnAConversionInFootball (UnsuccessfulAttemptToFn ScoringOnAConversionInFootball))
(disjointWith ScoringPoints (UnsuccessfulAttemptToFn ScoringPoints))
(comment PlannedAssassinationOfChildericI-Event "#$PlannedAssassinationOfChildericI-Event denotes the planning of an assassination of Childeric I by his (noble) subjects, due to his having seduced some of their daughters.")
(comment ChildericIsDebauchery-PoliticalScandal "#$ChildericIsDebauchery-PoliticalScandal represents the political scandal resulting from the behavior of the Frankish King Childeric I that offended his subjects into ousting him from his throne. Cf History Francorum, II, 12.")
(comment Bisinus-ThuringianKing "#$Bisinus-ThuringianKing was the king who took in #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing during his exile from the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks.")
(comment ChildericIsFlightToThuringa-Event "#$ChildericIsFlightToThuringa-Event represents the escape of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to #$Bisinus-ThuringianKing and his wife #$Basina-GermanicQueen in the after-math of the #$ChildericIsDebauchery-PoliticalScandal.")
(comment ChildericIsRefugeInThuringa-Event "#$ChildericIsFlightToThuringa-Event represents the escape of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to #$Bisinus-ThuringianKing and his wife #$Basina-GermanicQueen in the after-math of the #$ChildericIsDebauchery-PoliticalScandal.")
(comment Basina-GermanicQueen "#$Basina-GermanicQueen was the wife first of #$Bisinus-ThuringianKing, but left him to marry #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing after the latter's refuge with #$Bisinus-ThuringianKing. She subsequently became the mother of #$ClovisI-MerovingianKing.")
(comment AgreeingOnSignalForChildericIsReturn "#$AgreeingOnSignalForChildericIsReturn is the representation of the instance of #$Planning where #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing and his confidant settled on a broken #$Coin-Currency as an indicator that the time for  #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to return to the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks had arrived.")
(comment BreakingInHalfOfGoldCoin-Event "#$BreakingInHalfOfGoldCoin-Event is one of the #$subEvents of the negotiation of a signal that would allow #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to know that he was good to return to the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks.")
(comment GoldCoinBrokenByChildericI "#$GoldCoinBrokenByChildericI represents the gold coin that #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing and his confidant broke into halves to use as a signaling and authentication device in their secret communications when preparing the return of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks.")
(comment MarriageOfBisinusAndBasinaOfThuringa "The #$MarriageOfBisinusAndBasinaOfThuringa is an instance of #$Marriage-Agreement and represents the time during which #$Bisinus-ThuringianKing and #$Basina-GermanicQueen were in the #$spouse relationship.")
(comment ChildericIsReturnToSalianFranks-Event "#$ChildericIsReturnToSalianFranks-Event represents the return of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to the #$KingdomOfSalianFranks after the receipt of the other part of the broken gold coin as a signalling event.")
(comment NidalMalikHasan "An instance of #$Person, Major Nidal Malik Hasan was a military psychologist. Major news outlets stated that he went on a shooting rampage in Fort Hood, Texas, before his scheduled deployment to Afghanistan as a counselor to combat soldiers, in November of 2009.")
(disjointWith GeographicalAgent (FormerFn GeographicalAgent))
(comment PersuadingChildericIToMarryBasina "An #$Action, #$PersuadingChildericIToMarryBasina represents the effect of the speech reported in Historia Francorum, II, 12, that #$Basina-GermanicQueen uses to get #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing to marry her.")
(comment Aegidius-RomanCommander "An instance of #$Person, #$Aegidius-RomanCommander was the commander of the Roman Army in Gaul during the time-period related in the Historia Francorum, II, and reigned as king of the Salian Franks for eight years in lieu of #$ChildericI-MerovingianKing.")
(comment situationConstituents "The most general instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate; that collection's #$commonGenlPreds.  This predicate relates situations (see #$Situation) to the instances of #$Thing involved in those situations.
<p>
(#$situationConstituents SIT CONSTIT) means that CONSTIT is a constituent of, or plays some role in, SIT.  The role played by CONSTIT might be almost anything, as long as it's \"intrinsic\" to SIT.  Thus to perform, to be changed in the course of, to be information conveyed in, or to be an abstractum the instantiating of which figures in a given situation is to be a constituent of that situation; but to predict, to be a cause or effect of, or to know about a situation is not sufficient to be a constituent.  Arguably, CONSTIT must in part <i>constitute</i> SIT, in the modal sense that SIT (that very situation) would not have occurred or obtained had CONSTIT not played the role it did.
<p>
An important specialization of #$situationConstituents is #$actors (q.v.), the most general predicate relating #$Events to their participants.")
(comment conditionTypeAssociatedWithIn "(conditionTypeAssociatedWithIn COND SUBST AMT FLUID) means the #$PhysiologicalCondition COND is associated AMT amount of the substance SUBST in FLUID.  For example, high amounts of #$ProteinStuff in #$Urine is associated with #$RenalDisease.")
(comment BroadcastTypeByIntendedTransmissionMedium "A collection that facets #$BroadcastMediaProduct into collections by virtue the transmission medium (the type of #$MediaTransmitting) that the instances of those collections were designed for.")
(comment VisitRecommendationForAgentTypeAndDestinationTypeFn "This predicate denoting function takes as arguments a type of intelligent agent and a type of location, and produces a predicate that allows one to say that agents of that type should visit a particular location of that type, when visiting some other location.  For example  if P=(VisitRecommendationForAgentTypeAndDestinationTypeFn Tourist Theatre) is a predicate such that (P CityOfMilanItaly LaScala) would mean that Tourists visiting Milan are recommended to visit La Scala. Similarly (P CityOfAustinTexas ?) would list all of the theatres in Austin that should be visited by tourists. If there were any.")
(comment ApacheDerby "An instance of #$DatabaseServerProgram, #$ApacheDerby is the free SQL implementation from the Apache project.")
(comment PositiveAdjective "#$PositiveAdjective stands in contrast to #$ComparativeAdjective and #$SuperlativeAdjective -- it is the collection of adjectives in the 'positive' form, as opposed to the 'comparative' or 'superlative' form.  (Terminology taken from Chris Kennedy's 1999 UCSC dissertation.) You know something is a #$PositiveAdjective when its basic form is #$regularDegree.  A test for this is whether you can modify it with 'very'.  Example: 'very childish' => 'childish' has a #$regularDegree form and is a #$PositiveAdjective.  If the #$regularDegree form furthermore has the right phonological shape, you can attach #$Er_Comparative-TheSuffix or #$Est_Superlative-TheSuffix to it.  Being suffixable with -er or -est is a *sufficient* criterion for being a #$PositiveAdjective but not a *necessary* one.")
(comment ComparativeAdjective "#$ComparativeAdjective is the collection of adjectives in the comparative form.  Their base forms have the predicate #$comparativeDegree. Example: 'prettier'. These can be formed with #$Er_Comparative-TheSuffix, and include periphrastic forms like 'more beautiful'.")
(comment SuperlativeAdjective "#$SuperlativeAdjective is the collection of adjectives in the superlative form.  Their base forms have the predicate #$superlativeDegree. Example: 'prettiest'. These can be formed with #$Est_Superlative-TheSuffix, and include periphrastic forms like 'most beautiful'.")
(comment ArchaealCellWall "The collection of instances of #$CellWall that are the #$anatomicalParts of some instance of #$Archaea.")
(comment UWTextRunnerSystem "The computer program built as part of the University of Washington's 'TextRunner' project.  Important players in the project in 2010 include Oren Etzione and Stephen Soderland.")
(comment CMUReadTheWebSystem "The computer program built as part of Carnegie Mellon's 'Read the Web' project.  Players in the project in 2010 include Tom Mitchell, Burr Settles, Andy Carlson, Justin Betteridge, and Bryan Kisiel.")
(comment SemiconductorProcessingMt "A microtheory that holds information related to the processing of semiconductor wafers.")
