(comment MeSH-Vocabulary2009 "The information in the expanded 2009 version of the National Library of Medicine (NLM)'s thesaurus of Medical Subject Headings.")
(comment SimpleSchemaMappingToolCreatedKS "(quotedIsa KS SimpleSchemaMappingToolCreatedKS) means that the knowledge source KS was created using the Simple Schema Mapping Tookit.")
(comment bridgingMtForKS "(bridgingMtForKS KS MT) relates a structured knowledge source (#$StructuredKnowledgeSource) to its bridging Mt, which contains rules for relating non-SKS predicates to the KS-specific predicates (#$SKSIOnlyPredicate).")
(comment BridgingMtForKSFn "This unary and reifiable function takes a structured knowledge source (#$StructuredKnowledgeSource) as its sole argument and denotes a bridging microtheory. It is the function corresponding to the predicate #$bridgingMtForKS with the canonical argument order.  See #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for details.")
(comment correspondingSKSIPredicate "(correspondingSKSIPredicate BASE-PRED SKSI-PRED LS) states that within the context of the
logical schema LS, interpretations for the predicate BASE-PRED can be obtained via looking 
at the SKS-backed predicate SKSI-PRED.")
