(comment ComputerUserProfile "The collection of instances of #$Profile-CW that are used by computer programs to store information about their users.  These often include a user's program preferences, shortcuts, and other features of the application context that are useful to maintain.  Some profiles aim to build an internal model of the user which they use to proactively adjust the user's interactions with the software.")
(comment PortableElectronicDeviceVideoScreen "The collection of video display screens made for portable electronic devices like cell phones, portable game systems, etc.")
(comment PeerToPeerInternetChat "the collection of all online chat sessions where a connection between two clients is established and the chat is a conversation between those two connected users.  This includes sessions that directly connect between IP addresses and chat sessions that are mediated via a 3rd party service (e.g. Google Talk).")
(comment ConferenceChat "the collection of all online chat sessions where a connection between two or more clients is established and the chat is a conversation between these connected users.  This includes sessions that directly connect between IP addresses and chat sessions that are mediated via a 3rd party software.")
