(comment NthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDateFn "<code>(#$NthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDateFn N DATE-TYPE DATE)</code> denotes the <code>N</code>th date of type <code>DATE-TYPE</code> that occurs during <code>DATE</code>, an instance of #$Date.  For example,
 <code>(#$NthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDateFn 1 #$Wednesday
         (#$NthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDateFn 11 #$CalendarMonth (#$YearFn 2010)))</code> denotes the first Wednesday of the 11th month of 2010, i.e., November 3, 2010, also expressible as <code>
    (#$DayFn 3 
      (#$MonthFn #$November 
        (#$YearFn 2010)))</code>.")
(comment nthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDate "The predicate that corresponds to #$NthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDateFn, <code>(#$nthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDate THIS-DATE N DATE-TYPE SUBSUMING-DATE)</code> identifies <code>THIS-DATE</code> as the <code>N</code>th date of type <code>DATE-TYPE</code> that occurs during <code>SUBSUMING-DATE</code>, an instance of #$Date.  For example,
 <code>(#$nthSpecifiedDateTypeOfSubsumingDate (#$DayFn 3 
      (#$MonthFn #$November 
        (#$YearFn 2010))) 1 #$Wednesday
         (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 2010)))</code> identifies November 3, 2010 as the first Wednesday of November 2010.")
(comment QuantifiedVersionOfBinaryPredicateFn "((#$QuantifiedVersionOfBinaryPredicateFn   RMP BINPRED) ARG1 ARG2) is equivalent to (RMP BINPRED ARG1 ARG2). ((#$QuantifiedVersionOfBinaryPredicateFn   RMP BINPRED) ARG1 ARG2 COUNT) is equivalent to (RMP BINPRED ARG1 ARG2 COUNT).")
(comment ScrollKnobOrKey-PhyscialDevice "The collection of scroll keys or nubs/knobs that are part of computer input devices that are meant to control the scrolling of information on a video display.")
(comment EmailFiltering-RulesBased "The collection of all email filtering processes that are gated by user defined rules.")
(comment regexSubstringMatch "tbc")
(comment MSExhangeUserProfile "The collection of instances of #$Profile-CW that are used by program copies of #$MSExchangeClient-TheProgram.")
