(comment arityTypeOfCodingFunction "(#$arityTypeOfCodingFunction FUNC ARITY-TYPE) relates a #$CodingFunction to its arity-type.  For example, (#$arityTypeOfCodingFunction  #$LockFileFn #$FixedArityFunction) means that #$LockFileFn always takes the same number of arguments.")
(comment |owl:intersectionOf| "An OWL native property that is used in constructing class definitions.  It relates a class, C, (typically an anonymous class) to a list of classes whose intersection contains precisely those members that are members of C.")
(comment |owl:unionOf| "An OWL native property that is used in constructing class definitions.  It relates a class, C, (typically an anonymous class) to a list of classes whose union contains precisely those members that are members of C.")
(comment |owl:complementOf| "An OWL native property that is used in constructing class definitions.  It relates a class, C, (typically an anonymous class) to another class, B, just in case C is the class of all things that are not members of B.")
(comment |owl:oneOf| "An OWL native property that is used in constructing class definitions.  It relates a class, C, (typically an anonymous class) to a list that exhaustively enumerates the members of C.")
(comment |xsd:positiveInteger| "xsd:int is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$PositiveInteger")
(comment |xsd:anyURI| "xsd:anyURI is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$UniformResourceIdentifier")
(comment |xsd:double| "xsd:double is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$RealNumber")
(comment |owl:AnnotationProperty| "Instances of #$owl:AnnotationProperty are binary predicates used to annotate ontology instances. ")
(comment |owl:cardinality| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to some #$NonNegativeInteger.  It states that each instance of the restriction class has at most and at least that number of values for the specified property (via an #$owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) to that resource.")
(comment |owl:minCardinality| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to some #$NonNegativeInteger.  It states that each instance of the restriction class has at least that number of values for the specified property (via an #$owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) to that resource.")
(comment |owl:maxCardinality| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to some #$NonNegativeInteger.  It states that each instance of the restriction class has at most that number of values for the specified property (via an #$owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) to that resource.")
(comment |owl:hasValue| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to some #$owl:Thing (restricted to an individual or particular data value in OWL DL).  It states that each instance of the restriction class has the specified property (via an owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) to that resource.")
(comment |owl:allValuesFrom| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to a class or range of values.  It states that the restriction is the class of things such that anything that is a value for the specified property to one of those things (via an  #$owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) is a member of the related class or within the stated range of values.")
(comment |owl:someValuesFrom| "An OWL native property that relates an #$owl:Restriction to a class or range of values.  It states that the restriction is the class of things whose value for the specified property (via an  #$owl:onProperty triple on the restriction) is either a member of the class or within the specified range.")
(comment |owl:onProperty| "An OWL native property that is used to specify the property used in an #$owl:Restriction.")
(comment |owl:TransitiveProperty| "#$owl:TransitiveProperty is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate")
(comment |owl:SymmetricProperty| "#$owl:SymmetricProperty is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.")
(comment |owl:FunctionalProperty| "#$owl:FunctionalProperty is an imported OWL/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot.")
(comment |xsd:nonNegativeInteger| "xsd:nonNegativeInteger is an imported RDFS/XML term equivalent to the Cyc term #$NonNegativeInteger")
(comment |skos:exactMatch| "#$skos:exactMatch is a mapping relation in the #$SKOSCoreNamespace which is used to link concepts in different ontologies.  The SKOS core defines this property as symmetric and transitive; some sources may further specify it as reflexive.")
