(comment SpecificationForTypeFn "A binary function.  This function takes a specialization of #$Artifact-Generic and an ID string and returns the instance of #$DeviceConfigurationSpecification with that ID.")
(comment SpecTypeForTypeFn "A unary function.  This function takes a specialization of #$Artifact-Generic and returns the collection of #$DeviceConfigurationSpecification that are specifications of that type of device.")
(comment specificationForTypeType "A binary predicate.  This is the corresponding predicate to #$SpecTypeForTypeFn.")
(comment HardwareGroupPositionFn "A binary function that takes a hardware group type and some positive integer and returns the model position assigned that index for that hardware group type")
(comment hardwareGroupTypeHasModelPositionWithIndex "A ternary predicate that relates a hardware group type and a positive integer to the model position for that group type with that index number.")
(comment HardwareSlotPositionFn "A binary function that takes a hardware component/card specification and an index (slot) number and denotes the slot position with that index number on the specified device.")
(comment deviceSpecificationHasComponentSlotPositionWithIndex "A ternary predicate that relates a hardware group type and a positive integer to the model position for that group type with that index number.")
(comment linkRequiresValuesForPredToStandInReln "(#$linkRequiresValuesForPredToStandInReln LINKPRED PRED RELN) means that a constraint on the validity of models/graphs that employ LINKPRED (in the appropriate context) is that if the arg1 and arg2 of LINKPRED stand in PRED to some values, VAL1 and VAL2, then (RELN VAL1 VAL2).")
(comment modelPairInconsistentWRTAttribute "(#$modelPairInconsistentWRTAttribute ARG1 ARG2 ATTRIBUTE) means that ARG2 is linked via some predicate, L, to ARG1, and ARG1 and ARG2 fail the condition given by some instance of #$ConstraintConditionPredicate.")
(comment linkRequiresNotAllStandInRelnToSomeNode-Inverse "(#$linkRequiresNotAllStandInRelnToSomeNode-Inverse LINKPRED PRED RELN CONDITION) means that if (LINKPRED ARG1 ARG2), then for ARG1 and ARG2 to be violation free participants in LINK, no 
 NODE linked to an ARG1 link member via PRED should be such that  
 everything linked to it via the inverse of RELN stands in CONDITION to ARG2.")
(comment modelPredRequiresAllExistsSpecMax "(#$modelPredRequiresAllExistsSpecMax PRED TYPE1 TYPE2 MIN) means that a constraint on the validity of any instance, INS, of TYPE1 in the model/graph in the operative context is that there is at most MAX number ARG2s (proper specs of TYPE2) such that (PRED INS ARG2).")
(comment modelPredRequiresAllExistsSpecMin "(#$modelPredRequiresAllExistsSpecMin PRED TYPE1 TYPE2 MIN) means that a constraint on the validity of any instance, INS, of TYPE1 in the model/graph in the operative context is that there must be at least MIN number ARG2s (proper specs of TYPE2) such that (PRED INS ARG2).  Note that when MIN = 1, this is a \"constraint\" version of #$relationAllExistsSpec.")
(comment cardinalityConstraintViolatedWRT "(#$cardinalityConstraintViolatedWRT THING RELN) means that in the operative constraint context, THING fails to have the correct cardinality of things related via RELN")
(comment modelPredRequiresAllExistsMin "(#$modelPredRequiresAllExistsMin PRED TYPE1 TYPE2 MIN) means that a constraint on the validity of any instance, INS, of TYPE1 in the model/graph in the operative context is that there is at least MIN number of ARG2s that are instances of TYPE2 such that (PRED INS ARG2).")
(comment modelPredRequiresAllExistsMax "(#$modelPredRequiresAllExistsMax PRED TYPE1 TYPE2 MAX) means that a constraint on the validity of any instance, INS, of TYPE1 in the model/graph in the operative context is that there is at most MAX number of ARG2s that are instances of TYPE2 such that (PRED INS ARG2).")
