(comment ComponentListToTotalWeightFn "A unary function.  This function takes a list of an artifact type and a positive integer and returns the product of the integer times the artifact type's arg2 value for #$massOfType.  This can be used to determine how much total mass a composite product has.  ")
(comment dateIsSubsumedByTimeOfWeek "(#$dateIsSubsumedByTimeOfWeek DATE TIME-OF-WEEK-TYPE) means that DATE is a calendar hour/minute/second that is subsumed by some instance of TIME-OF-WEEK-TYPE.  When TIME-OF-WEEK-TYPE is an instance of #$TimeParameter use #$temporallySubsumedBy-InsType which has dedicated removal module support")
(comment dateIsSubsumedByTimeIntervalSeriesType "(#$dateIsSubsumedByTimeIntervalSeriesType DATE INTERVAL-TYPE) means that DATE is subsumed by some instance of INTERVAL-TYPE.  When INTERVAL-TYPE is an instance of #$TimeParameter use #$temporallySubsumedBy-InsType which has dedicated removal module support.")
(comment temporalWindowForOpenDuring "(#$temporalWindowForOpenDuring THING TYPE DATE) means that DATE is a time interval that occurs within the range of the time window established for activities of TYPE associated with THING.  E.g. if the support hotline for ExpressoInc is manned on Mondays between 7 and 9 a.m., then (#$temporalWindowForOpenDuring EspressoInc SupportHotline (#$HourFn 8 (#$DayFn 7 (#$YearFn 2011)))) holds.\").  Often this will be asked with (#$IndexicalReferentFn-EvaluateAtEL #$Now-Indexical) thereby asking if the window is currently open.")
