(comment AtLevelToObjectFn "<code>(#$AtLevelToObjectFn PART-TYPE OBJ-TYPE)</code> denotes the instance of #$ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Precise <code>PRED</code> such that <code>(PRED A B)</code> holds just in case the altitude of <code>A</code> is identical to the altitude of the highest-most object of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that is a #$physicalParts of <code>B</code>, an instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code>.  For example, <code>((#$AtLevelToObjectFn #$Ankle #$HomoSapiens) Woodstock CharlieBrown)</code> means that Woodstock is at the same altitude as Charlie Brown's ankle.  Were they standing side by side on a level plane, this would entail that Woodstock's height is the same as Charlie Brown's foot, up to the ankle.")
(comment BelowLevelToObjectFn "<code>(#$BelowLevelToObjectFn PART-TYPE OBJ-TYPE)</code> denotes the instance of #$ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Range <code>PRED</code> such that <code>(PRED A B)</code> holds just in case the altitude of <code>A</code> is less than that of the altitude of the lowest-most object of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that is a #$physicalParts of <code>B</code>, an instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code>.")
(comment AtOrBelowLevelToObjectFn "<code>(#$AtOrBelowLevelToObjectFn PART-TYPE OBJ-TYPE)</code> denotes the instance of #$ComparativeAltitudePredicate-Range <code>PRED</code> such that <code>(PRED A B)</code> holds just in case the altitude of <code>A</code> is identical or less than that of the altitude of the highest-most object of type <code>PART-TYPE</code> that is a #$physicalParts of <code>B</code>, an instance of <code>OBJ-TYPE</code>.")
